<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="6">

  <DocumentRef DateTime="20260831T153232" id="1fd4fb33-3760-42e0-9685-a537324e2a7f">
    <XRef DateTime="20260723T203625" id="f11bbf89-77bb-4245-a22b-5e08a11b4653"/>
    <XRef DateTime="20260723T203709" id="0655bd2a-e317-4541-9c59-80af8cc083c6"/>
    <XRef DateTime="20260726T003052" id="1d131615-3728-4220-96b9-810af0cc0bd2"/>
    <XRef DateTime="20260828T230000" id="bd7d195d-91f6-4c4f-80a6-8840275b55c8"/>
    <XRef DateTime="20260830T121653" id="ff5ccdbf-23d1-4e9d-b19c-cd3b634ebc38"/>
    <XRef DateTime="20260830T122513" id="bdafce3b-f032-4a42-a532-6825fd3a77dd"/>
  </DocumentRef>

  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="69d158e6-50cd-4991-a7e4-ea9d1f1e6de9">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="dd2fcd28-bb01-40f3-a220-8860523cfeb9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="23379b31-bf41-4eea-b94e-0075824d9fa2"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="77cc8720-bdbf-4a78-b429-66b90c6caa16">
      <Text>BLACK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2701b924-5299-4fe7-945c-a957a0ec8659">
      <Text>Breathing. Close, mechanical — air pulled through a regulator, pushed back out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e2c5ef9a-fcca-4056-b0cc-da95b8fe0275">
      <Text>Water moving. A pump throbbing far off, through walls.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b6de7a38-e876-4b0c-acdf-14855cb37513">
      <Text>A helmet lamp comes up: light that reaches three feet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8ff2c8f5-b45a-439f-b197-2e3c3f03fd0f">
      <Text>Gloved hands on a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">hoseline</Text>
      <Text>, following it forward.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8a7e9dd9-553f-45f5-9b6a-3061fb71e33d">
      <Text>SUPER: HALE RIVER, ALABAMA. 2014.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dbc49030-e247-452d-a435-0cc18ae19c31">
      <Text>The lamp finds the nozzle. DANNY MERCER, 25, probationary firefighter — broad-shouldered, young — braces behind it. CAPTAIN CARL SLOAN, 50s — barrel-chested, gray mustache — keeps one hand on Mercer’s shoulder strap.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="61e19676-4869-4f40-b92f-d67cb928cc0b">
      <Text>They move on their hands and knees. Heat keeps them there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb67ca1c-1f92-4c45-8eaa-979b3c0f55a7">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="b66d5785-7726-4f78-aaf4-15b08d5ac1e3">
      <Text>(muffled, mask)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4467dae0-2029-4b29-b6ae-2e012ac98a41">
      <Text>Pencil it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f5154c65-e20d-4d01-a504-595d9315e9bd">
      <Text>Mercer opens the nozzle at the overhead — one short burst. It comes back down on them as hissing steam. They keep moving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a9897480-9013-46a2-8f45-5c70f18347fc">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6af975f4-470f-4b57-b16c-62852eb61422">
      <Text>Where is it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f804a173-20ee-4166-a43d-944a055caa32">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8188fcca-559e-4cd7-81f9-9050b40bcb1e">
      <Text>Above us or ahead of us. Watch your ceiling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="ce4f6246-20fb-440a-9d78-5fcab0ce0795">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="1" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="INCIDENT COMMANDER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="65e8ba83-bd85-426c-8159-c0ca4863d7a1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="13ae7c42-164e-4d07-a32b-51ff2eae0c74"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a4934633-a2e7-445f-ab84-c9d2acb67bfa">
      <Text>A two-story red-brick building on a block of shuttered storefronts. Smoke pulses from the eaves. No flame visible.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="da8be60b-8c41-4677-a776-b49fd1280a1e">
      <Text>An ENGINE sits at the corner. At the pump panel, EARL </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">DOBBS</Text>
      <Text>, 40s, company engineer, checks the gauges and looks up at the roofline.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="751de311-5693-4255-b34d-d3d33c6e2e5d">
      <Text>Crews mask up at the entry. Ladders rise to the roof. The </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> team waits with tools ready.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="92da3a7b-c0c8-4147-b8fd-10cba61ce3c0">
      <Text>At the command board, the INCIDENT COMMANDER, radio traffic in both ears.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="94364729-33be-43fd-b532-10111a4009cd">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="27e5fd67-1451-4c5d-961d-de16be7a79b9">
      <Text>(into radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1c4aaa73-1cfe-41f0-8f19-1f5777ea872e">
      <Text>Command to all units — building reported vacant, occupancy unconfirmed. Interior, give me conditions.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcce55ff-d84e-4e5e-8e83-50eeb1944dc2">
      <Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3e016d62-1f3e-4746-b524-19618d851b67">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="15602fd2-46f6-479d-bd8a-d18f77c8623f">
      <Text>Heavy smoke. High heat. Zero visibility. We’re penciling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="71685b66-767d-4946-9acb-cdcf9b09f730">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="541ad5d0-a165-4c45-841d-209ae68660b0">
      <Text>(into radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="468d140e-99cc-4f93-9b4b-f1143c6c41b3">
      <Text>Interior, you in position with a charged line?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5fe2ed9e-e58e-43f2-b1b8-bd51e70e7420">
      <Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="fe4022f7-f62b-413d-9229-7184c30055a6">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83b32ba0-6ef2-40d4-b7a7-3c69306f5b72">
      <Text>Charged and on it. It’s above us. Give us a hole and we’ll take it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b4d6e56d-dac6-4796-bd87-3b37f75e0d23">
      <Text>Three firefighters sound the roof ahead of every step with pike poles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7972cc25-8350-4f53-98a5-65c128b0ad96">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="97b035e7-63dd-4ab0-998f-37fe968cf096">
      <Text>(into radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32075ac5-c0e6-4a56-97b2-05c8dc0fbbb8">
      <Text>Roof, Command. Open it up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="209c641c-ba38-4459-8777-1d9237791598">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - ROOF - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7e9aaede-b5ea-47ca-bd16-e00e24cd65f4">
      <Text>The saw starts on the third pull. It revs to full power. The blade bites hard into the roof.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11692d9f-a7e7-4aaf-b7d7-1e3ffa6376be">
      <Text>Smoke presses along the cut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1935050f-5ee6-4e67-96d2-a9a6b3a5358a">
      <Text>The opening breaks through. Smoke stands up in a hard column.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="03eb4e78-5a5c-42e4-93d0-27cbc69e4d32">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="2" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="eefb12b3-9044-4734-a4c3-495a45f47834"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ALDRIDGE - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="29088d97-4313-4b7b-9ce7-28f35b7a0f1b">
      <Text>The smoke LIFTS a foot off the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="22b15a32-e140-4c0b-939b-90e7c7cc280a">
      <Text>The building appears as the draft takes hold — shelving rows. A dead forklift. An aisle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="63c2ff83-e096-4643-8e9e-ba62d824f496">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="34fec436-fdab-4f28-95b2-922b5461d500">
      <Text>There’s our vent. Move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b1770eff-eb7b-4e97-a8b9-4a2a48f8f8de">
      <Text>They advance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fcfdee1c-5280-4e71-80a3-c56652392639">
      <Text>Outside, the engine pump climbs higher — </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Dobbs</Text>
      <Text> feeding them more pressure.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8faa20bb-119c-4efb-bbaa-313d1103b4f9">
      <Text>Ahead... the ceiling GLOWS through its seams.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ebd2ce3c-f123-4491-bf01-2a55f307ba93">
      <Text>Fire rolls from the ceiling void — across the overhead — running for the vent.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="77e2a4ba-9027-4363-9932-67c1756b6816">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="3" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - ROOF - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="79090c79-67d6-4e9b-a6af-0caae0b77d1d">
      <Text>Fire ERUPTS through the cut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="41981c1e-b0a4-4afd-b82b-c0e1bb43eef0">
      <Text>The roof crew instinctively ducks, throwing gloved arms across their </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">facepieces</Text>
      <Text> as the fire blows past.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="227510c1-b578-4aef-b70b-645d552ec7aa">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 1/8" Page="3" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="INCIDENT COMMANDER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bc8af172-f8f7-48a5-94b0-dabaf98ba40b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d71338ae-2687-43e7-96b2-5ab92f86b249"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RIT FIREFIGHTER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0350af27-83f7-49ec-ace5-e5b37431fed1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RIT OFFICER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5a4d9713-7941-414b-9054-0ca570f1344b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="cbfe7282-56aa-4aca-95ba-134acbb1cde1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ALDRIDGE - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e6289e29-c932-4dd1-8b72-7518567af877">
      <Text>Behind Sloan... a section of ceiling and steel rack lets go. CRASHES across the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">hoseline</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e9cefbf8-1427-41f9-a943-1d5ae05279c8">
      <Text>The lamp beams disappear into black.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="58c0dbef-e70f-4131-8e9c-bab210230468">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e39eab8f-d543-4e9b-a427-6dd97486073f">
      <Text>Back it out! Back—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ad31ee34-3905-4cbd-a4fe-737461124b46">
      <Text>The hose line is pinned beneath the debris. Sloan hauls at it. Mercer is three feet deeper into the room, cut off from Sloan by burning shelving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff0f2494-06b1-4909-a418-cc0b0e78dbce">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d7dfcaa5-a25b-4971-9be8-fe696939fa1c">
      <Text>Cap—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7acd3c93-3fe3-4ddf-8c7a-bfa84f1eb644">
      <Text>The </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">VIBRALERT</Text>
      <Text> goes off against his jaw.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bd1182b5-9a12-47f9-b101-3b302c1dbedd">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="512f97f3-6c75-4c56-ba83-2198a6a68a66">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af03275c-284b-420f-bfa6-06946ad79abb">
      <Text>MAYDAY MAYDAY MAYDAY — Engine Three. Firefighter separated. Northeast corner. Low air—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="16140558-34e4-4223-83ae-13393e5d366b">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4181396c-1427-4346-ade2-4660175bd843">
      <Text>(radio, tinny, far)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f99d0d04-a7df-4caa-bec3-5cb99c5612ad">
      <Text>Command copies the Mayday. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> is deploying.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="18fc2ff7-819d-4b3a-b6b4-d7a1b75684a4">
      <Text>Mercer, alone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="41876616-0b4d-4a51-9bcd-fc5fae913789">
      <Text>He drops a glove onto the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">hoseline</Text>
      <Text> and follows it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3200c166-481e-4c2f-92a0-6143ab7937a5">
      <Text>Five feet. A coupling. His fingers find the lugs on the far side. Wrong way. He turns and crawls back along the line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="10a602af-d48c-4540-b87c-3655028610d4">
      <Text>The regulator gives him less air. The </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Vibralert</Text>
      <Text> pounds, slows, then stops. He inhales and gets nothing; the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">facepiece</Text>
      <Text> seal pulls tight against his cheeks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="40bb4383-cc6a-438c-9532-8e02203c5ba3">
      <Text>His gloves grip the edges of the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">facepiece</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0b62b17f-6cfc-4640-9c99-425549635803">
      <Text>He does not pull it off. He releases it and puts both hands back on the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">hoseline</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="03b0cdbf-a039-4836-867a-905f5900bc8e">
      <Text>He crawls. Slower now. Each attempt to inhale pulls the seal tighter. His helmet light drops toward the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2aaee1f9-dbbf-443c-9de2-9d6b6bdf6e8b">
      <Text>He stops moving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3d7aafa1-48c3-4113-a481-257e1d7681e8">
      <Text>The beam remains fixed across the floor. Smoke passes through it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="82f5a6bd-cc06-4639-8de5-8ddb91079ed2">
      <Text>His PASS device begins to chirp. The warning accelerates, then rises into a full electronic SHRIEK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a8796079-6f50-4ec6-b777-22e050a15e85">
      <Text>Nothing else moves. Faint traffic comes through the radio on his chest:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="de5cdf4e-246b-4166-b0c4-410ad972c7bf">
      <Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f78b5e32-7e0a-4e27-a062-04da1d2645c6">
      <Text>(radio, tinny)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6a217c9e-565c-4431-8ba7-430dbcbf6deb">
      <Text>Mercer. Mercer, key your mic.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ebae741e-b830-4038-99d7-1c04cf9e5448">
      <Text>Nothing. The shriek. Smoke crossing the beam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dc99bdee-49b4-49de-9f42-6ba0e3704da4">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> OFFICER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c38e67ff-3c22-45dc-973a-a0a87634ff23">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0275a22e-29ad-4bd1-8072-4333e3536e17">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> to Command — we’re at the collapse. No contact. We’re digging.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec656d9b-43ae-4d3d-878b-a1d8048e7d0c">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="bcf037ea-4675-4c42-ba25-9222edc111dd">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a6ffafde-26d1-48d8-8fef-c12a55d6b588">
      <Text>Command to all units — emergency traffic only. Three minutes on the Mayday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="df4d2f7c-bbe8-4666-9f24-f7513da1e9ae">
      <Text>The beam is dimmer. The smoke is thick and rolling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97021f63-9b80-4c1e-88c9-cb34fb429e3c">
      <Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="9ad03d14-ee1b-4b23-8a27-dc4181053f23">
      <Text>(radio, raw)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ec46d34a-3c6e-4479-8643-5f27e94e7e23">
      <Text>He was right beside me. He’s on the line. He is ON the line—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="42cd906d-22b3-4248-b848-b0c80259bb04">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="5c0cb60d-9d40-446c-92fc-d5a92e4be17d">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eebb255d-bd6a-4824-a991-e1ae3b5dbe3b">
      <Text>Engine Three, Command — stand by. ... Four minutes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bd855594-036d-4b4f-a162-a6c84594af04">
      <Text>The shriek keeps going. The beam is almost nothing now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c2e31fc0-cb36-4d74-ac6c-98fc3be28f46">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e398103b-a2cf-4302-bc85-f8bddc62f73a">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a406b21b-d501-40c0-a8bc-dbd88645b8d8">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text>, Command — status.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9963febd-6d6a-464b-b62b-1f2501253731">
      <Text>Static. No answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="caee0817-e647-4159-87d2-ef128d51889c">
      <Text>The beam. The smoke. The shriek.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d89b405c-811f-4e17-9c5e-6fd525b3cdd9">
      <Text>A GLOVED HAND reaches through the smoke, finds Mercer’s shoulder strap and locks on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a858a041-c5ba-4ffa-8d02-8f58dc3eeed1">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> FIREFIGHTER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="bf455dd7-7800-480f-93bd-1e5cb7cdf89f">
      <Text>(muffled, close)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="94e886f2-1dd3-419b-861f-d7e27f6dc5a5">
      <Text>GOT HIM! We got him! GO!</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7e0bc80d-d3d5-4c3a-8bd9-fdf474442185">
      <Text>Mercer is YANKED backward. Floorboards rush beneath him. His lamp swings away from the beam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="2d7e857f-8908-469e-86a8-a4abcdc7d4a5">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="5" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="AED">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0094d88e-7c25-4267-853a-02866d1d1f16"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COMMAND">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ed8c6179-3b48-4296-91a9-d95cb8027f33"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b5eb71f6-ed4f-486d-a20d-ea17b2b2e413"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - ENTRY DOOR - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cdfba3ca-4b39-46d5-8edb-dc49e8174152">
      <Text>Two </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">RIT</Text>
      <Text> firefighters drag Mercer across the threshold. His mask is still sealed. His PASS continues to scream until one of them shuts it off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a1a09344-e0c2-41f7-a5fe-5285b214adcd">
      <Text>Clean air. Concrete apron. Mask off. Helmet off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9d3bfb4-08e7-420d-aab4-fb0da1eb4f0c">
      <Text>A FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC’s fingers go to his throat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="90cce28f-298b-4c86-8a76-7016172eb236">
      <Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e8715674-a006-4a90-98c4-4b6f9540afa7">
      <Text>No pulse. Starting compressions.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0089b142-ede8-46aa-bfd1-38ba01089b8d">
      <Text>Coat open. Compressions. Bag-valve mask. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">AED</Text>
      <Text> pads. Behind them, the building ROARS as master streams open up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fccde65f-2f4e-4c51-893b-6d909e654845">
      <Text>Mercer COUGHS — wet, tearing. Fights the mask on his face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0b6740c1-12e5-4273-a1ab-b656aa904403">
      <Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a8c24351-ab6c-47d7-8ad4-1fdb02cbf16c">
      <Text>Pulse. We got a pulse. Package him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c84753a0-ca04-4053-8c2b-dd802968d036">
      <Text>He keys the mic on his shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1408e4eb-9055-42a0-915c-d671862afc07">
      <Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="804cd165-177d-4e92-9100-4a9ccebd6a2a">
      <Text>Command, Medical. I want the helicopter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7ec45997-5eef-453a-909d-5d498dc192d6">
      <Text>COMMAND (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83903ffc-69ac-48ea-b9e7-148df5a0c928">
      <Text>Say again, Medical.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="86f228cd-01d9-49e3-b536-5fe6a55b0f11">
      <Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="26b440f5-ca0c-4719-b257-fb01a68cab6c">
      <Text>Helicopter. He was down and he’s back. We need to get him to the nearest trauma center, stat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="ac540a4f-d8fa-4c23-bbac-a203cd67596f">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="5" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - CLEARING - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="389eba50-5d1a-4a30-bddb-f6a0526fca2e">
      <Text>Open ground a hundred yards off the fire. Mercer in the aircraft — board, straps, the flight crew over him. The door slides shut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13d09780-9b6f-4922-ac1c-e5eb765a9a55">
      <Text>It comes up off the grass. Rotor wash drives ash flat across the lot. The firefighters under it turn their backs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4869375e-fb8b-4338-b81e-a8e936f0e80e">
      <Text>The aircraft noses over the tree line. Gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="bd18a6d7-5cbf-43eb-a7cf-05f6e6b068db">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - REAR - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d5a23ab2-8499-445c-b01d-cad7dd73d54a">
      <Text>SUPER: EARLIER THAT NIGHT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0ea20a13-e48b-4e24-8a9b-f55d38fbe8f1">
      <Text>Dark windows. Closed loading door. No traffic on the block.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b84c06fc-82f4-4174-93ee-674417fa75a0">
      <Text>A BICYCLE comes down the alley and stops. The rider is small, a canvas bag across his back. His face stays out of the light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0b2f0001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001">
      <Text>He lays the bicycle in the weeds. Packing straw and baled dry goods crowd a timber post against the rear wall. A pocket knife starts a strip of cotton sheeting; bare hands tear and twist it tight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7ea57242-eff3-4a15-9795-97189c56c472">
      <Text>He kneels at the timber post, clears away the loose straw and places the twisted cotton between the post and the lowest bale. He pushes the straw back around it, leaving one end exposed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1477b4af-f177-4c14-a776-7b10aa5441e4">
      <Text>A lighter. He cups the flame and touches it to the exposed cotton.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c2588c5e-5cae-418a-a179-02e05aff0140">
      <Text>The flame travels down the twist and disappears beneath the straw.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="74aa96e5-f452-4789-801d-7b42414f480d">
      <Text>He closes the lighter. He lifts the bicycle out of the weeds and rides to the far end of the block. He stops with one foot on the ground and looks back at the building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13090c2c-ff93-449e-8d85-6f9032d327d8">
      <Text>Smoke slowly thickens around the timber post.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="0b2f0003-0000-4000-8000-000000000003">
      <Text>From the end of the block, the boy watches the smoke build.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="cf73ed0c-d11c-4caf-808a-3e9a0c91172f">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="6" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ee5b0511-0ee5-4c57-b001-4de9b16ff99a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6c5b0316-3c13-4494-86a0-197efde60371"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ddc0513f-db7c-4166-bf3c-42eb092525e8">
      <Text>Only steam rises from the building now. Yellow tape closes the block.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7f2e0d02-925e-47c3-b4b8-55c2e28664b3">
      <Text>Crews pull hose lines back toward the engines. Pike poles shoved into compartments. A firefighter removes his </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">SCBA</Text>
      <Text> and sits on the bumper.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="de80f879-2dbd-40ba-a840-83285c07004a">
      <Text>A white STATE FIRE MARSHAL TAHOE noses to the curb. State seal on the door. Low-profile light bar. Nothing else announcing it. Out of it: ELDON RUCKER, 46, Deputy State Fire Marshal, tall, square-built. Clean white shirt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="08319ca5-563d-4626-89a9-e6cdded6fdd0">
      <Text>From the rear hatch: boots, windbreaker, camera, clipboard, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Maglite</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="260d9e72-6aa0-479c-930d-7a4d9606d6d3">
      <Text>Sloan approaches. Rucker keeps his eyes on the building: steam at the eaves, a blackened window, roof sag, open doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="83cb050a-c2b2-4d80-a855-14c5a6f2cb0f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a735d959-759e-4fc5-9534-467ed2cb2ae3">
      <Text>Your boy?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0a200289-9f97-4874-a876-74c38290bd36">
      <Text>Sloan falls in beside him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7045a560-9061-4062-8b5a-82385a970c41">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="584e0c29-3f68-49a7-97fe-07d741dd5f7f">
      <Text>Breathing. They’re keeping him the night. His mama got there about four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="63e6e45c-3303-42c3-8bec-9d08a48724a5">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cce9b0fc-c58b-4290-b17d-8bd4aa3ae2ed">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cc0d8b3c-1cd5-45c0-9673-57a16a62bb33">
      <Text>Good.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="31ba8e10-4334-54c4-8a55-e0a35f1087e2">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="67e15451-b139-432d-94d5-85047107ad88">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3b2c3d85-6833-4103-8caf-f6d91152daf8">
      <Text>Anybody inside since overhaul?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ded1e790-a016-442f-9d17-f162b69e1e1b">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aaffee28-d19c-4d60-ba01-f596a69fceb2">
      <Text>Chief walked it about an hour ago. Ain’t nobody been in it since.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e94c2f37-339e-4f01-bc86-6153902e9dec">
      <Text>At the tape, Rucker stops for one look — roofline, windows, cornice, entry, ground — then ducks beneath it. Sloan follows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="20b25137-82d4-4d62-abb7-c91ae403e0d9">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="7" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="3a18514d-9316-4763-b5ad-8c8e18d6e44e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ALDRIDGE - BURNED SHELL - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="77200fd2-e69a-4c8a-a487-0ebd483174a6">
      <Text>Wet black. Daylight coming down through the roof cut. Water dripping off everything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7596ce82-fdb0-45d9-9afe-649a337151e9">
      <Text>Rucker enters, stops. Scans the room, then walks the main aisle, slow. Puts the light on a wall and follows a smoke line down it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0e4615da-d904-4fd1-a981-fc5f9d665d6b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="41b80be7-9fb9-4d7d-a5b1-0a3a2b47a8b7">
      <Text>(to the room)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="143801b0-c4df-4df4-b994-c54d63ded62a">
      <Text>All right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="085ce4c4-1173-4245-8ca9-5b33209a45f7">
      <Text>He crouches at a burned-out rack. Runs a thumb through char, then checks its depth with a small gauge from his shirt pocket.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d6f7f375-c1f4-4422-8770-cc89199c64ba">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fcb95a38-0f8e-44c7-a86a-fbe6a96c8a92">
      <Text>That’s the water. That’s not you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7a4da54e-1c25-4e84-ba26-1e92108e6584">
      <Text>He puts the beam up into the truss, then along the ceiling to the roof cut and the daylight standing in it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0c9f8d40-727e-4b0e-b75b-9efc902b6728">
      <Text>Down the aisle. Bolts of cloth on their sides, burned to the core. A rack of cotton ticking. Packing straw everywhere, gone to gray.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6c372097-6b5d-4606-945d-c40c8247bc6f">
      <Text>He moves down the aisle taking readings, photographing the floor clean here, cooked there, his light held low and raking.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e54fa00a-3e48-415e-ba93-79dd0bcb2eda">
      <Text>He arrives at the REAR CORNER. Low burn, deep char, climbing out of a heap of what used to be stacked stock and packing straw. He crouches. Stays down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fd92d100-8fd6-4f1d-88f5-f1abca7a8cd8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="33bb921c-6546-4190-ada5-c35199ffc610">
      <Text>There you are.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="46cb2bc6-9fba-4fc6-b85b-0de491c32567">
      <Text>He lays the beam along the base of the wall and follows the burn where it runs the joint.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1e1705f7-1f6f-4cd8-b82c-f490ca42187a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bec2521f-f96f-470e-90c6-47cfd24f2c89">
      <Text>You stayed low. All the way down here, low. Low is work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eff8c90a-d26d-4310-922d-c39fd514ce5c">
      <Text>He puts the light up the wall. Bare block. No box, no conduit, no fixture.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="237b0902-f0a8-4bfc-897e-71f06683c645">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="77777aed-a032-4d6a-b18e-e629a68830af">
      <Text>No box. No cord. No lamp. Nothing in this corner had any business getting hot.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8ee990b-6132-4d65-bb6f-d1d546d2e33f">
      <Text>He lifts a length of collapsed shelving with a pen, looks under it, sets it back where it was. He works the corner with the light. Turns over a piece of burned strapping with the pen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="feab0984-ecd5-4348-a794-4be43cb8ae94">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="24d6c549-e967-4fe0-8b20-1fa162aab4b2">
      <Text>Sat here half the night. No can. No splash. Used what they left.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d0a8c5d-64a7-4121-ae20-29a7ab84da64">
      <Text>He lays the beam flat across the floor. Follows it into the heap.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1676172e-e115-4bdf-854e-770454b75bc3">
      <Text>Under the packing straw: a STRIP OF COTTON, twisted tight before it burned. Still holding its twist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0628bafd-e6b2-4774-97ba-1b3f95d96596">
      <Text>Rucker doesn’t touch it. Photographs it where it lies.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec6907d8-1521-4ff4-9c5b-45dd5f0ff2da">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="27dd2b3f-14ab-49a1-bcc8-a506177246f8">
      <Text>Same as Cedar Street.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="818ae382-80db-46f2-a324-bb04685aedbd">
      <Text>He studies the twist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d0de3867-7335-4d2a-9394-6752d3457557">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2d39d007-91da-4fab-b508-b24b4ac46d8c">
      <Text>Same hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="f686f72a-14b2-43de-9954-1e7af73dca0e">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="9" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fdf234df-46b5-4ddb-87d9-abe497f4b5ae"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL - FIELD OFFICE, HALE RIVER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="06825746-5bea-4a92-a1bf-a545e3f2ff0e">
      <Text>A storefront office. A scanner murmurs from the next room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ec482450-bf13-40e0-b3bc-9c5e9b333749">
      <Text>On the long wall — a county map. Three pins. Cedar Street, the mill store, Aldridge. Dates beneath them in a careful hand. Six weeks. Then four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d4c56fb-14fa-4abb-807b-08dda30f9f0a">
      <Text>Rucker stands at his desk, phone to his ear. His camera sits open beside him. He wipes soot from the lens with the corner of a cloth while he listens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ae897767-569a-46f5-9bef-9f59b8fcd3d4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ac83920a-f958-431b-a25f-37d251857b3f">
      <Text>(into phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="36623b2a-85b8-4c78-9509-b923c96667ef">
      <Text>No, sir. Not kids. Kids burn what’s handy. They burn it where they’re standing. This one’s picked three buildings nobody’s had a use for in years. Month and better apart.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e57297e2-7445-40de-ad85-d6e9db957d40">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2348d0de-a127-46c4-8f8d-09e068175957">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="909fcba6-6229-4e85-a843-7e0cdf3a7438">
      <Text>(into phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d97be010-7ca8-4ec4-bd34-7977a627be10">
      <Text>Yes, sir. I’d keep that word off the radio a while longer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ddd0c958-6d52-4fc0-bb6c-1f56ae7281aa">
      <Text>He hangs up. The cloth stays in his hand. He walks to the map. Studies it. Not the pins. The roads between them. The rivers. The abandoned mill properties.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="409cd875-8654-4a73-a9d6-a119c2eb15ce">
      <Text>His finger hovers over a crossroads, then lowers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="2857a6ca-97c8-481a-b822-5b719be9454f">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="9" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DEENA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b54684ee-2194-458b-a247-8c787ddfa021"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7427c393-8139-49e2-964a-75c9a78afda3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUNE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="40cbcff6-9336-4a6c-819b-0a09a8afdcb2"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA LOUNGE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="82e6069b-59b1-4b5a-9833-c7388db5dfc0">
      <Text>Chairs up on the tables. Daylight through the front doors on a floor that’s seen a Saturday. Christmas lights over the bar, off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="32031956-a874-4a03-a545-27f40e6f23e9">
      <Text>On the bandstand, JUNE HOLLIS, 23 — small, dark-haired — runs a song alone at the mic, half-voice. A BUZZ under it in the PA.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="201a0ae9-3827-485a-b5f4-12170b338857">
      <Text>AMOS HOYT, 40s, Black, lean, in a work shirt with the sleeves rolled, comes out from behind the bandstand with a cable in his hand. Reseats it. The buzz dies.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="25c3a81c-c1a6-407c-b26a-1cd834fe0de1">
      <Text>JUNE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d03bc414-531e-4ca8-a544-ee4549c882b2">
      <Text>You fix amps now?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="74b37f0e-58be-422e-965c-ed219918d0e6">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="26ee23b0-3a58-4530-917c-a463d614147e">
      <Text>I fix whatever’s broke before Friday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4ca8ae13-8ed2-477d-be4b-a2d96c0b28fc">
      <Text>DEENA CALLOWAY, 40s — lean, handsome, fast on her feet, a pencil behind her ear — comes out of the kitchen patting her apron. Pats the bar. Checks her jacket on the hook.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1dff9e1f-5c89-4a3a-a74d-b852fa561d5c">
      <Text>Hoyt holds up her keys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="543fd4a5-ed8b-43db-80b5-b0702cec1993">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f3acfc7b-0cb2-4f83-97d7-7c1fab4634e5">
      <Text>Walk-in. In the lock. Again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f1cc6e18-8170-45d5-bacf-27e25c489dbc">
      <Text>DEENA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c88b6262-8489-4e84-a432-e1065b14269c">
      <Text>I was coming right back for them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="51edaef7-68e3-4960-8d9e-caa89c84bbc5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76a7be12-072a-46fb-bf70-dc4af3e7c129">
      <Text>Third Friday running you were coming right back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="148637f3-4dca-4802-90c2-732de25d2b15">
      <Text>DEENA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9647868b-a3d3-4cf0-8ec1-235db490e2c4">
      <Text>You counting?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="be49abee-7836-4f04-a069-f844d43913ff">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cc85ab68-6570-4f45-9aa6-6f015ef6558e">
      <Text>Somebody in this building better be.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8d4da7ff-b838-4aef-baaf-fd1717436174">
      <Text>She takes the keys and swats him with her bar rag. Hoyt picks up his toolbox and goes toward the back. June starts the song again from the top.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a95ee62c-3ff3-4554-b8de-522c4cd1fee6">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 1/8" Page="10" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5a00db49-4133-46ac-8718-754fadaa05d7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MISS ADELE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="527db9da-b02d-4af1-a855-f7f2e2cb65da"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="72a70f01-594e-44f6-862c-528bc8f55de7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. DOT’S DINER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4094c574-010b-4f43-8654-2a77dbbaf05d">
      <Text>Lunch thinned out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d6336771-a8ce-4035-8909-c8aa233e690c">
      <Text>Behind the counter, DOT </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">MABRY</Text>
      <Text>, 60s — flat-footed, forearms built by decades of handling trays. She pours before she’s asked to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0f183a72-d6f6-493d-b1f8-30ece022c277">
      <Text>In the back booth, RUCKER. Hat on the seat beside him. A file open. Cold cup of coffee in front of him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a826f323-2692-4ae6-a8d9-e18d00ad1957">
      <Text>Dot tops it off without breaking his concentration.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a15e8dec-8dc6-4166-8ee4-9e0cebc0cb3b">
      <Text>MERCER comes in — civilian clothes, a hospital bracelet still on his wrist. He spots Rucker. Crosses to the booth. Stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b778e9e3-4649-4f29-8685-eb9bf8da9508">
      <Text>Rucker turns a page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a9a28dc8-38c3-424a-b8f9-cbefa89dfc43">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9b24cdba-487b-482d-bd83-f15e1f2b32b1">
      <Text>Marshal. Captain Sloan said I’d find you here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fcbdc07c-7e74-41e1-9419-810c4f0ebe5f">
      <Text>Rucker’s eyes touch the hospital bracelet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="146613f4-ef05-4e83-ba22-1fd172bc8a79">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8b8f5f66-c468-4daf-80a1-f6ef9c997a99">
      <Text>You’re his </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">probie</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="461754c1-0505-42c5-985b-330417770fe8">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4cc3a534-5c20-48ae-bf7b-dac5e2e42d9f">
      <Text>Danny Mercer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7de949f4-6426-4c08-ba67-7d21b6bb789d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="959fd5a0-b102-444c-9426-59a1ecc4c7c5">
      <Text>They tell me you kept your </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">facepiece</Text>
      <Text> sealed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="98a5d2e0-f60e-478d-8a1e-e0cfbb9d55e9">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3af181a0-53c9-444d-9f37-5592d4fe0f12">
      <Text>Yes, sir. Academy said keep the seal. Better to go into arrest and give them a few minutes to restart your heart than pull it and breathe the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fdf6c36b-6eef-4d0f-95b2-facebd689202">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ad2c8aea-750e-4e2d-8274-6f1799e07ada">
      <Text>Good.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="17f90f75-3222-4443-99ce-7114c42383f3">
      <Text>He turns the file toward him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3e9c8de2-8d99-47de-9474-7e8e0f2b207b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="252013dc-4f31-4717-8d72-59d9905450cf">
      <Text>The ceiling in that building. Tell me the last thing it did before it came down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d33a8d7a-4aec-4135-be1d-1f6e9aaebc02">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1f9e1ac4-db13-4a1d-9ae0-5ca57c351fc4">
      <Text>It came down. It let go all at once —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0af6a239-5fd2-4b65-aa04-a73334fe5a22">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ca537bfa-9d6d-4a47-b2e8-2f58fbd98f45">
      <Text>Before that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c46ffb06-8753-482a-8aff-1ebb101e0915">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcacb3e7-ab48-4f08-bf08-41cd0c72d54c">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0dd24863-4482-4edb-bdc2-62569f6109d6">
      <Text>...It got quiet. Rolling and popping the whole way in... then it got quiet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a146f19f-6bf6-4ca0-b1c1-47d9e1ebcdad">
      <Text>Rucker closes the file. Looks at Mercer for the first time. Pushes the chair out with his boot.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="552423e5-c27f-49dd-8f58-c0f61302077d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d514cd2c-2a41-4790-b02f-338cc7c084b5">
      <Text>Fire in a void goes quiet right before it shows itself. You had four seconds of quiet. You spent them moving. Sit down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="68899f62-00bb-465d-b39b-02e601be8d34">
      <Text>Mercer sits. Dot passes. Without asking, she leaves a fresh cup beside Mercer. He starts to thank her. She’s already gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="497fbe9e-5789-48aa-8f31-b0c922242852">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="75cd9a05-e522-413a-9238-de316544f720">
      <Text>They tell me you can’t pull hose for six weeks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7fa0ad7a-ec01-445c-b9a5-b3259296f6b3">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7bdd66f2-b18f-4640-915e-c4ede312dcc7">
      <Text>Yeah, light duty. Driving a desk basically.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="14293190-5238-4a92-9c50-07ea81718387">
      <Text>Rucker slides the file across the table. Cedar Street photographs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="45518d2e-e5b0-4873-8a4b-2a5ac0e03d22">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="54fb4a45-4a03-4f1c-be76-6c2c3c46f3e4">
      <Text>You’ll drive mine. Carry files. Run a camera. Listen twice as much as you talk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fa988fad-48ba-47c2-bc77-77764aa73d50">
      <Text>MISS ADELE </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">FANNIN</Text>
      <Text>, 80s, stops beside the booth on her way out. One hand flat on the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7c5f6a22-85ff-460e-8d59-b0682e7e75a6">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="33754c37-89f3-4b91-8dee-deb57a910e7f">
      <Text>You gonna catch him, Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6f908675-d8c3-4c57-bb75-746baa1794b6">
      <Text>Rucker looks at Mercer. Opens the Cedar Street file to the first photograph and turns it toward him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c390b7b1-b6d2-470c-be04-35b841067d28">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e4a85cc4-632e-4ca3-9ece-c0a7e2fd6372">
      <Text>Yes, ma’am.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bbf79ef5-1b45-4543-b6cc-4f3857911a1b">
      <Text>Miss Adele pats the table once and heads for the door. The bell jingles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="87dd81c6-0b47-4738-b211-ccd4166139dd">
      <Text>Mercer studies the first photograph, then the next.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="185e9508-ea9f-49da-8984-7b555365afb0">
      <Text>Rucker drinks the cold coffee and watches him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="aa0b89fa-89d1-4dce-9bf9-b9cdaef27f2a">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 6/8" Page="12" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ac346605-89b3-453a-8f9d-44403022cd3f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="1b96842d-763f-4b67-8f1a-e6f0b074e08b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL - FIELD OFFICE, HALE RIVER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bbeb3ef1-8e1c-4d3c-b4e2-61303cd059d8">
      <Text>Two desks pushed together under the county map.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="12e6ea40-0b06-46c6-893a-fc0d6db03ba2">
      <Text>A liquor box of pink message slips on the floor. MERCER works through them at the second desk, three piles going.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7012d8eb-32f6-4462-a4d8-2984e073db56">
      <Text>Under the lamp, evidence photographs from Cedar Street and Aldridge lie side by side. In each, a strip of burned cotton still holds its twist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e3d333fe-c028-4694-a7c6-2c24b4a09d92">
      <Text>Rucker puts the loupe over one, then the other, then back again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="834deb57-188d-4bfa-9e59-520fadcc4ffb">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="e0b5ab32-f63e-4e2a-b53c-6699a15bbe1c">
      <Text>(to the photographs)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7aa98732-e3f7-4c45-b12a-7571e0364042">
      <Text>Did you bring these with you, or did you find them there?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="190d53f8-5890-4abe-8b2d-c039124ddeed">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="46096708-36a3-427e-8025-9ce0b6061e38">
      <Text>Sir?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6edfaa81-5f02-4cfc-9d2f-704f4fa91fa1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="54526167-f387-4569-953a-febfc5dfdde6">
      <Text>If he brings it, he shopped for it. If he finds it, he knows the building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="70ee399d-cacb-4c31-b595-22c0fa2be426">
      <Text>Mercer comes over with a slip still in his hand. He studies both photographs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="02aecf81-82a8-44b5-82b4-3f706885e5f9">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c6567a8-de3c-412e-8b7f-fffd3e1d36a2">
      <Text>They’re the same cloth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7227fd8b-575d-4982-a49d-8e070db3c82c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9e1ffda0-6e6a-4649-ad6f-3bb6f138ed94">
      <Text>They’re both cotton.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="65f62491-bdff-4c1d-837f-f02e5b6878ad">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7f6a4597-7dfa-480e-867b-c0fa9fd87514">
      <Text>No. Same cloth. Both cut clean on one side and pulled on the other. Somebody cut off something big and tore the rest by hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cb96a348-7040-40ec-b616-8195899d6877">
      <Text>Rucker moves the loupe to the torn edge. Looks at what Mercer saw.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6de01148-ab6e-47ad-9ff6-78844fcbe67a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d2b2520d-f72d-4514-9de6-cc5a25e93678">
      <Text>Sheeting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4f172979-2d8f-472e-8d3d-a7b03dcf5d06">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="afe9e9cb-7418-4936-ab1f-bcc180423d25">
      <Text>Mill sheeting. My grandmother had forty yards of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ca96af6e-bc93-44b8-b2a0-a83d4ddbb3d6">
      <Text>Rucker reaches for the phone and the county directory at the same time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb8ad2c3-4aab-47d5-b552-588ae8afa9b8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="50a8cbf6-74d3-400c-b741-42684ec3eff5">
      <Text>(into phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74f90275-bd6b-4c7c-a6d7-653e7e2c5c6e">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker, State Fire Marshal’s Office. Who took the dry goods out of the Hale River mill when it closed? Sheeting, ticking, cotton stock. Where’d it go?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="75f1a008-0fc7-42ea-84cb-c9fa9cb05dfc">
      <Text>A long listen. His pen stops before the man is done talking. He hangs up. Mercer waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a2d75b7d-bd07-48ff-ae7f-deb9dc4d72bb">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4255acb0-6b4f-4600-9887-d9e60092ee79">
      <Text>Auctioned in seventy-one lots. Nine years back. Cash off a tailgate. No names taken.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3a9104ef-e5f1-4818-8d30-5cb6dca630a9">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="050169ea-4cc8-4f58-9c01-56478802b4f3">
      <Text>So it’s in half the houses in the county.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="494e9a08-45f3-4bd1-bbc8-3e6c10cc6bd4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e8d5e249-c8f7-4ce8-ac01-faae8c7383aa">
      <Text>It’s in half the shop rags in the county. There’s a piece of it in my own truck box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="26707af8-de0b-4e5a-af90-3356779adf3e">
      <Text>Rucker squares the photographs, one over the other.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cc4db6a6-ab6a-4df4-a0da-e73939304c51">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5104d5a2-fd87-4415-a2b7-bf7cb9c501ac">
      <Text>Now I know he didn’t shop for it. That was worth a phone call.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="244c4130-f447-46e4-9570-60c6638ec78f">
      <Text>He returns them to the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c8ae0ef-8de2-4bc8-9849-2161624e0ab8">
      <Text>Rucker looks up at the map. Six weeks. Four weeks. Then blank wall where the next pin goes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1fac2f92-7b9e-462f-b597-390fb893b576">
      <Text>Mercer returns to the message slips. Rucker stays on the map.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c40af0b9-8311-4eed-9c47-efc48dd0068c">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a518947a-7dff-4849-afd9-ed455e1c81aa">
      <Text>You ever ride an engine?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="24d09e26-afc9-44cb-b101-3386dbbcd16a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3ddb49f6-4d27-4cad-bb69-1be14b640068">
      <Text>Eleven years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d716fc6-7ae5-4a1b-9ec4-279ef3821d02">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83def223-4c79-407f-98f0-c70545399938">
      <Text>What made you get off?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c4187d87-4852-4f1d-94cb-ca607e9c21ac">
      <Text>Rucker doesn’t turn from the map.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="55dfbf4a-b63f-4633-83af-333378bba6f5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c855f33-cca4-49e6-846b-0a41048a233a">
      <Text>Put out four hundred fires and couldn’t have told you what started three of them. Got to where I couldn’t stand it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="825e000d-0415-4c47-b2e1-2f0a4d692d68">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a18a7345-5d29-41ec-b737-b1cbe65a087e">
      <Text>And now you know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1cb6c37f-3bdb-4eae-9fd0-5739dd30935f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7b98b5bd-b0e7-464c-a3d2-65452dde57a3">
      <Text>Now I find out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0e80cd50-0a71-4bf9-85da-0b07c1ce0b71">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4e2ca1a3-cd6e-47da-80cb-c32b2ea9128a">
      <Text>Chief asked when I’m coming back on the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d620caf2-0659-4656-8112-2fc0f5339ead">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d02cae10-fb27-420a-9127-d27391b5d779">
      <Text>What’d you tell him?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8d4831e8-7dce-4018-8cb6-96f464956eeb">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5d877d0d-f6d3-43e8-88e3-dd7a5cb51da5">
      <Text>Six weeks, like the doctor said.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="98dc2de7-94b4-4d2a-9874-639b5bf899b4">
      <Text>A slip. Another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="36f65aee-a090-4267-b398-7f7b917718af">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6d9c2ead-43bc-4365-9efd-37e2a97f6fa1">
      <Text>I didn’t tell him I don’t miss it. Figured I would. On that floor I wasn’t thinking about the engine. I was thinking I never once knew where the fire was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="941bff57-ab3d-44ed-966c-b5b3fe9392be">
      <Text>Rucker looks at him. Says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2963acf3-bbe9-4359-8754-174db79d42b1">
      <Text>Mercer sorts a slip.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a8b237ef-1857-4cdb-bfc8-9a0b8a06085a">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="96f990a7-1e70-4d04-8ab9-5dcdc4410f05">
      <Text>Your wife mind the hours?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d8069bdd-ccdd-409f-b2ec-d8d8087eaa15">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de3a4ad5-40da-411e-9635-f04a7901e2a7">
      <Text>Ask her Saturday. Twenty years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="abdc31b8-7852-4832-a8ff-6f89f5da3c13">
      <Text>Mercer picks up the next one from the tall pile.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ded511b-8961-4642-93cc-719ac1807ba1">
      <Text>This time, he reads it again before letting it go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="93f9f67b-370f-44b9-9b59-c64ff3539fe0">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="15" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DISPATCH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="8bae80c5-316a-42f5-bd45-37397e2350f8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f67c6205-b175-4cc0-b756-41467a46edf6"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d92fe533-f5f3-4e09-9a15-a0bff717fc4e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. COUNTY ROAD - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ff6be396-e791-4ca3-8f00-bb3b3124c56f">
      <Text>The state Tahoe moves along two-lane blacktop, fields on either side. Radio traffic runs under everything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e7029890-039d-4f3d-a2cd-8691f27f3c39">
      <Text>DISPATCH (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a8a1c8d2-9373-422c-adb9-081c03b1cc34">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aa6b9308-c202-4e9b-980a-ccc4cb2af171">
      <Text>...tip line’s got eleven more from overnight, Marshal. Where do you want them...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2ca3d222-2cdf-4786-ba0c-c2172c919efc">
      <Text>MERCER rides in the passenger seat with a short stack of thin folders on his knee. The top one is a county juvenile referral form.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c5d4c268-a8b2-40e4-8b3a-fe3c4d34fd3e">
      <Text>The Tahoe turns in at a small frame house off the blacktop.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b47c1a02-0000-4a01-9a01-000000000008">
      <Text>A bicycle lies on its side in the yard, half in the tall grass. Rucker parks beside it and looks at it. They get out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="20914686-9c23-490e-9881-5792b9e3ab96">
      <Text>They cross the yard. At the porch, Rucker stops with his hand short of the screen door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="925e1a9c-3004-447c-957c-0fc91cb24a2c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5c51ce4e-1ccd-4009-b515-85f180f63754">
      <Text>This is the part nobody makes me do.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fc520604-4c7a-4bcb-a29f-da49b957f9ee">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eab45939-c7ab-4895-820f-c99d0bbc6c6d">
      <Text>What is it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff817d8b-fb5f-4664-8ece-febe32542e01">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="227dbb23-76bd-4bbb-ab98-4dde0096e00b">
      <Text>Sixteen-year-old lit a grass fire behind the school. I’d like that to be the last one he lights.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="47fc2723-0d00-4482-9fa4-6319709b133d">
      <Text>He knocks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="1f470b94-a613-4009-ae5c-cce07c64fca8">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 1/8" Page="16" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DISPATCH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="24145dcf-cb35-4d49-8582-187bfcd0b5dd"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MOTHER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5e85a0a8-83e4-4b56-8a3c-e3dd796824d0"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="1681801b-90f6-4b89-a03c-476ffb6c4685"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SMALL FRAME HOUSE - KITCHEN - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="522c5e79-7cb7-41cc-8dd1-ff222299588a">
      <Text>A clean, tired kitchen. A dish towel of old mill sheeting hangs on the oven door. THE BOY, 16, sits at the table, eyes down. His MOTHER stands at the counter. Mercer stands inside the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="016175ea-424a-4929-83f6-d996789d48d0">
      <Text>Rucker sets the juvenile folder on the table in front of the boy. Squares it to the edge. The boy’s name on the tab, facing him. He leaves it closed, sits down across from him and puts his hat on his knee.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="90b8e2f5-6f43-4108-8d65-1d8f8a847fe7">
      <Text>The boy looks at the folder. His mother looks at it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc7be0ae-9583-4d8a-99df-d00471375996">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4b1d4021-9c22-4732-9034-d27ea02d05c7">
      <Text>That grass caught quick behind the school. Dry as it’s been.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ccaf2a57-5ad5-4f30-ad58-6263f5647ab7">
      <Text>Nothing from the boy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f7176b91-0341-46fa-a327-56d47d1c613b">
      <Text>MOTHER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8928fb3d-3ccb-47e6-90cc-f9fb4c74ae0e">
      <Text>Vernon. Look at the man.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="295f2c47-1124-479c-aba3-b0ec155eea61">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="16c0d962-e5f5-409a-bccf-60d07285c2cd">
      <Text>Ma’am. It’s all right. That’s why it’s me sitting here and not a deputy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cf506ae3-12fb-4c8a-bfbf-f77c7884af38">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="60c6d728-1496-4a5b-bb30-ff0e4201eb69">
      <Text>(to the boy)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5c29578d-0543-4104-b9a8-69fcf921aee1">
      <Text>Station One runs a junior program. Thursday nights, they’ll let you pull hose. You want to be around fire, that’s where it’s allowed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d0770ea-52c0-4fb8-8417-7c88cf171e87">
      <Text>He writes his name and number on a blank contact card and sets it beside the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fe2a12b0-8be9-450e-8cb4-30cc10b0e8b5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c8e66c19-1d02-4130-94f7-763ae3f2ca0c">
      <Text>Any other night you feel it coming on, you call me. I answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e2242764-9d23-4b26-81b0-47af3c5b56b1">
      <Text>He puts two fingers on the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e5b5bdac-8cc5-4386-b1fa-67b3622f33d0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="6401b636-25fc-4edb-b56c-e9e5d2fff2da">
      <Text>(to the mother)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d116008b-3824-415e-a90e-4edf6aa9a221">
      <Text>He shows up Thursdays, this stays closed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5442264a-0e24-4f24-abcd-12c3c4e7e815">
      <Text>Rucker puts on his hat. Mercer follows him out. The card remains between the boy and his mother.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="84715a05-2085-42fb-aabe-1838eca5b7f1">
      <Text>From the yard, the Tahoe radio carries through the open door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1986c9f9-91dd-46d9-a726-fe32b47375f2">
      <Text>DISPATCH (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="6e54da7e-2d01-4600-b2c9-46df5351c75f">
      <Text>(radio, off)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="21af9319-372b-4def-9d79-02633fa47e04">
      <Text>...Marshal, you copy? We’ve got —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="d997e008-a7d6-4370-aa16-6d966b26dbf2">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="17" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. MILL DISTRICT STREET - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8199c4b9-cba8-4dfd-8107-dbe02d475c3e">
      <Text>Three in the morning. A dog barking. Porch lights come on down a street of small frame houses.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="18d50844-cab2-47d0-a9a5-8b0c4584cba9">
      <Text>Beyond the rooftops, smoke rises, lit orange from below. Ash falls through the streetlight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3fb8ead1-7b40-458a-a7f3-aab5269b53a8">
      <Text>Screen doors open. Families gather on their lawns in bathrobes and unlaced boots. A man carries photo albums from his house to his truck.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1635765f-feac-4d5f-85ca-09b3289682f2">
      <Text>Sirens, converging on each other.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="fdb11241-ab9b-4260-93d8-d04ed10e9e0e">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="17" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="60557628-7c8b-4526-9752-fb0e0aebbb9f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7cfab505-65a5-48fb-8a0e-bbe162c5895f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="46b15893-9e95-4552-87a2-873acbf3e9cf"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE OLD LINE HALL - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8c0643eb-16a2-4474-b286-7401ca79af8f">
      <Text>A hundred-year-old, two-story heavy-timber building. Flames are already through the roof as the first engine pulls up. SLOAN comes off the rig.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="548951d8-6e66-47f8-ad1f-05bacb7adcfc">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d7131e27-d290-4f2f-b89c-19867a66842a">
      <Text>Hall’s gone. Get lines on the houses. Both sides.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="00b32b5e-93e8-4a8c-9fd5-38e3c2315fc7">
      <Text>Crews pull lines toward the neighboring houses. Firefighters raise an aerial ladder. Its master stream sweeps from one roof to the next.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e08d5a0f-d119-4674-94b7-819e7df1e9ce">
      <Text>Wind carries embers across the street. A firefighter sweeps a hose stream through them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2348f748-5bc8-4467-b99a-3ac78bd34c5b">
      <Text>More residents gather behind the tape—bathrobes, work jackets, children on shoulders. They watch in near silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c575d9e8-2035-4748-bd1c-b1808c8af1f0">
      <Text>JUNE runs up in a coat over her nightclothes. She stops at a charged hose line crossing the street.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e7117689-21ea-4826-8e50-d222c03f7aa9">
      <Text>Across it, the hall burns.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7043864d-9791-4d77-9bc5-cf8274103740">
      <Text>A neighbor puts a hand on her shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ddb58fdc-b585-4a1b-a0d0-4a9333c160a3">
      <Text>At the edge of the crowd, Rucker’s Tahoe, driver’s door hanging open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dea91cac-d538-43e7-a284-a793fc76f004">
      <Text>RUCKER stands at the tape with his back half to the fire. He watches the faces.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b11bf371-9ea9-411e-a943-69b64114514a">
      <Text>Mercer arrives beside him, camera in hand. He’s watching Sloan’s crew haul line toward the houses.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4e2fb00f-ac43-4125-9642-7aa72a170dd7">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7a8f5ab2-c41f-4e33-b72f-5520a1e279c3">
      <Text>Three weeks ago I’d be on that line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="40edbced-70cc-410e-9803-0d10d92be40b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7f0a9a8a-6657-4721-bc30-cd9cc23bc421">
      <Text>Three weeks ago you were on the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="70ce436c-3167-45f2-9447-ef987bd9ff16">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a50ff324-0262-4da7-94fa-cb890df4cc7f">
      <Text>What do we do?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="57e26d48-e96f-4503-b5f2-0d03d355d008">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cfca9458-7d82-413c-8ed5-aba4830aecd8">
      <Text>Not the fire. Them. Every face you can get.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a870a326-d125-45ad-8ff4-a6c3f79fca7d">
      <Text>Mercer turns the lens on the crowd and starts shooting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="656cf1d0-f37c-43af-8818-02a28ffc0a27">
      <Text>Back from the tape, hands in his pockets, a boy watches the water hit the roof. Not the fire. The water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="01f32e86-8cc5-482f-88ed-74b57fe8005a">
      <Text>The hall’s roof collapses inward, sending sparks above the building. People behind the tape cry out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="be8c22bd-829c-471f-b431-af9b7bc46ee0">
      <Text>Behind the tape, June stands beside a hose line, her arms at her sides. Orange firelight flickers across her face.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="258576f1-2a4a-4b86-92e6-b2d58b019d06">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="09b0913e-ac49-46e8-a886-6b0dad0a7d7e">
      <Text>You think he’s here?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b58905c8-e28d-46af-9391-635eea2e36f1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="434087af-404f-4754-b7d4-353dd65125a8">
      <Text>Keep shooting.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="afd9a450-22fb-4c14-89cd-503e02ca4e51">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="18" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MAN AT MEETING">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="779c0e37-e2dc-4f75-b8fa-e9e8b4c9f55e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MOSS">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6e6fe44c-a4d7-43b8-aa31-66044247d935"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PARDUE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="8d4fab3b-bb0b-41c8-ab3d-1c34d07d7094"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d8505704-0685-4107-855a-99c5732f9058"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SECOND WOMAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2cae86a2-c7d2-4ad0-b129-e4f92f68dc45"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="WOMAN AT MEETING">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="c4966b7c-b1ad-407c-9224-2baeca5db17e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. VFW HALL - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="93d5e151-1400-42a2-bafd-a4144936572f">
      <Text>Folding chairs, every one full. Standing room at both doors. Phones up and filming. Beside the entrance: a coffee can with a slot cut into the lid and a hand-lettered sign-up sheet: NIGHT PATROL.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c6dc2897-dea8-4a17-b32a-ae520d1660a1">
      <Text>FIRE CHIEF ARLEN MOSS, 50s, thick through the middle, turnout pants under a department polo, and POLICE CHIEF ROY </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PARDUE</Text>
      <Text>, 50s, small and neat, hair combed wet, wait at the front without a stage or podium. RUCKER enters with MERCER.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="19b7b152-df76-4d4e-927c-e56e79efced9">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PARDUE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8ae6ff1c-5f00-40ca-a4d6-7ade5c969174">
      <Text>I got four men and two cars. They go home scared, half this town’s walking their street with a shotgun by Friday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="34362ca8-e65b-436b-baeb-ddfeb4151661">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="018661a0-37fe-4b0a-a8a6-3663fc9f0a4b">
      <Text>Then let’s give them something to do that ain’t that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c4a6736f-fe47-444b-abc9-bbae57ca4ed3">
      <Text>Rucker hands his hat to Mercer, who moves to the side wall. Rucker walks to the front and waits. A chair scrapes. Someone lowers a phone. The last conversation stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fab31b28-dcf4-4d5b-9572-5d09758f8d51">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cb01ed45-1394-4a7c-bb4e-cf65267571a6">
      <Text>Evening. Eldon Rucker. Deputy state fire marshal. I’ll stay till the questions run out. Nobody leaves ahead of me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="36cd01b4-89a2-4a4b-8852-1e4f791b3ce1">
      <Text>A WOMAN is already on her feet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c5065130-ed57-424a-8ea0-3f440ca71b58">
      <Text>WOMAN AT MEETING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c4e145f9-4902-434d-b9f1-7a6a4bcc09a9">
      <Text>My kids sleep upstairs. What are we supposed to do at night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e0f25a53-a381-46e6-8794-52c650c28163">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2e0da0db-65a2-4c08-9c79-549ae33d6eeb">
      <Text>Sleep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fc64bcaf-0bdb-46dd-8b2d-912795d6fe19">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a2e538de-e07b-4261-b309-c257e83e790e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3dd39155-b149-4c04-90b1-28c1ff619962">
      <Text>That part’s mine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6432f4c3-5af3-4d77-9e4c-e49e968bcdb9">
      <Text>The woman sits. The room settles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b2018b3c-3bec-4242-8f67-5ebdfd0d780b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="63954d97-1713-4a49-b115-e0997011369c">
      <Text>Four fires since spring. Same hand. Three empty buildings, then the hall. All four empty when he lit them. He looks before he lights, and he’s looked the same way four times running.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8bcbd49-67fb-4dea-a745-73ce06c6305d">
      <Text>A SECOND WOMAN stands near the back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89af2517-c1d1-4428-bf2a-15ebc8e44f3b">
      <Text>SECOND WOMAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="81e17535-fecc-4693-acfd-08d0dd60267f">
      <Text>The hall wasn’t but a block from houses. What if he stops being careful?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="612eabfd-62aa-4aa6-b975-b629b0c235e5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7b483e0c-6483-412e-8cd6-1839f8c2fd2b">
      <Text>He’s had four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8dff2aa5-6bb7-4582-8344-cefe2f93a0e3">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6d694302-a262-45b5-83dc-5a338c7544c3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5a49985b-3d14-4a3a-a04d-d2cedf68cfa5">
      <Text>He won’t get five.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f6852a8c-0bd4-4822-a99c-5e926ae7f21b">
      <Text>Nobody moves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1e37890f-a1f9-4340-a617-bf828d408fdd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9e1be44c-500e-4907-abe0-491574192164">
      <Text>Porch lights on. Sign that sheet if you want to walk with a deputy. You see something, call it in. You do not follow it, and you do not carry a gun looking for it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2f792853-9acd-4445-ab61-0b2e1536ce3e">
      <Text>An OLD MAN takes the patrol sign-up sheet and passes it down the first row. Rucker answers questions until no hands remain raised. On his way out, he puts several folded bills into the coffee can.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d1562658-3a50-4967-b51c-a24b090883f8">
      <Text>Outside, two men lock their rifles in separate trucks. Mercer returns Rucker’s hat. Rucker watches the room empty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6d39afce-90fd-4ce3-b6f5-2115f934e88c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7caf3bc1-f0d7-464a-8f5f-d0619f06d1e8">
      <Text>If he was in that room, he didn’t come for answers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4cf4335f-9eae-450e-a138-5f128bb032d7">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="20" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BIG PETE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0996e9ae-0176-4e31-81aa-a0895773a168"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COBB">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6e61dca7-7768-42a4-877c-493edd60bc38"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR DOOR - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1c80fb1e-c45e-43f5-ac1f-1f3e10e24bbb">
      <Text>Late. The lot is nearly empty. The rear door stands propped open, kitchen light across the pavement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5e0497e5-3a58-4935-9f9b-bf04cbfe65b0">
      <Text>MERLE COBB, 60s, owner of the Magnolia, reading glasses pushed up in his hair, waits beside it, phone in hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="42e3432c-c43f-48eb-ad26-775dde15abe4">
      <Text>BIG PETE TILLMAN, 50s — six-four, heavy through the chest and belly, thick hands — arrives carrying a hardware-store bag. He takes out a length of chain and a padlock, the price sticker still on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="efd5a487-7c28-4274-8046-f1b60272e273">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a17e2b3d-8ce0-466e-806a-60e54691fbeb">
      <Text>Somebody’s burning buildings in this town. Nobody comes through my back door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7af2ad64-86a4-4bc8-8ca0-562af9d91cc1">
      <Text>Pete looks at the door. Then at the push bar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a78241cd-63fb-48fd-bd1c-f7b21930b790">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7da56132-4254-4391-af5e-602c575de86d">
      <Text>That’s an exit, Merle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb638dbd-11bd-4b27-925e-9f441571cd78">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab4b9bd0-b7cd-418f-9080-9c46cf1fc3b9">
      <Text>It’s a service door. Ain’t nobody using that at night.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="65a594e9-4d3a-4a76-9ad5-09eb284dbc57">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f77cd636-975a-4778-b286-d86cb7f5782f">
      <Text>It’s got a bar on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2090e0b1-5df3-434f-87b8-b685d8f69f11">
      <Text>Cobb says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4239c0d1-2210-4a65-b6f3-fd3af5a07eb5">
      <Text>Pete holds up the chain.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="af331b5e-243c-4478-a129-876c74a361aa">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e35bf88a-39ca-405e-8d90-3661d1e5fe52">
      <Text>Fire marshal sees this —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f11f80c1-37a9-4162-94c7-669e03bd9564">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a3afed3c-98ff-47d8-81e5-34f023f0204a">
      <Text>Fire marshal ain’t watching my back door, Pete.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1a55d0ae-8ee4-4790-95b9-ed0279f763b2">
      <Text>From inside, a burst of laughter. Music underneath it. Pete looks through the open doorway.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8134fa72-6705-494c-b9a0-945d53913198">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="733ce54d-9dff-4ac2-bd8f-76e02f80d8b7">
      <Text>Every night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="90d6789b-e28b-479b-8706-6f79522569dd">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ff78d4f7-dd4c-4761-9bb9-6ab41faf56f0">
      <Text>Every night. Once the kitchen’s closed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="708b5686-7e1b-4ef0-a43d-58043e12957b">
      <Text>Pete runs the chain through the door hardware and snugs it tight. He closes the padlock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bfee1d2d-8944-4085-bcb0-21134a57dc46">
      <Text>SNAP.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b0987f06-183b-4725-b6ad-dbf466f4326c">
      <Text>Cobb takes the key and threads it onto his key ring. Pete glances at the chained door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9e7f6d47-d799-466f-86fa-774a9f42ff68">
      <Text>Music, voices and bottles clinking come from inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b4bfd3a0-7a8b-4675-b910-571fafe54359">
      <Text>Cobb pockets the key ring.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="b9cb65c6-daf8-4fb5-80ed-0965146980a7">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 4/8" Page="21" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COBB">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="11cf36af-a879-4f66-bdc8-9a08bd8e9585"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="3d58aade-c1d8-40c1-b53c-c477d70636b6"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR SERVICE AREA - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="42f28844-adac-4a5d-bb6d-39322652c9e6">
      <Text>The rear kitchen door stands open. Inside, pans clatter, glass racks slide across counters, and the walk-in door repeatedly opens and closes during afternoon prep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="70df2f72-2237-48a2-960d-b739af78c796">
      <Text>Outside, the walk-in’s CONDENSING UNIT runs with a loud, uneven hum. HOYT kneels beside it with the access panel removed. Meter leads are clipped inside. He has lined the screws on a folded shop towel.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d78c74c2-e140-4f1d-8ec3-67ba09a2ac1b">
      <Text>The unit shuts off. Hoyt checks his watch.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="302557b2-871d-4cdc-82a7-7d7f0f0cb8d4">
      <Text>COBB steps outside through the rear door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="74647dff-37b9-4404-aac9-b438c0f4483c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2c842de6-fae2-4c01-a239-ecb4ac48cb63">
      <Text>Thirty-six seconds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c8b637ec-85d6-437e-8454-ed2705f3dcb6">
      <Text>The unit kicks back on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8620a2e0-dee5-404f-a972-9e38e7291cda">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab1d46a5-f61b-4892-985e-12997aced358">
      <Text>Amos. Leave that a minute.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f3a1b5ff-4971-46c2-b209-ff18eb9c2204">
      <Text>Hoyt listens to the restart, then gets to his feet. Wrench in hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="85272807-3218-49c2-b995-e5fcd7e03a5e">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="461967cb-ab2a-475c-8561-3f7c65c1d346">
      <Text>Bank finally approved the sprinkler work. Thirty-one thousand, and they rolled the mechanical into </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Dunphy’s</Text>
      <Text> contract. Heat, refrigeration, service — the whole building. I can’t carry that note and keep you both.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="61929d88-0147-4b80-979d-062d256a98d2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="adda56c6-2bf4-4796-9bf0-8ecb78b4ae0a">
      <Text>Wait... What? When?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="988b29e7-fc1f-4f7c-9afc-30fd99a51813">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c8fa072f-595d-4252-b545-c0f216b83ea0">
      <Text>Today.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24977e6e-06af-4380-8e3e-1c1ecac07a64">
      <Text>Hoyt looks into the open unit. Cobb remains standing over him. Hoyt unclips the meter leads and coils one around his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d1ad7a8-7256-44df-8e3c-8012ff37c5f4">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="123acd11-5844-4f45-9407-d457bac9f426">
      <Text>I wanted you to hear it from me before somebody else told you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b25fa448-7e52-49c8-8331-b2ee935a3436">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de327303-fe6d-4588-b493-9bf302582b71">
      <Text>When’d you give </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Dunphy</Text>
      <Text> the work?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1deb75ea-9fbe-4313-b3f5-807b78d573cf">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="31527957-7e46-42d4-a7de-ff94e405bac1">
      <Text>This morning.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="54940bdd-3593-46c2-b7ee-f14b95f663cf">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="11c676f0-0f85-4988-981c-7f8f1100de94">
      <Text>Nine years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6c66764b-f5dc-4d14-a31e-23618b9d179e">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0c797218-ed2c-4792-a5f8-d6ada908c202">
      <Text>I know. And I know what I owe you. Three Sundays, two weeks on top. It’ll be cash on the fifteenth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e3d26c34-ded5-48b2-bbed-1ef719836206">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fe6c383d-29f6-40c7-8b10-5bdeafcf8ec0">
      <Text>That ain’t what I said.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e948201b-642f-4991-8fc3-31426cc08d88">
      <Text>The unit shuts off again. Hoyt checks his watch. He stops with the meter lead half-coiled around his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3cf88431-fa2f-4c48-adce-61b9a374da39">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="743f5f57-5be2-4b8b-afeb-9d5b8c37a8e1">
      <Text>Part comes Tuesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b1670f9d-2b59-4d9b-96ce-0a6e394dd77f">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="125598db-132b-4bf1-9b1b-bcd41929af89">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Dunphy</Text>
      <Text> can handle it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c71303a8-08ae-4090-aa97-74e88d6cf139">
      <Text>Hoyt looks through the open rear door, across the kitchen and into the dim rear hall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="152646de-9fad-49ca-865f-f4409e97f82c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a5eea985-44ce-4253-abea-fadca5bb21de">
      <Text>He don’t know this place. Don’t know what that motor sounds like when it’s right, which breaker goes when it rains, or which doors hang when the weather turns. You don’t learn nine years off a work order.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="21fa7584-503c-49ce-8e00-b3aaf7983e6b">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b973ac9d-664e-4586-a086-99b68624f413">
      <Text>He’ll learn.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="721800ec-0e60-433a-a6a8-c42fb13dca35">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91dd9937-e3a3-43b0-baa5-dc7113d9b7d1">
      <Text>He’ll learn what breaks. I learned what keeps it from breaking.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="334ded82-787e-4b24-8908-32108e31fa66">
      <Text>Inside, a glass rack slows across the counter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d33f2978-b5b4-467f-843d-7a4d4f6ccd91">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0164dcc9-b7c5-4108-b0cb-64a57fdc2d60">
      <Text>Nine years, Cobb. Every Sunday call. Every storm. Every time something quit after midnight, you never had to wonder if I’d come.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d97a7a56-a030-4a7d-bdae-02e8a612f4b4">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d291ceee-0660-4e76-9641-3ed22388ec66">
      <Text>I know what you did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="60eb4396-e91c-4c4b-97af-c265b79f4e31">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a6c38e71-9db2-47aa-a601-a2aa5e244e1a">
      <Text>No. You know what you paid me for.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="97643111-060f-41e1-9b9e-5edac35754b9">
      <Text>Cobb has no answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb4e3166-7e25-46b2-816c-2af3bee92299">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="09b2bc9a-ac90-4ce0-8f34-72042282766c">
      <Text>Don’t stand there counting Sundays like nine years fits in an envelope.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="60b4c1de-f636-4925-a809-1e21fd290e01">
      <Text>The glass rack has stopped. The KITCHEN HAND holding it watches through the open door. Cobb notices.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5313201c-0e8f-4c14-ae2f-14c0643e05f1">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="79105a17-c6a0-4046-b98d-dc131bd14b43">
      <Text>Lower your voice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9b7c37cb-2788-4d28-893c-e7ed77a1d5ca">
      <Text>Hoyt doesn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c22da7b0-663a-40cc-a0a4-4a038893268b">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32263394-b755-420c-87a8-49c60dc97ba9">
      <Text>You gave him my building before you gave me the truth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e299e43e-5637-494c-9044-972a82e925b3">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d55f6c78-d925-4d58-842d-ba73c4cfb6e2">
      <Text>It isn’t your building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a5e3edd9-1a67-42a7-bb83-c0dfb263dee8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="335b1a78-f01e-4afa-b495-f21d21dd5751">
      <Text>Been mine every time it broke.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aa921145-a7af-4411-9366-2b67c65d0319">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1ad83fa4-b405-4a69-8e45-1fcf074d6ff8">
      <Text>This is business, Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dfa1172a-2f6c-4d5b-a022-636d742b625d">
      <Text>The meter lead tightens around Hoyt’s fist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6d601795-3a2c-4c65-99aa-4ccf62d21e83">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8658673e-460a-45c7-8585-dbbca7b57ebe">
      <Text>You keep waiting till everything breaks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6cfd565b-6885-42fa-8eb0-3754261ed54c">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="42f6b7aa-64de-4884-9e64-4a6fc956c5c3">
      <Text>That’s enough.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d41cf772-ea9c-40d3-b151-d9119608caf1">
      <Text>Hoyt steps toward him. His voice carries into the kitchen now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dd436369-3ec9-4da4-a653-b064e409fcca">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="294b1c47-1846-47f9-8651-632b04069604">
      <Text>One morning you’re gonna come in here and find this whole place gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="042fa943-d94c-4334-8ea5-4f6c02a84315">
      <Text>The last pan settles into the sink. The kitchen is silent.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fc809fdd-5730-4084-bf78-7efa60c15756">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="df1d4f2c-e9df-463d-9e84-f3a441f7693e">
      <Text>It ain’t anything you did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d8ee486-c722-4427-8154-cf959154cb1e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6906bc74-6799-41f1-85f3-40b0eb9711b1">
      <Text>I know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="26d0053f-0023-468e-88bc-a4d6809f354a">
      <Text>The glass rack starts moving again. Prep resumes, but quieter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="499f466b-5379-4889-8ec7-a77064ffc344">
      <Text>Hoyt kneels beside the unit and fits the access panel back into place.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15625145-f3c8-4620-832f-31cf34b39271">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a1ee970d-4f38-40ed-b6ef-8ab472ab22fe">
      <Text>You can leave that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fb66f565-79c6-4d76-919e-07658ae16f43">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="796a8ac2-4aab-4e1a-8c00-01fb83a8de6a">
      <Text>Can’t leave it open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7b0ee882-1d5f-4696-a14b-eb83ebfd2ba4">
      <Text>He runs in the first screw.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5e2227d9-ffaa-41d1-be63-be8c74f1a57d">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dfd75778-7788-424a-8166-8dfa75bbf696">
      <Text>Ordered that part off my account.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="227c5671-cceb-42ac-93d6-c27fdec84866">
      <Text>Cobb considers him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="500f6579-fcde-4045-bb23-ffc908a868c2">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ce959b26-7c0c-4fc4-bea3-ad6489f67ab8">
      <Text>Then finish this one. Part goes in Tuesday. After that, bring me the keys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="77b16274-7093-4c51-a4b7-71c71e3f1caa">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="65c315d1-87e3-41a7-9e78-58831f9f7243">
      <Text>I’ll get it in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="491ab797-50ec-4cbf-8ef6-d03eb73fa35d">
      <Text>Cobb goes back through the kitchen. The unit kicks on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cea701cc-ad35-48ba-9a6e-55f6c70f5d71">
      <Text>Hoyt listens to it working.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="2fda24fc-4980-4ce7-ada1-749f06fa608d">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="25" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="64a1d1c8-d76e-4d6e-8cf4-65a20e9a695e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUNE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0bafb4bf-f316-43d4-9850-24be46adc708"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR LOT - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e101d5b9-647b-4576-bb56-ee075274431c">
      <Text>Hoyt walks past the renovation trucks carrying his toolbox. He places it in the bed of his pickup and climbs into the cab.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="92aa5156-c2c6-41df-9439-be0a957a09c1">
      <Text>He closes the door. The noise of the lot falls to a distant clatter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1ef34e03-4e1b-48a0-8fca-00237a2fd1e4">
      <Text>Hoyt sits behind the wheel without starting the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ace8b27a-e329-4143-8fe9-24af215646f0">
      <Text>Through the windshield, workers unload lengths of sprinkler pipe. Beyond them, the Magnolia’s open rear door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8a9dd0d-61ca-438e-ac76-45f0035884b8">
      <Text>He watches a moment longer, then takes the building keys from his pocket. He finds the worn brass front-door key and starts working it around the split ring.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="66ef549a-35c3-4220-8998-e95e4197f177">
      <Text>His phone BUZZES.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2827c3df-3097-4e23-84e3-f23dedf91af9">
      <Text>The screen reads JUNE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c18312d7-76ca-47a3-8d69-a9d0bcab3028">
      <Text>Hoyt closes his hand around the keys and answers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="590b5bca-b330-413d-90a4-04bf2c365fe4">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="df8bc05a-d2b7-4729-9cd3-1e1a379c7538">
      <Text>June.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5a4510e2-6ea9-4d4b-9478-0c5ee921055e">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aaf3c3e9-57ea-4156-8796-6dbf5bf2f935">
      <Text>Merle ain’t picking up the office. Is he in there?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="550722c8-128b-4c2f-9120-e241f215438d">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a4bca81a-8dcb-40c9-a3ee-73f758ecc5ca">
      <Text>He’s in there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f222856d-b666-4d10-b3da-1f6cace43972">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7d44b920-34c5-4c9e-87cb-57e23aee7dd6">
      <Text>Tell him I need the room Thursday. I got two new ones I ain’t run with the band —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="512e630f-e350-46af-9a5d-f44631b80f11">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f5e1cdf-40e5-4d68-8329-6faa84aef768">
      <Text>He let me go, June.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b70b81af-f8d4-4259-a0e8-8239f3bde091">
      <Text>Nothing on the line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="86f1121b-92b6-46a7-afa4-984a5df05eb9">
      <Text>Hoyt looks at the rear-door key, halfway off the ring. His thumb presses against its edge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e132a96-69ff-4196-86e3-6462d6dbb8b5">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cdaf507d-c245-4371-8e27-483cf827d337">
      <Text>Since when.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="acd341a0-d673-439b-bcd0-3a528f44f597">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e5dc9f60-2ae6-4782-948f-a6287ea35482">
      <Text>Since ten minutes ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9eec11be-748b-4dd6-8ad5-b0fc6a4ef3c7">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a6c09a08-42d2-487e-b959-a7d212640cd2">
      <Text>Nine years, Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d3550819-7f6c-4b48-b7dc-a778c4a1006c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4343fb8f-a5aa-4134-8f6b-fe160d738bbc">
      <Text>It ain’t him. It’s the sprinklers, he says.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e60a58a-d0bf-4575-8e46-2f525f1e546a">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="210adddc-0912-4270-a132-e3b16090ee73">
      <Text>Friday’s my last show.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcce600d-8afc-407d-a651-18ddacfd14a0">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e557e374-672e-4aac-abd0-6d830c53989d">
      <Text>Might not be welcome now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1aa2473b-d3e5-4ca5-a0c5-37b9c1455583">
      <Text>JUNE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dc376bdc-e923-4d4e-a1cf-bed8ae7a0614">
      <Text>Come anyway.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f527a65d-01ae-4a92-96c4-68d177ff86cf">
      <Text>Hoyt watches the workers carry the sprinkler pipe through the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f37ca030-71b9-4678-a1a4-d587dc4d4862">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0b8063fd-f648-4574-baef-d6f29d41192f">
      <Text>What time you start?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b7f5772a-863c-4282-aa51-943c9e284d16">
      <Text>He works the rear-door key back onto the ring.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1fd0d748-6952-4575-bda9-14c23f2721d3">
      <Text>Hoyt puts the truck key in the ignition and starts the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="4fc17e24-4730-497c-93de-7f35b658ee3c">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="26" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="CREW MAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b7314f35-72d3-4458-b07c-f8b6e499b6a1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DEENA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fd4f7002-d4fe-4649-b738-40782c300953"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d48fce3a-dc0d-493a-bba7-e2db88d8245d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - STOREROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c9cf826e-3ce5-4451-9f11-c86dfc091748">
      <Text>A narrow utility room opens off the rear hall behind the kitchen. Steel shelving lines the walls beside a mop sink. The walk-in cooler’s compressor sits with its access panel removed. A high window sits above the shelving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3f7bb031-82a0-4318-b155-8ae3fe9ccdbd">
      <Text>HOYT sits on the floor beside the compressor, cleaning a component with degreaser and a rag.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ab370f7e-dc72-437e-b601-af0a21348e43">
      <Text>Rolls of renovation foam stand along the wall. A CREW MEMBER carries in another roll and adds it to the row.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b4e5d061-49e8-4409-a0d3-132d5d68d6e2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bc313393-9a7f-4cc1-b104-01bfd60ebc08">
      <Text>Who the hell stacks it against my shelving?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b112da58-de14-4b95-9321-647a7b7558fd">
      <Text>CREW MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8986d96f-2cdf-4ea3-82ab-bd923b866236">
      <Text>Boss said out of the barroom.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6e52f4f8-f55d-4048-b8cc-c7a52fa62160">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c9f321f8-8583-447b-961e-8ec3da367f7f">
      <Text>Boss don’t work back here.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="789d4ac0-cd6d-5b14-8835-d4c4631b65e5">
      <Text>CREW MAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ff50aa2b-6549-5472-9c12-1038fde4f46c">
      <Text>Rest of it comes Friday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="710b68a1-466a-43f6-9455-4fd10bfc5011">
      <Text>They keep stacking. He keeps working. The compressor kicks on, runs rough, then settles. Hoyt ties the louvered door open with a length of wire knotted to a shelf bracket.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5a30d3e0-a492-4678-845c-c609d024059d">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="0ae5ee90-a5dd-48b9-9e50-586aba431a51">
      <Text>(to the crew man)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7bf09c4e-2616-4c73-a718-56e94a8f9f3b">
      <Text>Door stays open. Thing’s got to breathe.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2795f935-796a-4e4a-806e-5b11844cf554">
      <Text>A five-gallon glass water jug — a carboy — with a couple inches of water blocks the crew’s path. A crew member’s boot misses it by inches. Hoyt lifts the jug onto the deep sill beneath the high window. He caps the degreaser and returns it to the shelf.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7f63c9a2-359b-4f89-94f9-01fd1f8eaaba">
      <Text>At the doorway, Cobb raises a cheap digital camera and takes a wide photograph for the renovation insurance file. The whole west wall fits in the frame. He moves on to the next room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4a04e121-e4c5-4906-82d5-1addf5269f59">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 2/8" Page="27" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a025a159-7955-478b-ba73-c55f432f603e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="34660474-29dc-4c21-aaa0-22d8ab3f19fc"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HOYT HOUSE - EVENING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dce49ab4-1702-412a-a9a1-de56fc7fa822">
      <Text>The small frame house at the end of the short street. The work truck in the yard, hood up. The window unit drips onto bare dirt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0d2bc946-c4bb-4066-a1f4-244aef7fd5df">
      <Text>KENDRA HOYT, 16 — her father’s long frame already, headphones down around her neck — holds a droplight into the engine bay. Her left hand’s nails are painted. The right one, holding the light, isn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1c32cd89-7293-4c85-bb26-b262fe80cf0a">
      <Text>HOYT is in past his elbows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="39af52f3-96c4-458d-a78f-3c1b23db3aae">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7cd599f1-177a-4e62-87ed-48ada2420a28">
      <Text>Light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="75a49f42-cb80-4df9-bb0f-fa0b53683622">
      <Text>She moves it two inches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ad53d33c-86b5-4da1-99fa-94d5ffc0a64b">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e494b70d-4d16-4ef3-be0d-4c11e637b776">
      <Text>Other way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="72db5a36-e1c6-49d0-b62a-d3b605a257be">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bfc5a341-1dba-4644-9333-b46ff94d160d">
      <Text>You could hold it and I could do the wrench part.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="442a1c04-b2ea-42bd-8555-0b19f148a580">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5ae2cd1b-6348-4ffb-902a-10722a2990cb">
      <Text>You could.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c2a8c0c-3d75-48ff-ae96-ca808e7f36a9">
      <Text>He keeps working. She keeps holding.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15164ac9-058f-4ccf-97fc-803709eeec26">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2e7d87cc-bc86-4bba-9a67-5ff728f7198f">
      <Text>Start it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="75376e5a-d8ac-4919-baa9-799f82a00875">
      <Text>She gets behind the wheel and starts it. The engine runs — a fast tick under the idle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c98dd451-b988-4072-97d9-6b317d9dab62">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="40138b2e-bf57-4af5-abe1-7011e44fbb16">
      <Text>What do you hear?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59ff9535-7bd9-4939-8d20-7cbf4ca651c3">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9b8e93e2-cf35-46d1-8077-7f8c4e7c085c">
      <Text>The truck.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b7d4114b-9e57-4e3d-b77b-84cfaa9b7582">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8ac3507c-ba7a-4024-af49-0c40b2f1b432">
      <Text>Under it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4292e549-b166-431b-8e35-9120f791913a">
      <Text>She closes her eyes. Listens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fd96cd74-0052-49ba-9e91-060e4e4b3a2a">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="81d18d50-9e17-4ca4-8e79-68e3f2f6526e">
      <Text>Ticking. Little fast ticking — like a sewing machine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="103c10ff-f9f2-4076-867b-bf317c5b2cdc">
      <Text>Hoyt nods once and draws a hand across his throat. She kills the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="acbf8ff8-a305-48de-b3f8-224430a61c47">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ad2fe44a-4116-4607-8c1d-08ecf32127d7">
      <Text>Lifter. Needs oil more than it needs us.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a505bd0f-c68b-596f-88f3-fd5c7316baec">
      <Text>He wipes his hands on the rag.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b550f782-614f-4127-8d26-b0c8bfaec84f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a1a5c814-b836-4b4e-aa7b-a95c625ceb81">
      <Text>Can’t fix a noise you can’t name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7513c332-cc3d-403a-a842-4bf6fef57f7d">
      <Text>She comes back around to the fender and takes up the light without being told.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0cb320b4-d61b-4f26-b51f-747bc197b351">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b8baf3a2-ab89-4d28-95a6-1b190a61ff0b">
      <Text>Trish’s after church Sunday?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ee711b61-12fa-4019-bdad-14e0c9c3f2c1">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="870fa6dc-8781-4261-816d-e8befa6ab384">
      <Text>Sunday’s Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13c139c9-a3f8-4a3e-a9ee-a1ef4ff9299b">
      <Text>He pulls the dipstick. Reads it against the last of the daylight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9185180b-40ca-4ac3-816f-60fb0a6abc16">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7b9c00a2-bf58-4159-b75c-9ec6b19211f3">
      <Text>You’re home before supper. All week you’ve been home before supper.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9ccfe63d-3faf-486b-b73e-b1b8e0d1913a">
      <Text>A moment. Hoyt seats the dipstick back in its tube.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2039a773-6820-4878-b2b2-02e03655184a">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="374f756d-a3f2-47c0-b8d9-8552c23d84d7">
      <Text>Hold the light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5a28a9c3-511e-4ee2-ac60-adeca2d84575">
      <Text>She looks at him a second. Then holds the light. He goes back in past his elbows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="22a55036-911c-40d6-8a9a-8e916c5a8cdd">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da70b88b-bf51-4af3-882e-d43e073e59bd">
      <Text>I get my license in March.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="16455789-867a-45bc-b2e3-9a6e949912c5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="330eaa78-dce2-4d92-8617-7c6689c07afa">
      <Text>Truck’ll be ready.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="be069bbd-f0a8-4a15-89f4-9a3462bb4fdb">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43011c65-c81a-48fa-a160-d15098195ef4">
      <Text>March, Daddy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5877c9d7-d793-4730-89f2-ca1c4baf82b4">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="000d1f42-a6da-454a-85f3-1a743ad53b7d">
      <Text>I heard you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e8cf7d26-eb80-454d-bbb9-33cffd29ec15">
      <Text>He works another moment. Then he straightens, wipes the wrench on the rag and holds it out to her. Kendra looks at it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b68659a4-2271-4b2e-9b49-4bf63d9b7a37">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9c685858-a6f7-41b5-be01-a6dc8786b29c">
      <Text>You name the noise, can’t nobody sell you one you ain’t got.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="875b5858-6423-4a0e-8ad2-c2c2ebeccd49">
      <Text>(off her look)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="14b946f2-8a56-4f36-a03e-4a3d7129052f">
      <Text>Trade.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fa8c5cf0-0157-4ac1-bc49-e0f594e88dcd">
      <Text>She hands him the light and takes the wrench. He aims the beam into the engine bay. Kendra leans in over the fender, both arms inside up to her elbows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6292e102-e1ec-49ce-85ea-290ec0f04caf">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b0f42154-def6-40e2-970b-27a7c55e74e6">
      <Text>Tell me where.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ede0cbce-9e96-4a5c-8a18-2cc3f21dd133">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dd14427f-ee26-4335-b63f-0825367260d9">
      <Text>Other way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b2d31620-53bc-427a-9e6b-876ef0a52e7b">
      <Text>Hoyt shifts the light two inches. Kendra smiles down into the engine and keeps working.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="af437fa5-4757-465c-b090-dfb46f9bf25d">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="30" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ad7cadd2-f01f-4b3b-9e88-8e29c565e6ec"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="59adbb0c-c063-49e7-a8e0-06a755c05338"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="TY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f301109c-2bfd-49be-ab65-8f345dca9f55"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. RUCKER HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7fcc17e1-1fb0-4acf-926a-addadca53b3b">
      <Text>A brick ranch on several acres. A state Tahoe and a pickup in the driveway. Fishing rods lean against the pickup’s tailgate.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5489e2e8-c828-4d36-bb54-cebc62c265ba">
      <Text>DONNA RUCKER, 44, small and straight-backed, her hair pinned off her neck, loads a cooler into the truck bed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4840a2f0-1973-4d8c-ab20-7a5fecd2c6a9">
      <Text>TY RUCKER, 16, broad-shouldered like his father, swings a duffel in after it. Rucker comes out of the house with the rods.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="abe36536-9f91-41aa-be5b-9da12a6b2a34">
      <Text>TY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="06d5d658-34a1-4f7a-86dd-2a7c236484ca">
      <Text>Coach moved me up Wednesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8de23166-19fb-4a77-87e3-c4112ec1c393">
      <Text>Rucker looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b5ff3a52-28ba-4d13-acd9-1fd5891f6ee0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d8436002-ad24-49f1-90ec-26463e765d6d">
      <Text>Varsity.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2f559c57-bb21-487a-9d61-f6e9351960f3">
      <Text>Ty nods.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fea97e60-d546-420f-9152-4bab6b95bc32">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="88aa4492-48cc-46d0-b653-5b4c9d49a6aa">
      <Text>Why didn’t you tell me Wednesday?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="18cdbf78-fac2-41aa-a982-68a2512e10ec">
      <Text>TY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2201f108-be48-4e40-bb2a-3c9402a65515">
      <Text>You weren’t home.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="84953625-5d65-43b4-be2a-491aaee3999b">
      <Text>Rucker takes that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c18fbd9f-8a87-474b-846c-cf25c195ca2f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="766c2fa3-7021-4a87-8e0c-a55c2aa7dbce">
      <Text>Where’s he got you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3ce20f5c-89ef-40ed-8c64-470ff1b120f4">
      <Text>TY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="492dadd8-6cd5-4ccf-bbad-2398994db471">
      <Text>Outside linebacker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bb2d612a-1d4a-4b04-a39f-77c47658d9e8">
      <Text>Rucker considers the position. Considers his son.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="55979b9f-e56a-4c07-b2d2-bc6955eeba55">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b022de8a-2290-4611-a62a-31b20b605ac2">
      <Text>That’s where I’d put you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="003cdbed-6665-4460-aa3e-cbd1d301c87c">
      <Text>Ty takes the rods from him and lays them in the bed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c55fbfcd-5e67-4382-af38-7b2a140061bc">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="69d133d0-e8ab-488c-b1fd-9e16d63a1c9f">
      <Text>Ty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="822ad219-1504-4d43-a4c3-e4d079714ce8">
      <Text>Ty turns back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1ba9fbf2-dba9-4f20-9c10-542d51d53792">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6a3526a8-9b1e-4596-880e-b5e989900ccb">
      <Text>You earned it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4ef33d10-4706-4bd8-b1b5-66459a192042">
      <Text>A restrained smile from Ty. Rucker’s phone BUZZES. The smile disappears as both of them look toward the sound. Donna watches Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b93ac48e-e91b-4b8c-9aa0-bc9932c581a6">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="73857a73-c16f-4ead-96e7-2132109469ed">
      <Text>Tip line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c6421054-5932-4f15-8c4d-1e44eeb24108">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2ad93ab2-641c-4862-9ccc-1d6f8540e2f7">
      <Text>Danny’s covering the tip line. You told me that Tuesday. You told Danny that Tuesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c0b63cb7-480c-4a0d-9304-f36f9085421a">
      <Text>Donna holds out her hand. Rucker looks at it, then takes the phone from his pocket and puts it in her palm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8dd711b8-8ee4-4971-8525-62e657a7283f">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5f4cc710-2c72-4d99-aeff-0e89e5c93f91">
      <Text>Glovebox till Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="44059b34-3f0a-4d3d-9ed4-fe7126ec0c33">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6ea009f1-27f1-496d-91de-596e040f86d7">
      <Text>Yes ma’am.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d20a0aca-52b5-4ae9-b99f-3c7bab30d7c3">
      <Text>Donna gets into the truck and puts the phone in the glovebox. Closes it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="fe3695a0-9f28-42f5-aeb5-c9c3e6724d41">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="31" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BIG PETE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="dc7738a3-e8e0-4f98-9e38-8e419e75bb0b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DEENA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="c580cfe6-10af-4ee1-a571-88cf460059e1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="62168b0a-4c51-4045-9c62-b52c8d49de3d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUNE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="74d5eb70-a57c-4097-8fb9-e13ce0e00926"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ONDINE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a49db23c-1887-4684-ac89-a7a880a89337"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RAY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2209b8a9-cef3-40c8-8330-5dcc97b19a7b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA LOUNGE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2e42879a-009c-4320-8529-a812b6428b56">
      <Text>Warm, loud, low-ceilinged. Christmas lights over the bar in July. A dance floor the size of a kitchen. A four-piece band on a bandstand one foot high.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7f961d4c-57a0-4812-8ccb-5f804a6d5555">
      <Text>Pete on the door, calling every name coming in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fee384f7-ca8e-447f-bfd6-4ef8b811ab84">
      <Text>Deena lands four longnecks on a table mid-story and keeps moving.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="165bf8fe-73ae-47a5-8bbb-34dbcff1e691">
      <Text>JUNE drops a basket at a table, then steps up onto the bandstand still in her apron and unclips it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="26d60ae8-aa6d-4b6d-afdb-ee250e78d995">
      <Text>DEENA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="dfffbb42-7619-42e6-b9a7-b51cf4aa0f99">
      <Text>(as she goes by)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a99f64c8-25e4-414e-83a2-d4c54a80f315">
      <Text>One of these days you’re gonna have to pick. Tray or that guitar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e9fec5d7-f04d-4092-a0ef-2703af1883cb">
      <Text>JUNE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8e11d5b8-5b18-413c-82eb-98e6b78dcfb9">
      <Text>I’m picking. I just need about four more months of tips.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d847ed09-4c70-44cd-8648-daa09056ec42">
      <Text>DEENA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9c0314e6-4965-42bd-b451-8c68dbbf8913">
      <Text>Four months. Listen to her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="da76b58d-f18a-44bf-8075-2ed149617150">
      <Text>At a corner table, RAY BEASLEY, 70s, lean in a pressed shirt, holds his hat on one knee while ONDINE, 70s, in a floral dress, talks with both hands and straightens his collar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24bb7d6f-82a2-4598-8bad-3573c7a157a2">
      <Text>At the bar, a bottled Coke sweats before an empty stool. LACEY STROUD, 17, slight, bright red lipstick and a church dress taken in at the waist, slips in behind a birthday crowd and claims it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2eed59d9-4dcd-490d-a42e-4622cd8ad256">
      <Text>HOYT enters in a clean button-down, empty-handed. Pete’s handshake holds an extra beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2a0fb6af-6c0f-486d-9f3c-d8de7c9ebc19">
      <Text>Passing a rocking table, Hoyt crouches and folds a coaster beneath one leg. As he rises, Ondine catches him by the arm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ab6e573-0435-4e54-b3fb-5b9e21ffb867">
      <Text>ONDINE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d01c1c83-2035-4fc1-bbce-b65ba1903e32">
      <Text>Merle ought to be ashamed. Nine years, Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e12310c6-1872-4a17-a684-5f449ccd4ab0">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="138f66c9-f1b7-41c7-a378-90bc2b07ff5c">
      <Text>Ain’t my place anymore.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0026b01b-8263-4932-b62f-408ee3ad6bff">
      <Text>ONDINE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="145d1dd3-af39-4461-9660-9ba4bdd78d43">
      <Text>It ain’t right, Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c35089cf-936b-42be-a4a0-90fe4429ba70">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cda972d3-290c-48ff-95f5-11a448a1f33e">
      <Text>I came for June.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cc2f1e6a-1dd8-443a-81db-146d38c1e9dc">
      <Text>She lets him go. At the end of the bar, Deena sets a beer in front of him without being asked. The band finishes tuning. The room quiets.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a9929b2b-49d0-43fc-b598-253d8b8da296">
      <Text>JUNE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="a1ac23bb-f441-4482-a7db-dada3d929b16">
      <Text>(at the mic)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cc36ea2d-daf6-4eda-a838-d76de974ef1f">
      <Text>All right, all right. This one’s for Ray and Ondine, thirty-one years married, and that man still won’t dance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a653f84c-e9be-4368-a8e3-c44a7337eb63">
      <Text>RAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="3db85c6a-01af-42ff-bf27-c740405672e1">
      <Text>(from his table)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1a5dbe2-973a-4d81-a392-d8473c33518f">
      <Text>Can’t. Not won’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="507678bb-8b11-4151-8c76-cf50c953c20a">
      <Text>People at the tables laugh. The band begins a slow number. Ondine looks at Ray. Ray holds his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ba78d2e9-f627-4b2b-af2b-045c8a61c7f7">
      <Text>At the door, Pete looks across the packed floor. People are still coming.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a717ecef-d02b-479b-a5a5-b751ba49ce0a">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="62bb84c6-2fea-4ed5-8af0-708b3cf263c7">
      <Text>(half to himself)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f3efe34d-40e7-4523-854a-0b4e3b403314">
      <Text>Ain’t even payday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d722f5a8-f06f-4597-b850-43d572b9eabe">
      <Text>Nobody answers. The floor fills.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4a21957a-6318-4d51-9d97-afbc81282022">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="33" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="db09c48b-8fc8-4fd7-a3e6-40f0110e00c5"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="62a12e5c-b980-4dca-8d79-1b6dd873ab0a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. LAKE CABIN - DOCK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f820ef4d-6cd6-4ca3-b45a-568e2a3051ea">
      <Text>A lantern on the dock. Still water. Crickets.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="56511258-54c4-44e1-a9fb-9a45df3f59d8">
      <Text>Rucker and Donna sit in folding chairs with their lines out. A thermos between them. Her bare feet rest on the cooler.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="172d6275-08f6-45ea-a0ed-654c63a12aab">
      <Text>For a while, only the water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1501ad91-09fc-4f4e-8d25-000c4311c0cf">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0247a091-3412-4b12-b867-24e6578ff1cd">
      <Text>First time you brought me here, you talked the whole way up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7069fafd-86af-45f0-9951-4d4204297d88">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ed8437e2-dc1e-43fb-8741-237057dd5dd9">
      <Text>Road was washed out at Hensley Creek.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="98631ea1-8f8d-4852-91e1-9f8bc5228743">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5b0bbc80-e57b-4109-a5f2-f5582d1e6b81">
      <Text>See.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="081875f1-4073-4a5b-a71a-3b0104cc71fc">
      <Text>He looks at her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0484d66d-2521-4ac0-b77b-b16eda653d1a">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e886b4d4-e225-4bb9-953e-388a22580063">
      <Text>Every bridge. Every ditch. Where the volunteer stations were. Which road the county never graded right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7c56abdf-a324-4ba4-ba4f-1c5b9e8981bd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43d53c7f-5026-43bd-a294-941a122e5e72">
      <Text>It still ain’t graded right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff3efdd1-5842-4c3c-80c3-73a403ea4503">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bbb08f39-1ac7-44a3-84fb-7599f1c20415">
      <Text>I thought you were showing me the country.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3300e898-171b-4e90-96fb-6caeffb9a552">
      <Text>Rucker watches his float.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="154f1835-1c87-4080-9bc6-d5dd7336415d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="924c9479-d9e3-47fd-88ad-6f5bf4f1b022">
      <Text>I was nervous.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="50ccb2d6-8997-4cfd-846e-30ee179c2dc8">
      <Text>Donna turns toward him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="52d159ac-8a02-4383-a5c1-5f038ac541da">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b2ebfaac-490d-4aaa-a073-586a0eb436cb">
      <Text>You never told me that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6ffe90a0-4851-4de7-a5fa-27074540a714">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83cbad4a-02eb-436c-a338-87b9a0c4942e">
      <Text>You knew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15b2eb4a-4bb1-4ba4-a523-d34bb591442f">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5e2dcdd7-bd9e-4632-bd82-823f126fa71c">
      <Text>I knew something. I didn’t know whether you meant to marry me or inspect the road.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b598dfa1-2dd0-43cb-a7a2-3adc264c5334">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c9d5c90f-c74c-4ad2-b3be-d1892d459885">
      <Text>Both worked out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1109eeb1-f2b4-453d-af90-09b3dc045c38">
      <Text>Donna pours coffee into the thermos cup and hands it to him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cd9e2405-6890-451d-9e19-790dd994833e">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="62345780-4579-4905-902d-32572722436f">
      <Text>Twenty years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ed7349f-eec1-472e-a599-21ff1be09c99">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af944e2b-59ef-4f91-aa16-0afdbf690ac9">
      <Text>Twenty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="434b0b9b-cffa-4110-9d0e-ed6633934383">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a6c0112f-13f6-41c5-9378-a3afc80bf4fd">
      <Text>Still nervous?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="00f51cbc-8d6b-4403-ba11-84df296eff14">
      <Text>Rucker takes the cup.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="427e405b-27c3-4acb-8b55-d0fdcaf8c57a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aaff6dea-6681-46d5-8f6c-d830a8a6d40d">
      <Text>Not about you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="382a8e2a-6cae-42ca-afbe-192f2054c74d">
      <Text>Donna settles back in her chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a04a29a8-8682-45ee-8575-2cb58b5fe6f4">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="34" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LAKE DEPUTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5f998c14-4fcc-4655-859c-5e9fc29ae769"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d19b0c9f-2648-4ca0-ae46-a2ec4b8a9d95"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>UP AT THE CABIN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a840df89-37a4-41ff-809a-2bf6a8affe3a">
      <Text>The truck sits dark. Inside, a phone BUZZES in the glovebox, light flashing twice through the seam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b86de0d5-b3f6-46d2-b234-03e8c30004ce">
      <Text>Far up the winding lake road, headlights move between the trees and vanish.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="81d8aab6-6d95-4419-83d0-f6aa52e36105">
      <Text>The phone BUZZES again. The headlights reappear, closer now, sweeping the trees as tires crunch over gravel.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7dddbda9-9b26-4d06-ae1d-89f34dbd8ced">
      <Text>A county cruiser noses down the road and stops above the cabin.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="c25c0c96-76cb-494b-baf8-335165ff865b">
      <Text>BACK ON THE DOCK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ae4ce9af-bff8-4fd7-ac1e-d88926d6ece9">
      <Text>Rucker is already standing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="833e76fc-6a42-4fbe-ba88-7b4e766bf7ea">
      <Text>A DEPUTY comes only as far as the top of the dock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b9e4f753-3048-455a-92f0-d5c04d063594">
      <Text>LAKE DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c0f77d85-da05-400b-b210-0c605b227805">
      <Text>Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b2032aae-05d6-45a6-8e0d-bdcbd1c5d25a">
      <Text>He takes off his hat and holds it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="19f86e19-786a-4486-9604-57ca5115aefb">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="839d2c5b-040a-4fac-9d13-cb4a672fc864">
      <Text>Where.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5c977152-eb98-4d61-ad9f-23ac513cebc7">
      <Text>LAKE DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1793fc49-c0be-4635-ba56-3dbd2272b87c">
      <Text>Magnolia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c5c15dd-389f-4f16-b879-b4768d6d1814">
      <Text>Rucker picks up his hat from the chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f8285f65-a8da-4cd5-9edc-98c05ac76355">
      <Text>Behind him, Donna extinguishes the lantern and folds the chairs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8519caca-71ba-4459-989b-f0b2ec073d37">
      <Text>The cruiser heads back up the lake road. Rucker’s truck follows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="381cce25-9361-4978-bb17-f7a4cb855a49">
      <Text>The fishing rods remain on the dock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4370ae8b-adb9-49f9-acd6-23e6bfb5e4c7">
      <Text>Two lines still in the water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="044f00de-a305-41b2-b81c-ac94cf195fb6">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="35" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e4f09b3c-52e3-4cc4-a6c8-21146d45d1cd"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="03fd18f3-5f56-47db-9f10-0986720c2897"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ad75ffca-5f31-48e5-90ac-317d80136f26"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. RUCKER’S TRUCK - NIGHT (MOVING)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="395a5cc2-2b79-4eaf-8b88-3ed0a6a52faf">
      <Text>Two-lane blacktop at speed. Over the trees ahead, a glow spreads across the sky.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c0599bf8-4632-479f-bb5b-a35935027294">
      <Text>Donna sits beside Rucker with his jacket over her shoulders. Neither speaks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="80b9ced4-87d7-4650-ae56-151404cceec7">
      <Text>The phone rings against the dash. Rucker answers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1b57ddcd-cc8e-4273-a308-baf21c39c3b7">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e7e0b40a-9bed-4ef3-9794-ae226b2341e7">
      <Text>Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="541949c3-c01e-4a0c-b6f7-0b5c43f5519a">
      <Text>The voice is COE, the State Fire Marshal in Montgomery.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fbe68ad5-f60f-4d91-87a6-23484faa92d4">
      <Text>COE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a84b90d9-c94f-4770-8d99-0ec2b15d5e16">
      <Text>Where are you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f14939d7-6576-4fcb-82ea-1f4a71307675">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e838b709-91b3-4387-b3e5-17d03de2f8a0">
      <Text>Fifteen out. What are you hearing?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cf3badbe-4d2f-4fee-ba96-27767ca7298d">
      <Text>COE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7909830f-3541-48ae-aedf-d9ba9b6d0fd1">
      <Text>Juke joint called the Magnolia, west of town. Friday night — better than a hundred inside when it lit. They’re still carrying people out the front, and command just went defensive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b2b2d913-f7f9-46ef-9a7a-c519d44e72d2">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d6b88973-17bc-4478-bbe7-cd398a1b5665">
      <Text>Who all’s working it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec9e7c7e-c504-470f-87e6-641d9b12099c">
      <Text>COE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6160c176-af09-4d3d-a571-a77b8948b34a">
      <Text>FBI’s sending a team to rule out terrorism. </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">ATF</Text>
      <Text> has a fire investigator rolling from Atlanta — Vic Saenz. Origin and cause stay with you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5ff59242-1a77-40e8-8547-0b91847917b1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="857e11f9-762e-4ac3-a33d-7b65fc20947a">
      <Text>All right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a6d8f85e-2c65-4039-9cdb-f014aae32843">
      <Text>COE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7b44cf77-cb51-4908-8ada-e2c4fa7e318d">
      <Text>Call me when you’ve stood in it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9419cb88-a7a4-4aa4-9e9d-aba7e3b2342e">
      <Text>The line goes dead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ba06efbd-f476-4d64-ac3a-0a6fd16e0903">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1de36324-0a45-4cf3-a366-d0d93f613542">
      <Text>Ty needs the truck at seven. They’re fitting the varsity boys at the school.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="78d3cbc0-10aa-4cc9-b7a8-d078a30a5b61">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0ed16e73-bcee-4098-949f-0b863c580322">
      <Text>Not now, Donna.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3955b0e7-af0d-473f-8813-642dc13be647">
      <Text>She looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6e07c190-5847-44dd-a577-ad231df3ca74">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fdd1c4de-93ee-475b-a759-680adaee4a8f">
      <Text>I didn’t ask you anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1381f71c-8189-439d-98e5-b18174aaed2f">
      <Text>Rucker keeps his eyes on the road.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8c553013-bba2-4f9c-a969-0c579cecdf6c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f19f5429-1dee-428c-8faa-6e18ca2c3fc2">
      <Text>No. You didn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b9635ab8-8c9f-4b39-9ccb-d616f707d92c">
      <Text>A moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6c4873fc-7cec-4aa0-9759-1860d8dca79c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="050f4d32-e009-44cf-a17d-a0bf613aa67b">
      <Text>I’m sorry.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="18ac292c-3b80-47fd-978d-4e5adfc72d40">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e464e527-ba55-4e6f-ab8b-a2d38f505381">
      <Text>I know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9385fb6f-b341-45f7-907e-be3d51d2d1ab">
      <Text>The road bends. Rucker takes the curve.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="de939a4f-5637-4d5c-9113-0e9259423364">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9832b1bf-f77c-4b98-b9d5-8722f2a4c8c0">
      <Text>I’ll take the truck home from the roadblock. I’ll see that your Tahoe gets out there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5c75bc18-c8f6-473a-9b18-f49a5b1e32cd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="170e040c-ccc6-406e-babb-41d65c76eca7">
      <Text>Don’t worry about the Tahoe. I’ll send somebody for it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="db00fe84-5a1a-4887-b6aa-505259d0de0a">
      <Text>His hat slides across the seat between them. Donna catches it before it reaches the floor and holds it in her lap.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Scene Heading" id="fb3bcfd4-aaf2-4131-aa9d-a8f7fc3133e8">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="36" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="INCIDENT COMMANDER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="520e96d7-72a3-4b84-b16d-8a4be370ea42"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cfb82be5-07fa-4730-b06b-3d0bbff9c3b4">
      <Text>Flames break through the rear section of the roof. The high windows glow orange. Smoke pushes from the eaves and rolls across the parking lot.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d6407196-aea0-474e-b6f9-193fa055ae64">
      <Text>Fire apparatus fill the lot and line both sides of the road—Hale River companies and mutual-aid crews from across the county. Aerial ladders extend above the building. Large supply lines cross the road.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8a72a138-3eeb-47cf-8a32-c2d471514360">
      <Text>At the front doors, a hose crew crawls backward outside, heads down. Steam pours through the doorway around them. Their officer signals the next crew to stay back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="79ecbcd2-8aed-439b-b8f4-a63e1bb22024">
      <Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="7db758dd-a45a-4d81-9c1c-21b13359166f">
      <Text>(radio)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7e60e621-58c1-4359-9e5f-ae177df42c1e">
      <Text>Command to all units — defensive operations. Surround and drown.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ace2c7f5-0859-4a45-87dc-2342a2d0f9d2">
      <Text>MASTER STREAMS arc onto the roof from three sides as handlines move toward the exposures.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="193393e0-29f3-42fc-ba05-f9c0678052c8">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="37" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>THE FRONT LOT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6d8010f4-6d06-47ad-bbd2-85c943f59ee4">
      <Text>Survivors line the curb, barefoot and soot-streaked beneath blankets. A deputy moves among them with a clipboard, taking names.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5998c85f-667e-4ea4-a1b6-da2910f975a0">
      <Text>Several feet apart, LACEY stands barefoot in an oversized jacket, watching the front doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e4dd4400-9529-4710-b77b-e996b1d57b9e">
      <Text>No one comes out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="89df723a-43c8-4106-9bb6-148d60c34071">
      <Text>Two firefighters drop beneath the smoke and advance through the doorway on a charged line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3cfb62fc-5c42-4f64-82a4-8e36fe2e60f8">
      <Text>COBB runs around the corner in his nightclothes, but a firefighter intercepts him and turns him toward the road. Behind them, the severed chain lies across the threshold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="95cf4688-24db-48a1-964e-066b4adf653a">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="37" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FRONT-LOT DEPUTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="15c0bd16-9e83-43dc-b9fa-0d5a111b46b9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9fb259de-abe0-4365-9233-582b7b6e81e3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>AT THE TAPE —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eee6361f-b262-49bd-9c52-3e5e006b5d46">
      <Text>Several hundred residents watch, including the woman from the VFW meeting who asked about her children. No phones are raised.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a9bf6ba4-bb93-40c3-9bad-b99b5819ca78">
      <Text>Inside the tape, MERCER photographs the crowd. Approaching headlights make him lower the camera.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6632f34b-bb4d-4cea-a55e-6dd1e0114df1">
      <Text>Down the mill road, beyond the last engine, a pickup sits dark on the shoulder, a red gas can beside its tank.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="89dfcdc6-2edd-4a59-a57b-42751b0b128d">
      <Text>RUCKERâ</Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft">€™</Text>
      <Text>S TRUCK clears the roadblock and stops near the tape. Rucker gets out, walks to the line and studies the building from roof to foundation.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b36d2248-b789-47e3-a12b-bce8d47b5e4f">
      <Text>He does not move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="24abdb7e-8f83-44b9-a791-433b07cda269">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="06488065-c20d-45fb-ab97-f0aa32952274">
      <Text>(to a deputy, quiet)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="78fd3498-c7d8-4271-b156-f860ed50422d">
      <Text>Who’s out?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4bc5b2a0-3991-47aa-8b62-f05df37ac1c5">
      <Text>FRONT-LOT DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="03f6c34c-db56-491d-bea2-3bfafa954eb9">
      <Text>Working on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="881649d7-7136-41ce-8d3e-ff47b306ac3b">
      <Text>Mercer raises the camera to the crowd.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a6e97afb-8171-4e34-ba2d-879acaa59358">
      <Text>At the edge of his frame, AMOS HOYT stands alone in a hospital scrub top, fresh white bandages around both palms, his hands held away from his body. He watches flames vent through the Magnolia’s rear roof.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4e7eb577-f354-4578-975c-0d28b79b1187">
      <SceneProperties Length="1/8" Page="38" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>CLICK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="b240509f-fbef-409d-9e1f-fbde774a0669">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="38" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7c0ec2ab-413e-42c6-9ade-c45abb22d78b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - BEFORE DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8a35847-fe29-4d02-b797-02829df31987">
      <Text>Black runoff steams across the lot. The master streams are silent.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="adfc42fb-3d93-413a-8df8-2ef02562ee87">
      <Text>The roof has collapsed into the burned shell. The rear door hangs open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d65a1c69-1862-48b1-9b51-a20738afc385">
      <Text>Firefighters slump on apparatus bumpers. A COUNTY CHAPLAIN sedan waits near the command post. Behind the tape, the crowd remains.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cb0e43f2-29b0-4412-b117-43b7c019ef92">
      <Text>SLOAN approaches Rucker, soot to his elbows. He steps close and lowers his voice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d7f22fd2-3ba1-40bd-8b31-e7a95d5ea616">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ff560f62-038c-4754-bc63-d7af1dfc9fb4">
      <Text>Nineteen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1f05dcdd-9af5-4dc4-96e2-815157637c54">
      <Text>Rucker stands still.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f371e6b0-7f0c-42e4-9c9e-408d98c7d180">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="54e477b2-0296-4e1e-8c57-9dd53332dc71">
      <Text>Pete was at the bottom of the pile. Facing the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6f643f52-9b55-4545-8180-11f5c496e025">
      <Text>Sloan goes back to work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="fe244a1b-11ab-4516-ac0e-9291e038ded0">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="38" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FBI AGENT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0c44108b-0462-41a8-90eb-20a3c2bc5baf"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="631f6d54-a5f2-4a0b-b03e-479539b70464"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6e37860b-e593-4532-ba40-5fd25af839a8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - LOT - FIRST LIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fd8606b0-41da-4be7-b57c-8ebccd088a97">
      <Text>Positive-pressure fans run at the front doors. Coroner investigators wait beside their van while a deputy logs the tape. VIC SAENZ, 40s, </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">ATF</Text>
      <Text> fire investigator, arranges evidence bags and tools beside a road-grimed government SUV.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f126a2a5-58be-4ccb-b430-f77d6820e61b">
      <Text>Rucker walks over from the Tahoe in coveralls and rubber boots, a camera hanging from his neck and a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Maglite</Text>
      <Text> in one hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="51fd2ef6-2c65-41c6-a6dd-02be4ad9a47a">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4e3bf5b9-4587-4e40-809a-6c0dd589c085">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker. Vic Saenz.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="afec929b-a818-4de2-9dcc-d3e149f569d8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="62255cdd-45a9-4606-b38d-b6068696939e">
      <Text>Coe said Atlanta.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f57440cc-2992-4def-bec7-5639556106a9">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="68dfa2da-816a-4d5c-966a-eb4e40f0aac2">
      <Text>Four and a half hours without stopping. My team’s behind me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4af441ab-80b1-4abd-99a7-949155729b23">
      <Text>A second man steps from behind the government SUV: an FBI AGENT, 30s, gym-built, in a windbreaker, slacks and street shoes. He carries no protective gear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6d0534ae-bb10-4d20-95b1-5dfb9d24b693">
      <Text>FBI AGENT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c5ec8975-40fa-4fce-bb1c-c6d91ff6c984">
      <Text>Marshal. Bureau’s here to say it wasn’t political. Give me a day, I’ll say it and go home.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cd3d5306-0af6-4782-bba2-004a377e3231">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a4387de5-38e1-4a2f-abd4-9ad3f5373d0f">
      <Text>You’ll get no argument from me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c7ebb9f1-3fa7-495a-9859-a3ecc0455997">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0112fa35-3c37-488f-b2f9-95f2203899e1">
      <Text>What do we have?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4746eace-4c60-4048-9e03-b7d2dbaa3dea">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b5e60153-1d47-462d-8ad6-dfbf6a126e4f">
      <Text>Occupancy card says one-forty. Friday night, and the lot was full past the road. Knockdown about four a.m. Nobody inside since.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="10d9c810-961b-48f4-80ea-35bfacac1564">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a1e559f6-02ad-47c3-8345-c0bfdc442cb3">
      <Text>You?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6ec2f35d-380c-4f5c-be41-e78c21f8329f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c05aa92-e941-4264-a11c-628340118590">
      <Text>Not yet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e22ce683-cffb-41ea-9666-4fa09a91c45a">
      <Text>Saenz closes the scene kit. Leaves it on the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c9c73cf9-2d1b-408d-a643-660798db04a9">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4c2ab565-b931-4f59-994c-769599df0289">
      <Text>Then the kit can sit until you’ve walked it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="14aa19a6-1315-4cdf-8248-d457192880de">
      <Text>Rucker looks at the FBI agent’s street shoes. He opens the back of the Tahoe and takes out a spare helmet and a pair of rubber boots. Holds them out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f020dd73-bafb-4cd1-bd6c-ac28d7c0f399">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dc73eebc-eeec-40c9-b7c3-fb225aef50c1">
      <Text>You’ll need these.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c435673-9d4e-4416-afed-42aa12ba568b">
      <Text>Rucker turns to the deputy at the entrance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="28b082be-6faf-48f1-abcc-0982d2863e5c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e23623b9-6f0c-4d9c-a915-2fab95c86376">
      <Text>Kill the fans. Lock the building down. Nobody goes in without our say. Nothing comes out without a tag.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cac63afd-16de-49d3-b999-f7bf330dd3be">
      <Text>The deputy signals toward the generator. The FBI agent pulls on his boots and helmet, then follows Rucker and Saenz inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="fc491162-1fe5-4cf3-8e48-924e96e2c7bf">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="40" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6700726a-43c5-42b2-913b-ff3914c2328a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a711fb53-2827-4936-ab56-d703f0601349"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="43c62dc7-2896-4bbe-83f1-f2c660230d7a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA LOUNGE - FIRST LIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8ef7f87f-880f-424b-850d-aa511ce129be">
      <Text>The fan noise recedes behind them. In the quiet, water drips.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7500ca91-1967-44b1-bde9-7e4cff732032">
      <Text>A sharp soot line marks the wet room — high near the entrance, descending toward the rear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7fffb765-548d-4bcf-aa7e-fdbbc5d00bf3">
      <Text>Three feet inside, within the parking-lot light: PEOPLE lie together, all facing the doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="94a87a9b-a4fe-4398-b025-62a8d3061d6c">
      <Text>Rucker stops and removes his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9208931-27fa-4b86-90a4-13fc9dc24ce5">
      <Text>He goes around them. Not through.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7ec69e7c-4138-49e5-8edb-6b8411b40f60">
      <Text>His </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Maglite</Text>
      <Text> crosses the front lounge: bottles still ranked behind the bar beneath Christmas lights; a drum kit and guitar on the bandstand; tables shoved aside, chairs stacked on top. A purse hangs from one. Half-full longnecks remain on another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="91f36917-506c-45b8-9200-e3954d7fc42a">
      <Text>Below the soot line, the room is intact.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f07c2038-f559-4f11-a80c-3372660d3b6b">
      <Text>Rucker photographs from front to rear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c42b57d8-1f16-435e-859e-5e15331d603c">
      <Text>Near the kitchen, blistered varnish gives way to burned furniture and exposed joists. The soot line falls to waist height.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13360f95-96d9-405e-aea8-0d21435e5fb5">
      <Text>The kitchen, walk-in and storeroom open from the rear hall, the roof gone above them. At the storeroom threshold, Rucker stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a3dea3bf-ef05-4719-b103-56faf7a1c4dd">
      <Text>Heat shimmers over blackened studs and debris as he sweeps his light corner to corner without entering.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="24733086-fe96-4b62-81d6-1c2ed52ef770">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6fa0f740-682c-4aaa-9414-f089c038aed0">
      <Text>Still working?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89ce3fd9-6ba2-4948-b8a7-6b3ee77711a1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="38615cc7-9fca-4855-9a48-e0d2020dc7f9">
      <Text>It’ll be hot for a while. Nobody in there till it’s cold and I’m in it first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4518ba20-8288-4aa3-88d7-6917c50c5fd0">
      <Text>Rucker continues past the walk-in cooler. A mop sink and empty crates line one wall. No EXIT sign marks the hall or rear door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0a5d87f7-5ac6-4f05-b815-18ef5a95782d">
      <Text>The door stands open. Several victims lie together near it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="63a4571f-b1c4-4242-8930-5f60327be7ef">
      <Text>Beneath the panic bar, the severed chain remains where the fire crew left it, the padlock still locked through two links.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c2d6f0d-a8df-49c3-991c-c3765f23c550">
      <Text>Rucker crouches and photographs it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="024d2985-12b0-4323-b12a-edfa5c9f9166">
      <Text>He retraces the rear hall and front lounge, the fan growing louder as he nears the entrance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dba9c4e7-c5a7-4c21-969a-2f67edfd01dd">
      <Text>MERCER waits at the front doors with the camera bag. Behind him, coroner’s investigators unload two folded stretchers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="31cd129d-abe0-58b8-bde4-b0f97bd5e500">
      <Text>Rucker looks from the stretchers to Mercer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4acf1c2f-08f5-4ea3-b760-54a8cc6f582f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3fc07612-9104-4f64-903f-939b7d855751">
      <Text>Whole room as it sits. Wide, close, front doors to back hall. Nothing moves first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a4f6ed77-503e-49a2-837e-ab0c924fb42a">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f1f2f57a-253c-411a-b00b-b23a0eb2374c">
      <Text>Yes sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e54421bd-1ab4-41ea-8e1d-c1994e72d4e9">
      <Text>Mercer shoulders the camera bag and starts inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0a719fef-bbd4-494d-9907-425a68f7f3af">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="807733fd-0074-4bbc-b8cc-79fc07002c1f">
      <Text>Danny.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b3c1a102-1364-4baf-b2bf-dd43946ce53d">
      <Text>Mercer stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="649365ed-e403-4bac-b6be-9781a3b5d70e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="affec714-e9e4-4489-8d02-656601a6bd22">
      <Text>Chain and padlock where they are. Separate signed bags.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="41fb98cd-abc4-4770-afe4-64c830c362d8">
      <Text>Mercer nods and enters.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f1940012-3f7e-4cb5-bff1-1ef77305b307">
      <Text>The coroner’s investigators reach the doors with the stretchers. They wait outside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="29802e39-cfb8-4c4f-ab8b-2ec8bdc25233">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="41" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FBI AGENT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="c62424e2-e36a-4b69-afcb-44095133fbf5"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LANIER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="be756a26-7be4-4796-b380-80fdf3c63fd4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MOSS">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bf53d479-f129-4e0a-9e01-246d00c4ea26"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ODOM">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="aeb81dcb-f3ed-4b1e-a09a-bf3769ce81d4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PARDUE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="febdd9e3-2496-421d-bb47-d5ab47c895dd"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="3e36aea7-347c-4172-b659-d2054d3958a1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="81721593-586f-402e-a35b-585b51b78b20"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="890ddce8-8560-4f6d-8952-07212c4f9344"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - COMMAND POST - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="190c9e6e-092f-43d5-85f7-6903cb489dfe">
      <Text>Sunrise. The sheriff’s mobile-unit awning. A county map spread on the hood of a cruiser, corners weighted with radios. Men stand around it — no chairs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ed8cadef-7cf1-4e90-8116-6859017b58bd">
      <Text>RUCKER, SAENZ, the FBI AGENT, SLOAN, MOSS and </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PARDUE</Text>
      <Text>. SHERIFF LANIER, 60s, silver crew cut, a belly held in by a gun belt. ODOM, 40s, the sheriff’s investigator — rangy, sun-creased, a notebook already open. Behind them, firefighters roll hose. The coroner’s van idles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bce30da9-d4e9-42f6-ab64-67243374c833">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PARDUE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="48c363f9-0a7f-4f11-92ad-c60fcc338c86">
      <Text>People at that tape have already decided it’s the same man.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a7f3c3f7-0027-4413-9545-d8cd42abb757">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0b41fb11-9948-4a22-80d3-05307248c601">
      <Text>The others were three in the morning, back wall, outside. This one changed the hour, the building, the way in and the origin.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="20a4fa38-914f-4108-b31a-93493050c26e">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">PARDUE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="10833f50-f2da-47e8-9bac-152a06e3ec5e">
      <Text>So he got brave.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="deb93580-7b9e-459b-9c93-5214ff698b5c">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2c68d352-a2dc-4f12-8306-ede7ee3bd29a">
      <Text>Or it isn’t his.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ea349c79-408d-4773-9627-9a4e67da4dd7">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af963756-1370-4dca-8ab0-ad96f925d8f3">
      <Text>Until the room tells me different, both stay open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f82c30dc-2c17-41f4-a469-8c343b1928e8">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="79bd09e5-8405-44ec-930c-330a0af949ea">
      <Text>Cobb’s carrying insurance and a renovation he’s half through paying for.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="278d11dd-a46e-4042-a52d-d1d6b58e7522">
      <Text>LANIER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1dd68aa-c440-4ebf-b587-372e397cf125">
      <Text>Merle Cobb’s been here sixty years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1c1de8f9-eccf-4f67-819b-f1872f7ed899">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="29106da0-9d62-40e7-8a13-8b384e89befc">
      <Text>So has everybody I ever arrested.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="26b2eadf-248a-4038-b330-e1d789e1b450">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e70429eb-5f7e-4238-83a3-93bce71b32d2">
      <Text>Paper it. Building value, debt, who gains. Keep the theory out of my ear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5f8c7c3b-b48e-4fc8-987c-0a8fc61238fe">
      <Text>Rucker plants a finger on the map — the rear of the building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="58e4bedb-3229-47d1-8e5d-e7b9331efd99">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7161dcb1-8bf6-4c8a-9c19-2de723ce172c">
      <Text>Rear exit was chained from inside. Who put it on. When. Who carried keys. Two sources on every answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cf930c6c-7264-4b5d-a6be-237bc89c7b3d">
      <Text>Odom’s pen stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c722cfb5-d367-4c59-9517-36e5077763f8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5ecd6d4d-a151-4b99-9346-b7633ca859f8">
      <Text>Everybody inside: where were you standing, where did you try to go, what stopped you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3b28d524-8b2b-4cff-95c8-65942074a79c">
      <Text>A DEPUTY leans close to Lanier and speaks quietly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="829f1842-65da-42f0-ae08-05dd5ca08316">
      <Text>LANIER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c28bb02f-7e46-4e5e-921c-e7b8684c91cf">
      <Text>They’re ready to start bringing them out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="12ba5299-4261-4e98-b3f4-46e81bc7ad37">
      <Text>Radios come off the map. The corners curl up. The men move toward the building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="85c15c7a-2596-4e63-8bf8-e94f22136286">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="43" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="637e3f23-68eb-48f1-80a4-8c635cf2eccf">
      <Text>Behind the tape, the county gathers in church clothes and work clothes, more arriving on foot along the shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="72228a49-c6bc-4a1a-a95e-d3dbc72e89d8">
      <Text>Hearses and funeral-home vans from three counties line the road, doors open. The coroner’s van waits nearest the building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="06bb759e-5d74-4c9b-9702-d7ae16a2cc36">
      <Text>The fans are silent.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="be69d2da-5c7f-4d8a-b1ee-1f2907cc05b2">
      <Text>The first stretcher emerges through the front doors — a white sheet, strapped. Nothing but boots on wet grit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9a870fcf-6ef9-42a9-a76e-ccaeda44bab5">
      <Text>Hats come off along the tape line. The stretcher enters the coroner’s van. Its doors close softly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5dbcf615-b19a-4bc3-819d-fea1e2f9fd8b">
      <Text>A second comes out. Then a third.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="aa4ebedd-ab6c-4387-98f7-8579c4073b3e">
      <Text>At the tape, a woman searches the surrounding faces - </Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft"> </Text>
      <Text>who is here, who isn’t - </Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft"> </Text>
      <Text>her lips moving as she counts.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="45d93ea7-a580-4836-b3e4-fbc0e2334b88">
      <Text>Somewhere down the line, the count breaks somebody.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="17674050-4dc8-4d61-a01a-901db51d0a32">
      <Text>It travels.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="606a55ef-113e-4758-acb0-71e28b7aef22">
      <Text>Rucker stands apart, hat in hand, watching the doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dc21b9b3-0f4f-495b-8cad-d707e9af946e">
      <Text>The stretchers keep coming.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="13a1cce0-a247-4605-b8a7-de88fd48b6a9">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="43" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="FIRE WATCH LIEUTENANT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f11282be-c55a-477f-b3a4-d4eebcd0fcba"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LANIER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2b285edd-45b2-4015-8560-803c493a81a6"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ffb48bc7-1a64-4ce1-9ea1-5f6493e2ffda"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="08712efe-3605-46f7-a8cb-41f3bbefdeb1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BURNED SHELL - STOREROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="00aab3d9-b5fa-4231-84ae-048e46c1ae55">
      <Text>The shell still smokes in places. A FIRE WATCH CREW works a reopened void along the far wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c4eebd22-127a-44e2-9d9a-e3cdcfb3dbf8">
      <Text>A FIRE WATCH LIEUTENANT leads Rucker through the marked debris lanes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6aedb946-f312-418d-9be9-7da5b6441f1c">
      <Text>FIRE WATCH LIEUTENANT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b49ec462-79c5-4a24-ab11-8d6a609d228a">
      <Text>Storeroom’s released. Floor’s soft in front of it. Nothing moved since recovery.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="202816c0-53a7-4354-a602-a66cfec019f3">
      <Text>Rucker checks the debris lane and nods to him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b664d4ed-a871-43df-a01b-8a62f17320f0">
      <Text>SAENZ has a grid marked outside the storeroom. MERCER waits with the camera.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c041b3b2-e555-4852-b463-9123bf8128ec">
      <Text>The room is open to the sky. Black shelving. What remains of the louvered door hangs from its hinges.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f135f8e5-4678-42bd-be31-8086a0e086b5">
      <Text>Rucker works the walls with his light, then the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c7bf8d9f-51b8-4c71-9f70-2a0ac8b577b2">
      <Text>At the far corner, the renovation crew’s rolled FOAM STOCK has burned down into itself. Damage decreases away from it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a121c5a5-3db4-47c9-a823-e1220de6f865">
      <Text>Rucker runs his light up the corner studs, then out along the shelving, tracking the char as it shallows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cc474e55-cacb-4d34-bd7c-79a7ee42eb47">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="d131a035-55bd-40cb-acfb-3c403504ae83">
      <Text>(to Mercer)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="97283272-6cad-4a7b-ab45-13304327d861">
      <Text>Fire eats longest where it starts. Look at the char — deep in this corner, shallower every foot away. Shoot the gradient, corner out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="27843f56-6185-4a52-b2a5-1bb57b738b46">
      <Text>He crouches at the burned-down rolls.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="00b1936b-e0b5-48af-82ca-b4740291a401">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="71ab2162-0a71-4faa-aece-c05c4d06e80f">
      <Text>Foam burned into itself, not across. It sat in its own fire longer than anything else in the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="43c73c54-2a66-4a48-95d3-67d20b72bbf2">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c89a1717-029a-445e-9b60-2c9b849d9260">
      <Text>Area, not a point?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="41434914-1067-4b63-bbf1-5496888d6eef">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1ba76809-9326-4073-be64-3921bfcfe456">
      <Text>The corner. I won’t call it tighter than the damage does.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c5e5a56-89b5-4251-8a8d-41559966c517">
      <Text>Mercer photographs. Rucker traces the conduit to the outlet and panel while Saenz marks samples at the corner and clean side.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d27bf31b-75a1-4b59-9420-a37c8135513c">
      <Text>Mercer’s camera finds the foam, shelving, high west window and slumped glass beneath it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="82da8db4-f6e3-472a-a9fc-a35705fead6d">
      <Text>LANIER appears in the doorway.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="10e28a88-a9ca-4aaf-94b0-e4889e1f336b">
      <Text>LANIER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0794d3e9-a833-472a-ac37-bfe79d9794cd">
      <Text>State wants a cause.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4097e4ac-6800-4e17-b9ee-7998ea51254a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="341c3767-cf3d-4682-b2dd-f56aece2a15a">
      <Text>They don’t have one. Area’s this corner. Foam’s the first fuel. No competent ignition source yet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="499fd54c-6fc1-4fda-9121-0047d7c59000">
      <Text>Saenz crouches at the foam and puts his own light through it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="01232a33-ea34-44ba-bb7a-e70c15430cf7">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba08a6f8-2986-464f-8627-ba34dc2acfec">
      <Text>Origin holds. Cause waits on the lab.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="fa68f50e-068c-460d-bdd6-58a5aa55b83c">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="45" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DEPUTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="60d73808-26c8-40cd-9c5a-c8b79b8fc1a9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KITCHEN HAND">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="28908537-f882-4895-8f84-044f36e547c8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ODOM">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="77bc7d67-e9d6-4925-a124-b1795001cebe"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ONDINE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a3781266-c584-41b7-b7c1-4ca01864b67b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HALE RIVER FIRE STATION - APPARATUS BAY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a0e0ebdb-6d4a-400f-8f9b-daf624169b58">
      <Text>The engines are parked on the apron. Folding tables run the length of the bay, a deputy at each one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="467372e7-6555-4335-a77b-b5a673269d56">
      <Text>Survivors wait along the wall — bandaged forearms, blankets pulled around their shoulders. One woman still wears a soot-streaked party dress.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8df62e6-5754-4253-a22e-c8a90e9cf672">
      <Text>At the third table, ODOM sits across from RAY and ONDINE BEASLEY. Ray’s hat rests between them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1bd00d15-b757-4f1f-98bd-196c3a1fa7e5">
      <Text>ONDINE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56ae03b1-c37e-44a3-8721-570658db84f5">
      <Text>— Amos was at the end of the bar. First time I’d seen him in there since Merle let him go. Had one beer and never finished it. That Stroud girl was down the bar from him in her mama’s church dress.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="774ee5a4-9efe-45a8-b66f-1e8d3921a731">
      <Text>Odom turns the statement toward her. Ondine reads it and signs. Ray retrieves his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3a29f0e4-74b5-40ff-8adf-7fe8e4745e6a">
      <Text>FROM THE NEXT TABLE:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f113529e-fd58-4d7c-9fcb-fe9b83059c6c">
      <Text>DEPUTY (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1f152a76-ce6c-46a6-aee7-3a309ca08131">
      <Text>This was the day Merle fired him?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f52381c8-056b-4026-9406-b649323c5172">
      <Text>AT THE NEXT TABLE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1b59be0c-bd97-40ed-811b-3c99eba913db">
      <Text>A KITCHEN HAND, 20s, her forearm wrapped from wrist to elbow, sits across from another DEPUTY.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ad719485-f665-4f7c-b74a-b17d9d4d81f1">
      <Text>KITCHEN HAND</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a5352b13-e596-4634-a956-176857eeee27">
      <Text>Afternoon prep. I was at the sink. Couldn’t see them from there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2b50e660-1648-4826-b9ce-8268f0013609">
      <Text>DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d1efc61e-0262-4f08-898c-495d6d508484">
      <Text>What did you hear?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0308a311-03e6-4e68-b65a-8672c21e4dbd">
      <Text>KITCHEN HAND</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9ab24f54-dfd8-448d-b7c5-93792ff7e69b">
      <Text>Merle told Amos to lower his voice. Amos got louder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3edb6c48-24bb-4c07-8735-2203a3ed77f5">
      <Text>The deputy waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="84a5a9ef-4ea6-4c2e-a911-5310b3d8e8ff">
      <Text>KITCHEN HAND</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9406464f-175a-483c-9fa3-940a6a59703f">
      <Text>Said, “One morning you’re gonna come in here and find this whole place gone.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4d61dac4-b73d-4783-94df-a895069cce06">
      <Text>The deputy stops writing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f3037ee7-8172-4722-bddb-5475363918b0">
      <Text>DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e61f951a-94e2-458b-9419-18becfb3ddb1">
      <Text>Exact words?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1f092b7a-1c66-4b38-a8fb-ad0332a67bc9">
      <Text>KITCHEN HAND</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="72c4817d-ebd2-42d2-a33a-df0bd83d6936">
      <Text>Yes, sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4b16f8c1-3e64-4b37-bdd4-6287028c5b07">
      <Text>The deputy writes the sentence in quotation marks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="903123b0-56c8-4291-ab02-2b92129d67f9">
      <Text>A PRINT TECH hands Odom a comparison sheet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8fb9bb27-5cf1-4a1e-93f3-9cab43b64e8a">
      <Text>Two usable impressions from the padlock: AMOS HOYT — LEFT INDEX, RIGHT THUMB.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4e2ebadf-6b13-4972-9c79-f1fce3bb0d7a">
      <Text>Mercer carries a box of signed statements down the row of tables toward Odom.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="068057bc-02b4-4425-833c-924b521f8341">
      <Text>On the concrete beyond the tables, a HANDLER walks the accelerant canine down a row of twelve paper hospital bags. The dog passes eleven. At the twelfth it sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot" id="0a005f1f-bf8c-4560-9918-ccde80586ee5">
      <Text>INSERT - THE BAG’S TAG</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5fe1ffe7-8eeb-495e-8a28-662d9afb0e4c">
      <Text>COUNTY HOSPITAL — PATIENT PROPERTY. HELD PER FIRE INVESTIGATION.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f13991cf-f038-4431-9add-2a4e92c3f067">
      <Text>DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bfaca041-22dd-4f94-809c-c294db1c806a">
      <Text>Bureau pulled every bag this morning.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f6797a6b-2c27-420f-a3fa-48c41786e49f">
      <Text>Odom reads the name on the tag. HOYT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="08f8b1d9-3d68-4ce3-ad55-ed4f91503ca8">
      <Text>Mercer has stopped where he stands, the box still in his hands. He looks at the bag a long moment. Then sets the box down on Odom’s table without a word.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="20304432-2529-4545-bd5e-9436a974b574">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="46" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COBB">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="577e1be6-aea3-48eb-b2ec-fe4132251168"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="84ec60f9-3427-48be-965b-98764328d65f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COBB HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="86ed7146-bfe8-4868-bcf5-4fcbc6f9bdba">
      <Text>Cobb sits in a recliner facing a dark television. Across from him, Rucker holds his hat against one knee, notebook open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b5feaaca-fbc3-40fe-8c09-75da9bb6d4cf">
      <Text>Between them, on the coffee table: an evidence photograph of the cut chain and padlock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f8a6cc2d-570a-49cf-806a-d8c05879313a">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ed068e68-45c7-43c6-9e04-e8df3be94279">
      <Text>Beer came through there. Produce. Trash went out. That was about it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="60ac40e1-6d4f-4dc1-9d67-44a185dc128c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba9d9a2d-d080-42a0-8e06-3a4547ec4030">
      <Text>Who had the back at night?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="786edca2-f9df-4fa7-b0d4-2ab859efaa5a">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="202ea235-656a-4694-8500-1516040ee81d">
      <Text>Nobody. Door stayed shut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5d078369-fbc1-4d41-b6f0-d12d36f5e5f4">
      <Text>Rucker writes that down, then taps the padlock in the photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc0407c6-9661-4e9f-9c5b-9a4627d524d0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c38ebe77-25e9-4637-9fe7-8525e9861881">
      <Text>Why would Amos Hoyt’s fingerprints be on this?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6c2bc5b5-f2e1-475c-9a27-be840547ddfe">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="878ae8cf-ca37-4a78-94c5-52cc11989395">
      <Text>Amos put his hands on everything in that building. Something stuck, he fixed it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4d9ffec4-c046-40fc-958f-f5e5ca3978a7">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56fad689-cf27-44f0-a37b-a21390f4f6a7">
      <Text>That lock was new.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="574b4a2b-92b9-47e4-a975-143832530d92">
      <Text>Cobb looks at the photograph again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e302b67e-b61f-4d88-aeef-8c358d2c0661">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0e0d6ba4-2a4a-441f-a1e7-9d3aded7334c">
      <Text>Then I couldn’t tell you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="7fa3c783-e0cc-4bc0-b0e6-1e76ff2f86ae">
      <SceneProperties Length="5 6/8" Page="47" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4cd7c7e1-1cb4-4ed7-9f82-de2acaf08f5a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bf4d448a-3665-4364-a7dd-98b1e24d1de3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ODOM">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b8493f6a-63f2-47e5-b187-4d3dbd27a652"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a95d2657-dcc3-42a8-a510-f3421208f5b7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SHERIFF’S DEPARTMENT - INTERVIEW ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d8cf8fa-d5e2-4662-b305-b199ee3fd851">
      <Text>HOYT sits alone at a steel table, four days unshaven. Both palms are wrapped. His truck keys lie beside one wrist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0c1791f0-9790-4644-b255-7d0eb3bfdd54">
      <Text>The door opens. Rucker enters with a folder. ODOM follows, sets a recorder on the table and presses RECORD. MERCER comes in last and takes the wall beside the door. Arms folded.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="727efa79-3234-44fd-a56d-c53de9f0f23b">
      <Text>The door remains open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="757b6316-8f5c-483e-ae8a-891df4ae98ff">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="652be59c-169e-4b14-a541-bc3d92f185b4">
      <Text>Amos, this is voluntary. You want to stop, you say so.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ebb09f05-7328-404f-b9b6-021f44ab5722">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e7693e8d-9acf-4fc7-91a1-eeb7e1fc7978">
      <Text>I know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6f004a27-7a6e-46f0-a6d1-d9edc8654ab1">
      <Text>Rucker sits across from him. Sets the folder on the table but leaves it closed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="76eaa61d-bddc-479f-892d-bc788882a2f9">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f7d6e600-676e-49c3-beee-07f752f54835">
      <Text>Start when you knew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7e53dcbd-35cc-4f41-9319-ccc79acf7dad">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a8b1c275-b2f6-41b0-94a5-9e082fe925f0">
      <Text>I was out in the lot. Seen smoke come over the roof and went back in. Band quit about then. People started pushing for the front. The way they come in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5313f76e-2f89-48e1-a809-e627c81cb9fe">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8141748a-052a-42ca-8080-4e0e9d13fdc4">
      <Text>You came back in the front. You went the other way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f4d33027-201b-4af8-acd2-ee16937cfb36">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="985d8be9-781f-47be-9f62-2e601b585229">
      <Text>Whole room was headed for those doors. Wasn’t nobody at the back. I knew the other way out, so I went to open it up. Couldn’t see it. Knew where it was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1897e902-0d4a-46fa-ab3c-4fbee08cb64c">
      <Text>At the wall, Mercer’s arms come unfolded.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7a8e942b-5eeb-4b51-91d0-5ce25a044680">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f9788a89-34c3-485c-a525-1d707629e136">
      <Text>What happened when you reached it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e4188e5f-c691-45e5-91d2-58fb778f60cb">
      <Text>Hoyt looks at his wrapped hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2399d54c-f4c1-4d4e-8596-b4173ba5887c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1d7283f5-2aea-4404-b8a1-86cee3700781">
      <Text>Door gave an inch. Chain caught it. I put both hands on the lock before I knew it was hot. Wasn’t opening. I pulled three people off it and took them toward the front.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="93133c99-8dce-4964-9a92-a14e74c2d349">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="12e62fac-4bd3-4c04-897b-50e04cd8c605">
      <Text>Who did you pull off the door?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b60d0796-a49b-4ee9-baa7-baca08fdc233">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1f977c6a-aba7-4ffa-b324-8036fbe40973">
      <Text>Couldn’t see their faces. They couldn’t see mine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c284d95-ce28-4e5c-8720-dd74ad0e9314">
      <Text>Rucker opens the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a6129e42-6e52-468f-be08-dc95c41e3ab5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5c8a9b3a-36a1-4b86-bf59-e364563dbe60">
      <Text>You left before a deputy talked to you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="72be1cc1-6741-4fa1-8ef4-0b59ead4b278">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6e807111-ef4e-4f6f-ba38-29d80c49066a">
      <Text>Ambulances had people who couldn’t breathe. I could drive. They wrapped my hands, took my shirt, and I came back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f7945cc7-531d-4e41-a035-62221ffafeb3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b9d308c4-e13d-41c2-ad6a-464f0db8336d">
      <Text>Nurse wrote gasoline on your sleeves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="504ebb0c-6d8b-4495-8922-cd0fef699cdb">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9692fa1e-d51a-441f-b8f3-2c7c6d016c40">
      <Text>Carl Vickers run his truck dry. That’s what I was doing in the lot. Pouring a can into his truck when the smoke come.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4dece1aa-33dd-4f02-a6aa-a1d75119b644">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5b97f189-27a6-4021-a858-ea651a2d8cc2">
      <Text>Vickers gave the deputy “in the lot at midnight” and went home. Deputy went back out Tuesday. Now he don’t recall who poured.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a7058b7b-577a-49d6-9981-b8e2d91d6d69">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="11c42ea0-4962-4b1e-aee6-6cfe26015b81">
      <Text>I know who poured.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11090862-1519-4cf1-be88-66a3e6890755">
      <Text>Mercer puts his hands flat against the wall behind him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="111a6e25-db3d-4822-a262-a27ee15f9394">
      <Text>Rucker turns an evidence photograph toward him: the cut chain and padlock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d6881304-ed36-477d-9c19-86c84bb527f1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8353def8-7f84-43c8-820c-f6b03de4872d">
      <Text>The print unit matched a left index and right thumb on that padlock to you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="63ae1b73-25b3-44c1-bd7a-5c19fd7a1a40">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bec82133-35dc-40f8-bc0b-a0045d6a89d0">
      <Text>I told you. I grabbed it with both hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6ee7a174-17f4-4dd1-90de-52f3cd64fc45">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="01135d9c-8dee-462e-92af-190d7882f24c">
      <Text>Did you put that chain on the door?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f3ddba36-88c7-44a8-8f32-60c7224c05ec">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e66e6386-f083-48f4-9726-8dd4af5fa094">
      <Text>No. That door never had a chain while I worked there. I never seen that lock till it burned me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7a600f1e-5b6b-4281-8656-ea574f46c38b">
      <Text>Mercer comes off the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3ca2f56b-00e0-4c18-a72a-1eff2585e35d">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6aa467b4-56a0-4c9d-bd92-51bcdd58c694">
      <Text>Aldridge Dry Goods. Were you there that night? Did you set that fire?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7a0a55a4-8755-4642-830a-5a2000da2c01">
      <Text>Rucker doesn’t turn around.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a520c3d0-dc4a-4681-a829-7ef9a6c4ba53">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="36583dd8-1d4d-44b3-949f-a5a3bd245738">
      <Text>What are you talking about?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a63044d2-b201-46ce-83d7-0cf38bd3ebef">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e96fb745-63cd-4f6c-88a1-9cd582fdfeb9">
      <Text>Danny.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f7fc48db-5cc5-4f7c-84f8-3c65f3015957">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f7217867-048f-4069-a992-39d4730b4a21">
      <Text>I was inside it. They carried me out with no pulse and did compressions on me on the sidewalk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="02ab2d66-96bb-42f1-bc55-9568fffb79fa">
      <Text>Hoyt looks at Rucker. Rucker gives him nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5861b5fd-64f1-43e8-af90-686e080be849">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="527c461d-fb0a-43f9-bfa2-bb8b7a186e33">
      <Text>I never been in that building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6b0a0218-36d2-4af2-975e-c2595a122735">
      <Text>Mercer is at the table now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dff3615e-bcee-4264-8779-aa2316a6e893">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fa32fe97-27a0-44fd-8469-50086871819f">
      <Text>You told Cobb what was coming and it came. So say it. Say you set them. All of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5724c1ef-e6ea-4139-ab96-0f8ee73db8c0">
      <Text>Hoyt’s mouth opens. Nothing comes. He looks at the recorder, then at the open door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="db17c7ff-fff8-4a06-be34-24e37a25fd76">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a52cb320-8bfb-41e5-8ce5-b9af1f000516">
      <Text>Hall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f1256e7b-d73d-40c8-a1ea-c3f8d3916f14">
      <Text>Mercer stays where he is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7f610e0d-9523-4843-b66a-dd4e58366b23">
      <Text>Rucker turns and looks at him for the first time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="39131115-cadb-4057-9428-9797b38fc3b5">
      <Text>Mercer goes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f15068dc-acab-4fa7-bb42-73b86f67af6c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="267beef3-7de2-4860-8f24-197d4d0cb153">
      <Text>He was out of line. I apologize for him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e97b36c4-7088-41bc-b2e5-1e54fb6a72db">
      <Text>Hoyt’s eyes come back to Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3afe6918-c52f-44c6-979a-f861c7d77726">
      <Text>Rucker stands. Moves along the wall until he is behind Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f95d52be-f7b0-4303-93ec-e0d7aa3fc858">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eb6eebbd-f1ed-459e-b4bf-76bb0fd2a363">
      <Text>Nobody saw you at the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="eaad70bd-fd61-4610-b5e4-05a672096473">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c09ec43-cbf8-46e5-84cd-48800fd0f4ad">
      <Text>Nobody could see the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="da586327-b9f4-4109-b1cc-bd0d4dc62a37">
      <Text>Hoyt doesn’t turn to follow him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c6e12a39-a4a9-4f6d-a71d-e2a9be37811d">
      <Text>From behind him, Rucker looks down at the truck keys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="99d0c7d4-12ac-4c8e-b461-9adbb0f2140f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9ef15d53-91c0-4dec-a658-35bf756c6c83">
      <Text>Cobb fired you Monday. Friday you still had keys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="633ce12c-57e9-4492-b7e1-df5240dc2e7a">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="82bda07e-7937-4246-801b-f9d224844740">
      <Text>Front and office. He told me keep them till the cooler was together.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bdd2d5cb-bfbd-439b-9dc7-b636ddfc18c3">
      <Text>Hoyt works the two keys off his ring and sets them on the table. Rucker stays where he is, over his shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="adccd62c-c513-427a-bbb3-a9c1d82efacc">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e562e0a1-0664-488d-be3e-696a6de6e951">
      <Text>Part came Tuesday. I put it in Wednesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fbf8a11f-2187-48a8-a187-459a2125058e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="79a5c4c6-a14d-4565-bda6-4f86a982e374">
      <Text>And kept the keys.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6db2e533-5417-4c84-8e79-8b214793327a">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aee8f5d7-dae3-4c2e-a2e5-c73846fbbc36">
      <Text>They were still on my ring. I forgot they were there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="80c07ee5-ecfc-405c-90b5-345e6240ac70">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74f7c10f-2a28-43d9-88c4-d19bc986ae1c">
      <Text>Kitchen hand heard what you said when Cobb fired you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="78ab8920-3f0e-41be-b85f-b1256f8635ce">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1be4bd72-d4bd-4220-a8b5-e9553cad829e">
      <Text>I know what I said.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ffd34c0c-5e12-4eb0-b5ec-47ce9b66667f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6e87e4da-d07f-4724-a1cb-83ad0147679f">
      <Text>“One morning you’re gonna come in here and find this whole place gone.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dd8d66a1-294e-415b-811b-db8983fe7d44">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eacf9a72-2d25-435a-95d0-5ba4d374ee3e">
      <Text>That’s right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9af920ab-9208-4283-b423-682fa3efa713">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="53fa43bf-bc17-460b-a3c4-855fce90a8a5">
      <Text>Why would you say that?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e64ee68f-ca4d-4b4a-bd98-8b6c8c1a0b22">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e371e310-0690-4439-91b6-ad4e3da26904">
      <Text>Because I was mad.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="34b2de51-fa2f-45b7-9955-624dec37a99f">
      <Text>Rucker waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8750fef1-d8c2-430f-9ac8-426afc98d776">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2abee8b6-52ca-4304-b98e-c99cbb9eee19">
      <Text>He waits till something breaks, then he calls me. I was on my knees beside his cooler with the panel off when he told me I was done.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7ec3e9a0-8235-48ef-af1c-22c1b277d2fc">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c75c3ab5-e684-4de6-a851-c974d6b34e1d">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="73e2e882-013e-4206-b668-2a8c7a8f7620">
      <Text>Nine years, and he couldn’t wait for me to stand up. So I said the worst thing I could think of.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4558196f-3dd0-4b44-bc97-a40898d711e0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="37cba6e8-b39f-4685-a217-0a5fc0dae86b">
      <Text>Cedar Street. The mill store. Aldridge. The hall. Six weeks apart, then four, then three. Then six weeks to the Magnolia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1da5cb29-fc71-4957-9749-23c2cc495bda">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da90e05d-47f6-4e7a-a2a8-7a70685dafa2">
      <Text>I read the paper.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bcae008b-d152-4c25-9cb1-b8de735a0738">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cf81f0d3-bebd-4a1a-84c9-f797bd220029">
      <Text>Where were you those nights?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="138283c5-2076-4a23-8a1b-d41d0f5a6cd2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7af6e501-b32e-4f1b-a363-e72061c1f3e4">
      <Text>I’d have to look.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d8a030f3-3528-495f-b418-9ab1c9fc2fb9">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c774efcb-23fe-4662-8330-e9632c913024">
      <Text>You’d want to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a2278779-891e-406f-8938-f5da200a27ad">
      <Text>Rucker comes back around the table. Doesn’t sit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0f082043-ccfe-4ace-93f0-81b4c300d472">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5fd9c3b9-04cd-4d59-a682-795746fa50ba">
      <Text>Nineteen people died, Mr. Hoyt. You don’t seem tore up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="63da24b4-cb59-4a0e-a79a-160db1d941fe">
      <Text>Hoyt’s wrapped hands press flat against the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="76789905-7335-45ee-a80d-4144d9accbad">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b74a1e62-9f2d-4573-b96d-b05444220f23">
      <Text>I can still hear them hitting that door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c4eb5cba-d439-408a-bf4c-de35b604363e">
      <Text>Rucker says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dcb8b15c-a39d-42f9-b825-ce96c6cc574c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="39ee0904-2115-44a4-ba18-837f763d89e1">
      <Text>The three I pulled off that door. I still don’t know if they made it out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7c0a5cfc-180d-4b63-9f1d-0230db827b89">
      <Text>Now he looks directly at Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="48574a14-1e79-424a-8ac2-e63329f896fc">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3b9e6549-6b57-4cae-b98f-a62894e7ab61">
      <Text>Don’t tell me what I seem.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c197b68c-7067-48dd-8b9d-41d178774798">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="99f9b125-a74e-4bc8-8c69-b965b929a23f">
      <Text>Did you set fire to that building?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="551a889f-798f-4cdf-9bed-3812d7b7a738">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ee178096-f6a6-4d10-a931-7af5c7bfff19">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="21deea92-b5db-4080-8664-ed6749e2393b">
      <Text>Silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d941ff4f-e955-46a9-920b-8dd445abd4fb">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f7fdab5a-d6cc-449c-81f1-6dc99b86b8d0">
      <Text>I kept that building alive nine years. I did not burn it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8deb8758-707c-4bbd-8c3d-a397ecb0779b">
      <Text>Hoyt stands. Picks up his truck keys. Leaves the other two where they are.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3f1ba632-1517-46cd-87dc-79477e7e158d">
      <Text>He goes out through the open door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a2744c7c-2ac1-45ac-b74d-13ba4770b444">
      <Text>Rucker looks at the two keys on the table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c2d8472-73df-4119-8f0c-56c080099773">
      <Text>Mercer is in the doorway.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="db8a157a-ae8b-422b-95da-cbd0fd897841">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c0098493-b56e-48c8-a39c-e96ed5c6c587">
      <Text>It’s him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="282b64ef-e81b-43be-9409-1cc3d6f6ce2e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ed77d7ae-c1d1-402d-af59-7778bc97fece">
      <Text>What lit it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="465ebd0f-0f34-423a-b969-fc824813ac77">
      <Text>Mercer has nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b0c165f8-b35d-4f79-8929-be53edf9c49f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="764e3f17-5607-40a9-a9c7-9b4648ced3c0">
      <Text>Then neither one of us knows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="32fc63bb-6fe8-4831-abdc-051d60440796">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 4/8" Page="53" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6dfedce1-7387-47f0-99de-208e442489a9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ODOM">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="87cebd77-9a47-4473-ba08-491f0934ca8a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bb0fa374-88ea-47a5-b472-76f5b65c8e4a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="18c02d87-1ecd-4d3f-8899-2727d8ec9c70"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COUNTY COURTHOUSE - BORROWED CASE ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2d5068ac-7638-4937-b720-79948d010514">
      <Text>A jury room converted to a case room. Photographs, floor plan, witness statements, canine log.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="74770a51-b640-44c9-b5c6-b9f250272956">
      <Text>RUCKER’S draft origin-and-cause report lies open. The CAUSE line is blank.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9031dfb3-b795-489e-864a-3cf2b0ab2c78">
      <Text>At the far end of the table, MERCER checks contact sheets against the photo log, frame by frame.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c3003709-18fa-438e-a3b8-f411f8e2448b">
      <Text>SAENZ takes a page from the fax machine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5cab63c9-bcc7-45bb-b78b-d2763ac40130">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91a4acd4-4ad6-4825-ab1f-65393f0dc4f3">
      <Text>Atlanta. Nine cans off the corner, four off the clean side, the floor run. Nothing. Degreaser can on the shelf was sealed and half full. Gasoline on both cuffs of his shirt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2e4317c3-5370-4f02-a9b8-69c52fc2dc7a">
      <Text>Rucker places it beside the canine log.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b8e7a578-9bb4-4ada-8db8-6bba316c5cf0">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e2e2815b-b7f1-40fd-acd3-f5851e17f1c8">
      <Text>Dog and lab agree. We have the corner and the first fuel. We don’t have what lit it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="035f1caa-53f3-4b46-bbd0-f8362a5b290e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="84fd0deb-9c58-4cd7-bb27-85e1caae84ec">
      <Text>Panel never tripped. Outlet’s clean. Compressor’s across the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="43923ea7-19a8-46d3-adb9-eb430421f3a6">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d54c09ee-73fb-4ff1-8ca0-1984fa3c2748">
      <Text>That’s elimination. It doesn’t put flame in the foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ea164604-6c92-42e9-bb8f-ebb18b8d3ae5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="10d3efb5-9e3a-4d3d-8c9d-d6044cff1298">
      <Text>Undetermined closes the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="47cde616-80ed-43c3-80e0-ba7a66c89099">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ecfa4d89-576d-43e2-8995-e21bf424d89b">
      <Text>Then keep the file open. That doesn’t change what we found.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9d51db2-f215-4f30-80f7-99f352f5c5cb">
      <Text>ODOM enters with a thin stack.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="92a4758b-b8e1-42c7-aefc-6101ca3cc354">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ffd4ca7e-75bf-4305-a78f-7993efa84d39">
      <Text>No cameras inside or out. Nearest porch camera caught the glow, not the lot. Cobb says he doesn’t know who put the chain on. Kitchen crew’s gone by nine; nobody alive worked that door but Cobb. Bureau went home, like the man said.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7803220d-5706-4170-a408-4365819ea6ef">
      <Text>He places the print comparison beside the padlock photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="30793373-9da8-4628-8ea5-a4c787e8cd8d">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e11cbfb6-8ba9-45c5-ba68-e025a30b9baf">
      <Text>Left index and right thumb on the padlock belong to Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="faf31aaa-c92b-49a5-be83-3eebeb6334de">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8d2c246b-f990-4387-9053-77563efb7fd1">
      <Text>Prints don’t tell us when.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a0673ebb-f030-4768-901e-c68e1ffed6b1">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f9d8b6e4-6d53-43ff-b07e-5474857ad7e7">
      <Text>No. Emergency room called the palms contact burns. They can’t identify the object. Same nurse wrote “odor of gasoline, both sleeves.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8fb119f3-fed9-4290-b2b1-7027f48c8a4f">
      <Text>Rucker studies the photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6dcc2e8b-f5cd-4eb4-9459-1ba9b6897148">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9561bb62-1e62-4782-a2bb-54996721b45e">
      <Text>He pours it, chains the door cold, burns his hands on his own fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0848d5ed-aeb7-4661-bc96-5db005f51df9">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c871b3ca-dc7d-49c2-be41-2d783c3ed0fa">
      <Text>Or he grabs the hot lock trying to open it. Which is what he told you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="43e5e185-8df8-42ea-8ae3-d0bda624d59f">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f02f120e-37f9-49aa-a1bd-ab65b1d7dbe6">
      <Text>Cobb fired him Monday. He was back in the storeroom Wednesday finishing the cooler. Friday he still had front and office keys. Out the front door at eleven-forty. First flame call at twelve-oh-one. Back inside the smoke at twelve-fifteen with his hands burned.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="41341e70-ca03-4305-aab6-0bea6f8f6c58">
      <Text>He puts down a witness statement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bf41d631-66f9-4ed6-a72e-40d3a99f9051">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aeb5ab5e-001c-4901-94e5-dcb322cc3a0a">
      <Text>Kitchen hand signed what she heard when Cobb let him go. Hoyt confirmed the words.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="68fcf5d2-52cc-4971-bdbf-64d203fc2616">
      <Text>Odom sets down the coroner’s preliminary.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f7ccf42c-dd21-48d4-8ee3-ad0dcdbb9bb4">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af070e1f-85f7-488a-9f8d-6214be0d39f1">
      <Text>Nineteen, carbon monoxide. Soot in every airway. Nobody burned.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cb487e10-a53e-45c3-a9f3-7c2db998d71d">
      <Text>He goes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ff27b4ce-c3db-4b22-9196-1b93aac414da">
      <Text>Rucker looks from the photographs of Hoyt’s burned palms to the origin photographs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="01b94b77-d619-45cf-9a81-c6cbe92fb648">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3ff6a8cd-4bfb-4c6b-a0bf-fa860a632a15">
      <Text>Fired. Still had access. Threatened the building. Gasoline on his sleeves. Both hands on a new lock chaining the exit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="408fd00d-a142-4986-be87-f5eb327e18fb">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b2d94af9-c3ee-4b3c-b93d-33687ce7a3a1">
      <Text>Dog sat on his shirt. Dog walked that room twice and never sat. That’s two facts, Eldon. You’re making them one. It doesn’t put the chain in his hands before the fire, and it doesn’t put flame in the foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8810b84d-80a7-4fd2-8709-cd89ab34b52f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b4653da4-11eb-47f6-adb3-c1c3430d77dc">
      <Text>No accidental source puts flame in it either.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b43334eb-30a1-44f8-a1c4-4e643e9f8f5a">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9574f782-214a-483e-99d8-e7acdf116651">
      <Text>Then it’s still undetermined. Hoyt doesn’t change that. You don’t get incendiary by starting with a suspect and working backward.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="08f3a220-88b2-44b6-94b7-3f7f3eb6c5fd">
      <Text>Rucker looks to the four earlier fire dates marked across the timeline — the uneven gaps between them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bff28018-64e4-4500-b150-127d9dab12df">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="121f58d2-97d3-4fe3-bd70-86cebb538a51">
      <Text>Six weeks since the hall. He was down to three.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="72d57250-2f92-4b12-bde1-a37a4177eca9">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7503ed8b-f0d0-442f-9b4f-8b8a55f1c86a">
      <Text>Since who’s gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f59b8ef5-90f2-4225-8332-215d66c34135">
      <Text>Rucker turns the dates face down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="642938cc-e3a7-4562-97dc-82eb14d479ce">
      <Text>He draws nine photographs from the contact sheets and squares them beside the report. Mercer watches him do it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5162feeb-ae08-400a-aba9-79bb0b70c661">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b92ebd53-e3b9-4e83-873a-ab9731ae315d">
      <Text>You told me everything before anything moved. I shot a hundred and forty-two photographs. That’s nine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2246e036-267b-4d43-afe8-b1b00bde7568">
      <Text>Rucker looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9598ddc9-6f89-403d-a436-24367c692d63">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f29760bd-d08c-4d90-84d6-04883b6a814a">
      <Text>Nine is what a jury needs. The rest go in the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="aa26d7ac-7a54-4e33-b7ff-5f4bbc232512">
      <Text>Mercer looks down at the remaining frames. Returns to the log.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e7c916ff-4364-4aac-a23c-70680890c73e">
      <Text>Rucker writes on the blank line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="26793e18-738a-458f-be5c-04c2810e522d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f0df95ad-f703-43cd-8e0f-cc29879739d3">
      <Text>Cause: incendiary.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="65f50bff-af89-464a-9990-235bd16007c4">
      <Text>He signs and pushes the report to Saenz.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5a49bacb-8426-4bc2-af73-dfec35aafe5a">
      <Text>Saenz reads the cause line. He signs the origin block and leaves the cause block blank.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1da5bd5e-7d23-495e-b42d-69eb030a7491">
      <Text>SAENZ</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f735110f-cee1-4d39-9ab1-34d8dc3b37e1">
      <Text>I’ll sign the origin. I won’t sign incendiary. The evidence stops at that corner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c8f914ed-13db-46d2-b0e0-fbf710bdca5a">
      <Text>He pushes the report back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="987a3076-0297-4cd2-af30-ad04cf74a320">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0ccf0ef0-541a-47ec-8f1f-0283e03c397c">
      <Text>Your report goes in whole.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="c589dc38-ccf8-4342-9801-75190fc91d48">
      <Text>Rucker ties the folder and writes the case number on the front.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="dcab48f9-d750-40b6-8982-19acc8dde8e1">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="56" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0ec718a7-24d2-4e4e-9eb7-aba8e9a0a6e4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="GOVERNOR">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9747c4ff-e26d-46e3-b606-2e67e117ddc9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="89c5c6e2-7dde-46e1-8bb8-b0d37f315102"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL’S OFFICE - MONTGOMERY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d0d6e6f4-a125-4269-a5c7-a102bcf57c17">
      <Text>Framed commendations, a state map, reports stacked along the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b3053886-626a-489f-8d27-17ae8615e583">
      <Text>WENDELL COE, 60s, State Fire Marshal — compact, stout — sits behind his desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="aff17304-57f4-40cd-a300-6aa22e4eca9a">
      <Text>The GOVERNOR OF ALABAMA, 60s, broad-faced, silver at the temples, stands at the window in a dark suit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7188575b-c9c1-4e34-b32b-48f85c4934f1">
      <Text>Rucker enters with his hat in his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a847e318-18ec-4eb8-992c-3cb6f1f7f3c1">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f919b329-5513-49c9-bd30-c2f34e930ba3">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker. I’d rather be meeting you any other way there is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="46cce2ae-32b9-4eda-84fe-65e1fd332cc3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="611d69ff-01f6-4916-9aed-800a0403cbda">
      <Text>Governor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7544992c-97a7-4255-b45e-841580260c46">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a972544-403e-4124-bcb7-62cac450b0e3">
      <Text>Sit down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6494ecd0-28e8-4509-8503-2e8cdc204270">
      <Text>Nobody sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ed07035a-c82c-4eeb-a5ba-344e9a20700b">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7aa1ded0-8657-461a-8bc9-d06bb4e5955c">
      <Text>I’ve been to four funerals this week. Sunday I’ve got two more. Every family asks me the same thing. Not how it started. Who did it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aba29122-684c-4b1c-b1a4-9d7c7c6120ea">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f367576b-5b6e-4a22-82ce-a2874d2a7116">
      <Text>Cause is signed as of this morning. Who did it isn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4671b499-37d2-482e-b1a4-8e7ef10e8caf">
      <Text>The governor turns from the window.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c3a25c4c-45f5-4e9f-817b-0b699d7f47ff">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="edee8745-5dbf-4632-af29-32a01420eba0">
      <Text>I’m not asking for a name that won’t hold. Everybody wants what those families want.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b875a4ac-2696-4d51-90d3-b0fa402a8597">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dfaf0a25-462f-4929-8a31-a68aca417654">
      <Text>Then it has to come from the evidence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d463bf3b-ebe3-41e5-8835-c9e4304662bf">
      <Text>The governor takes his jacket from the back of a chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fdfb1ba0-e876-4359-ba69-4dd9c41e9ce9">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0e0561bc-2c55-4278-be1c-345041ecd684">
      <Text>Quick as the truth allows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b9f23805-d05c-4acd-b7da-b385bbd34108">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1c19f811-7ff7-4760-9624-f4bf66f4c700">
      <Text>That’s the only clock I’ve got.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3dcd7f60-3277-435d-a209-dd7bd6d546be">
      <Text>The governor studies him, then crosses to the door. As he passes, he puts a hand on Rucker’s shoulder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2c133384-4c07-4d8e-9c5f-240d2535a17e">
      <Text>GOVERNOR</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9e1acb3a-c54f-4cae-888d-1ea3883b92e0">
      <Text>I need a name on that fire, Marshal. One I don’t have to take back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6a1784b9-5ea1-413f-b54b-a40e97a8f50e">
      <Text>He leaves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1453affb-8fda-47ef-b772-67049be73cb5">
      <Text>Coe and Rucker remain standing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9f755017-7e21-455f-80b1-842080d5b94d">
      <Text>COE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56464541-a40f-4641-b062-c1f1d2c209a7">
      <Text>Lanier’s waiting on your report.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9c65de3e-7d2b-480a-8568-c95307c26c5e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c477fdd8-1871-4cdd-a4f8-8108251eb98e">
      <Text>Yes, sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15aeb624-3f9c-4cba-ae47-49124e573599">
      <Text>COE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="55ffa2a5-af7b-48fa-908e-cf7d48aedd40">
      <Text>If the governor hadn’t walked into this room, would you be ready to hand it over today?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d75ae7d2-cedb-48d7-93e0-238cf0379a42">
      <Text>Rucker looks at the hat in his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3d9079f3-fb6c-4a88-8f43-cf7f32c08b8a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b10ad5b2-9e1c-4979-97cc-f073ad8ecc3f">
      <Text>The evidence would be the same.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2a0160ed-66fb-43ba-b7bb-9c0d4bdaf404">
      <Text>COE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1d288270-baf9-410c-8c1f-6b606ac745dc">
      <Text>That wasn’t my question.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="052edbc5-90b6-4774-a699-f38a85430a59">
      <Text>A beat. Rucker puts on his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6f8aefd9-b3f1-4446-9c85-b0a01a25960d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6a7fb40d-5dca-480c-9534-ff571edd1f65">
      <Text>I know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c0a42f6a-0c1e-4ca8-af24-6b4ab1d52d82">
      <Text>He leaves. Coe remains standing behind his desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="081c52ab-fc97-43a0-89a8-7b1f6cf8655b">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="58" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f0c6f498-bd60-4331-8a01-fc58906b6055"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4de5f658-de94-4447-8806-67b7de791393"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL’S OFFICE - MONTGOMERY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d65ab6ac-5f08-477c-8d75-b17bd49688a6">
      <Text>Rucker crosses the lot toward the Tahoe. His phone rings. He answers without breaking stride.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59ec9c39-c7a0-45db-a2ce-5849f7031a2a">
      <Text>MERCER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="66f4c8d9-81d1-4c9f-90e0-eb64d5bc1ada">
      <Text>What’d the governor want?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="36820a9b-b14d-46d0-95aa-d4d9c8230aa1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab558508-843f-4877-a369-d45e787fabdc">
      <Text>A name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="399a27fd-b1d1-474a-9486-9bb55a7f28d7">
      <Text>MERCER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9047b59d-de68-47bd-b412-5e745d53dfd2">
      <Text>We’ve got one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4d0a42f4-3a57-4b52-a4bc-0db90f2d8d39">
      <Text>Rucker ends the call. Gets in. Drives.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="f03054db-422d-4c33-a79f-bbe5c4d27ab9">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="58" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fe11d4ea-d517-4045-9657-fdf8085a1d06"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="953caa61-63e3-4d1c-be54-2a440c298fb9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HOYT HOUSE - DUSK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e49c11f2-3246-492f-8455-d85c0deeb91f">
      <Text>The work truck in the yard, hood up. KENDRA in past her elbows. HOYT holds the droplight. Both palms wrapped. The beam wanders.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="918efa2b-ae89-463b-bfb6-4102c90d3de5">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f4548f8-2227-4151-91a8-0bb3c967d416">
      <Text>Light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bd69fd64-be88-4a6c-8fd8-1bc68af4bada">
      <Text>He steadies it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f259ed2f-f84c-4fce-a72a-ff235a451556">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a26246e2-7e1c-44b5-8c35-8551184f0e98">
      <Text>Other way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3d209a43-c0fa-4571-a161-bce028fe023c">
      <Text>He moves it two inches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e30a2a16-9653-4271-8261-d88f9c1b51a1">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7a1c8e1d-b1d4-4350-a5c9-99acad0d5345">
      <Text>Anybody comes to that door with a paper, you don’t say nothing to them. You call Miss Ondine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="98f2cb92-45a2-417b-aef8-43187b2e9929">
      <Text>Kendra stops working.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b84b7f07-da4d-4563-b33c-86194bdf6f67">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b4ec4971-08d9-42df-8e36-3656cace1a2e">
      <Text>Who’s coming to the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8c23ee37-7ff9-4cc7-81bf-a3f7176a4474">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="87143e45-2f62-461a-8ad5-0fdd178d83b8">
      <Text>Sheriff’s people.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="58ca13c7-e9ac-4fcb-b82b-e9d55450278b">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d423e321-3a37-44d5-8d58-2aa78f93eab7">
      <Text>You were pulling people off that door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4a29ecd7-65f3-4acf-a643-be0558125fe5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6b05bdcb-0675-4bf8-8905-e89578571da2">
      <Text>They got a state man’s boy in there says I set all five of them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="18acadd4-ab2f-412a-b420-44a809568305">
      <Text>A moment. Then Kendra leans back into the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="73493cc0-c8c7-48aa-a4b2-17a83069038e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7060866a-1a7c-4758-8e1b-13582fd608bc">
      <Text>Tell me where.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ab023880-33dd-4a75-8228-5837f163f8a1">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5e8c2d07-8869-4f40-8988-287ec2ec528d">
      <Text>Other way.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c27208c5-0448-45c5-b65d-6bb1371e0103">
      <Text>He moves the light. The beam isn’t steady. She can see it from where she is. She keeps working and doesn’t look at it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fd42dd70-76f7-4cd6-9e9b-2cf5b7da61a3">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="55c9af13-b852-4dff-8679-6e5d9ff05982">
      <Text>Kendra.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4781c95a-60b9-4d0f-9778-15ad21f18693">
      <Text>She stops. Looks at him across the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="184de954-4d59-4ad9-86a4-9e7dd3ccf00e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="505233f8-6daa-4162-8c81-4f36c6070305">
      <Text>I ain’t done nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4b1fdba8-f4c2-4169-9c4d-1edbc89823e7">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="85f067a7-f937-4fea-a951-82941cb3eb0c">
      <Text>I know it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24ce1502-e064-419a-9482-405a071a5f64">
      <Text>She goes back in. He holds the light steady now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="84f5b852-bae7-4779-bf3b-3c878ea2ff5f">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 1/8" Page="59" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="dac624f9-f0d9-4b65-bbc1-60e71708a21e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a21f48c7-d046-4815-9089-fb781f01f961"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SAENZ">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="13d1671c-1b2c-4ece-ba00-83337bae50e2"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HOYT HOUSE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b92dbba0-e1b3-4eb7-aeba-5b842e237f85">
      <Text>The same yard. The hood is closed now. Porch light on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4d39a66b-8b92-4841-ab08-ab792ecdaa7d">
      <Text>Two county cruisers park one house away, lights off. Rucker’s Tahoe stops behind them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="85a6483e-7767-4c34-89fd-3fe4d193113a">
      <Text>ODOM and TWO DEPUTIES cross to the house. Mercer stands beside the second cruiser. At the Tahoe, Rucker opens his notebook, checks his watch and writes the time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="47ecf5ea-26b2-44d8-9535-fe19c59e8142">
      <Text>Odom knocks. Hoyt appears behind the screen, both palms wrapped, and lets them in. The words don’t carry.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9de8ea3f-b1b2-499e-9e48-475a8fe8f40e">
      <Text>Rucker waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ff6e6ed0-a374-4b08-bc72-9774f173c805">
      <Text>The screen opens again. Hoyt comes out between the deputies, wrapped hands cuffed behind him, boots unlaced. They walk him to the first cruiser.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b27cbf4c-602d-400a-bfa6-b209d2d61af8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fe8fd046-ec12-491c-ac84-648ecb1af33c">
      <Text>Eldon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dd270bfc-5b60-42a2-b9b4-5199d7580f53">
      <Text>Rucker looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4386f8ac-d422-43d7-91f9-f0ad76cb76b5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dd3d1f39-586f-48b7-9d5c-394c59e31380">
      <Text>You believe I set that fire?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3f326c24-8013-48d1-b3a9-1938f0d51bc8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="941aa01c-e1d2-467f-9255-d93bc1e94d85">
      <Text>I signed the report.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="41e7bdf2-35aa-4050-846d-78d79ae48f1f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e5df44e4-a747-4d29-b1fb-688cf50dd284">
      <Text>That ain’t what I asked you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6277c147-c284-4dda-b4dc-24378172d8eb">
      <Text>A deputy opens the rear door. Hoyt stops. He does not get in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59d9b472-bbe1-40ea-aaff-6de0fb7f7787">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8dcfd837-8f77-4020-97ae-2ebbf866b99c">
      <Text>Pete shook my hand when I came in. Deena had my beer down before I sat. June asked me to come.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="324d6d6a-b6da-4a3f-a0eb-21371ebb1143">
      <Text>Rucker holds his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d3495a4-a94e-4c56-bb5e-cfdcc822ca70">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9443e16a-97c7-4c75-812a-d272668d2c76">
      <Text>You think I killed them?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="56ccca28-6d04-4034-99b8-bbf54ae1a59d">
      <Text>Rucker does not answer. Hoyt studies him another moment, then gets into the cruiser on his own. It pulls away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6e0bc735-2877-49c2-bf40-a7c6430d742f">
      <Text>Porch lights come on. Neighbors emerge in slippers, work boots and housecoats. Mercer watches a whole street watch Hoyt leave.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="538feadc-0256-4bfe-84de-5e906f9e1be3">
      <Text>At the Tahoe’s hood, Rucker records the departure time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="83118d19-c879-4138-a086-d1b5486797e7">
      <Text>Through Hoyt’s front window, the kitchen light is still burning.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="84f2214b-a3e1-452c-ae0a-78f0f8bd2cc5">
      <Text>Rucker drives away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="30dd6852-efe1-4fab-a81a-ea0a56c087f4">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="61" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LANIER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0182ca2c-121b-46d0-95d7-f2759a44a390"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="REPORTER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ebc8b1cd-fe16-430c-bc0e-bd5fd90c49a5"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f7f5a909-921e-429b-8154-d19347ae21ea"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ab98ba9c-1d60-4a64-a7fe-8fd15da0834e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HALE RIVER COURTHOUSE - STEPS - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a0c9ab42-985e-4270-b53a-37ea53c347f5">
      <Text>Microphones crowd a lectern at the top of the steps. Reporters fill the sidewalk below. Local camera crews stand beside two network cameras.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ce40fcd5-0055-4618-8dd4-ecb23a349b69">
      <Text>At the back of the crowd, SLOAN leans against his truck, arms folded, duty shirt still on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ea399363-f6c2-48b8-8d87-538beded582b">
      <Text>RUCKER waits behind SHERIFF LANIER, hat in his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca1740ed-3ea8-4977-930a-8ed1991c8ebf">
      <Text>REPORTER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="763529da-8893-4a06-a8bb-f7ae18ed28cd">
      <Text>Sheriff, who do you have in custody?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7fb367bd-e5fa-45e0-a8ef-0d64fb765380">
      <Text>Lanier glances at Rucker. Rucker steps to the microphones.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="83a21b99-8357-4f95-b702-4a75e518802e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="05b6a3a7-f995-4c9c-9e55-f352537a178e">
      <Text>The cause of the Magnolia fire is incendiary. It originated in a rear storeroom. A man is in custody in connection with that fire. That’s all I can confirm today.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="223ab622-2cac-484d-83a0-362753dcdca6">
      <Text>He steps away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d51476f7-474c-46d5-b7e0-69a9246c2bae">
      <Text>REPORTER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aec46224-bb6a-465e-a7e5-13d0214307d0">
      <Text>Is the suspect Amos Hoyt?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a0dd1dfb-d61f-403f-9179-3a46657fe87f">
      <Text>Lanier takes the lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="900321ba-feff-40a5-a64d-03ae57877b61">
      <Text>LANIER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dc130506-ab94-4d32-9995-5c0629361fec">
      <Text>His name and the charges will be released after booking. That’s all for today.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ef9a144c-36df-49f2-b82a-f1c4594fd464">
      <Text>The reporters keep calling questions as Rucker heads toward the cars. Sloan pushes off the truck and falls in beside him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4d4a5e84-d08e-4514-93c6-3b80555c3b81">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5460f739-8457-4960-a764-b13a08d3c09a">
      <Text>Man in custody. That cover my four empty buildings too?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b3b13eb5-f975-4e9d-a93d-fbda07f5f948">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="28b69c56-3186-47c7-b221-29885757b51c">
      <Text>The Magnolia carries its own file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bca10da2-a66b-448c-b11c-33cab05cbfa4">
      <Text>Sloan stops walking. Rucker doesn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="30da353a-80e4-47a9-9ea6-13408e8bf920">
      <Text>SLOAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2cb575c4-1117-479e-96e7-f5fc05a2ce65">
      <Text>Then he’s still out there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eed659d5-5696-43e0-8bef-91e257b4bb12">
      <Text>Rucker reaches the Tahoe. Behind him the crowd is already thinning — the county going home with its answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="f7d4ef8c-7e64-4771-8a7c-fa2c2bb5019c">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="62" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PREACHER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e6d5f1fb-1b26-4e86-b93d-d7b1fb56ad6e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MOUNT OLIVE BAPTIST CHURCH - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5072429b-d9e6-4fe2-b93e-94ae72711079">
      <Text>Every pew is full, hand fans moving. At the front: a closed casket and a framed photograph of June — head back, laughing at something outside the frame.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cfec2262-37d6-4b46-8966-8b6883eae230">
      <Text>Near the piano, two young men from Friday’s band sit in ill-fitting suits, one holding his guitar with no cable attached. In the front pew, Ray’s hat rests on his knee beneath Ondine’s perfectly still hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="923c8a9e-40d7-4dc2-8126-bd668beccc3c">
      <Text>The PREACHER, Black, 60s, collar soaked through, waits for the programs to stop rustling. A handwritten page lies folded inside his Bible. He closes it without opening the page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c225c975-a25a-43d1-9354-fe0c5b4bfc4d">
      <Text>PREACHER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e25a79cf-f777-4841-8894-6b911d68c285">
      <Text>June never waited on words when a song could carry farther. So we’re going to sing first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e9b3ba93-1b50-47c0-8ad8-208bb8e693e0">
      <Text>Ondine begins humming under her breath. The slow number June dedicated to her and Ray Friday night. Ray lowers his head.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="29b20e0d-2583-4d33-a418-e13e973ddf4a">
      <Text>The guitarist recognizes it. He finds the first chord quietly. Others join until the melody moves through every pew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0457dcf6-e753-485f-8eee-b3acf2a319e8">
      <Text>The congregation takes the first verse without her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="826b7a45-a8df-4b7e-a388-8c1bbe30e6ba">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="62" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b77ca283-2792-48b1-a3a1-c5d1f7672d67"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUDGE HARLAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a2978847-88e7-4884-9189-a793d1c19d56"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COURTROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="af7f8eb0-9434-4301-8f14-6cdacfa75bab">
      <Text>SUPER: 2016.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f27731dd-f992-42bd-8b6e-df29b1fcd6b7">
      <Text>The gallery is full again. The jury box is empty. Kendra sits behind Hoyt. Rucker on the last bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2fd7b0d6-02f0-4597-8c38-d512e17d296c">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN, 70s, white-haired and gaunt, takes off his glasses.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e3d20806-9bbd-409d-8435-df755de202f1">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3809830c-9cc2-479c-87ea-53377c5e5deb">
      <Text>The court has received the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">presentence</Text>
      <Text> report, heard the parties and considered the jury’s recommendation of life imprisonment without parole.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e0eb62da-2ac9-41b8-9481-e77922fdfd85">
      <Text>He looks at Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b9112a2a-77a0-47a1-9ec4-338bfd800533">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="640f799b-ff36-49a3-b541-f13c0e7013fb">
      <Text>Mr. Hoyt, before sentence is pronounced, is there anything you wish to say?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3512b55c-b860-4931-8dab-0428554e6f94">
      <Text>Hoyt stands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="91fc3ba6-3d99-4926-b444-3f70dd328615">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="45c252fb-a0c4-4a2b-bac3-e2ed208909bf">
      <Text>I did not set that fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="34441c76-dbee-4c78-ace0-4589fe5d64f9">
      <Text>Harlan waits. Hoyt has nothing else.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="95d4df16-b3c6-480e-92ee-bf6a2f1b70dc">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6bf24bb1-25b3-4f3f-9c2a-b0961cbee3f4">
      <Text>Under Alabama law, the jury’s recommendation is advisory. It does not bind this court.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="da4cac26-49ff-4f72-a169-31075fcd2335">
      <Text>He looks down at the sentencing order.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d92f900b-b4da-440a-831b-4537087fc473">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5056a95f-9eaa-465a-afba-5ef0f6325a60">
      <Text>This court finds that the defendant, acting in retaliation after his dismissal earlier that week, deliberately set fire to an occupied building and secured an exit against the people inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2c3b3d56-b2f7-4ef5-ab4f-73ab921bb481">
      <Text>Harlan looks directly at Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="529d1571-23b8-4a94-a47e-8362e54119ec">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1aa078e9-8c72-49e1-8fb2-e08dbcc67fae">
      <Text>Nineteen people died. Scores more were placed at risk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e6fcca9b-2e5d-479b-8c4d-41861f5d69eb">
      <Text>He sets the order flat before him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e37a38e4-cae8-4186-973b-7ccbaf47a37e">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="71a77bc4-2ec1-4046-9ef3-45a9fabcdc92">
      <Text>The court finds that the defendant knowingly created a great risk of death to many persons. That aggravating circumstance outweighs the mitigating evidence and the jury’s recommendation.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6fdb5596-2731-418d-be12-47a46ce7ee6e">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b67eb70e-79c1-403c-9bf7-a3bc6eb4fe4d">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1c30d015-935b-485e-9fe0-0e28e2d4655d">
      <Text>For each of the nineteen capital-murder convictions, the defendant is sentenced to death.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3b29087a-9a31-46d5-a0c6-b292f0a964d5">
      <Text>He puts his glasses back on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f775d0cd-5fe6-432f-8f34-e185740bd955">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83a26a04-366e-4dfe-a923-71096d892ecc">
      <Text>Upon pronouncing a sentence of death, it is customary for this court to say, “May God have mercy on your soul.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d9594e16-07df-4216-aa79-73409aca5663">
      <Text>Harlan looks directly at Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7905af09-2f6e-45eb-9de5-3c8e376b672b">
      <Text>JUDGE HARLAN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e17737bd-1538-48d8-b462-f4b1e97b8792">
      <Text>I will offer no such prayer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ee3db132-4df4-4210-bd61-885cf79b8184">
      <Text>A low murmur rises from the gallery. Kendra remains motionless in the second row. Hoyt stays on his feet, eyes fixed on the state seal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11c954e0-5645-4044-b8c9-fbba8fbadf4c">
      <Text>The deputy cuffs him in front and turns him toward the side door. Hoyt sees Rucker on the last bench. Rucker meets his eyes; neither looks away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="65cdaaf6-08f7-4ad7-89b8-7e92ec86dd3d">
      <Text>The deputy leads Hoyt out. The gallery empties, the rear doors swinging before settling shut.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6d9948bb-dae5-4700-8f37-3da84c5c66a0">
      <Text>Rucker remains alone on the last bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="4cdee99d-6e1e-4db3-8d60-9d193b59772e">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 1/8" Page="64" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e5c59161-5887-4d07-b8f7-7d6fc15b9e80"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fd59a9ff-dedb-45d2-9a3e-0f662e02f99c"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MISS ADELE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6306ea8a-05e3-4a14-94c7-21f6faf8a752"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NEWS ANCHOR">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e67ed3f4-867d-4c00-95e1-76e31b39b443"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4b0beb60-320d-4a20-8c1f-6fccee28a529"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. DOT’S DINER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ff2560a4-b584-4331-9908-65b6dbde35a3">
      <Text>The diner is packed for lunch. Every counter stool is filled. Silverware clatters against plates. Coffee pours. One customer’s laugh carries above the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b820fbaf-7551-4222-8392-59a68ad0296e">
      <Text>On the television over the counter:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2e3d23f5-eba9-4aa7-b7b9-9561d4447411">
      <Text>NEWS ANCHOR (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="45fa9de7-0193-4320-accb-c43a018626c1">
      <Text>...the Hale River jury recommending life imprisonment before Judge Samuel Harlan imposed the death penalty...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a6b99f54-8416-4667-9bb3-0d763de33dac">
      <Text>Nobody looks up. Rucker sits alone in a booth. Eggs. Toast. Coffee. He cuts into the eggs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8d0ed79b-c10d-4653-9388-07fc9cd9dc32">
      <Text>MISS ADELE stops beside the booth on her way out. Pats the table twice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="90fe53b0-7c96-41f7-afca-fe91b6473344">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="89eda423-b2f0-442e-bbbd-5550b92c9b62">
      <Text>Knew you’d get him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d1c7c1e0-ffc3-4a0f-bd71-07ae4460696c">
      <Text>Rucker looks up at her. A beat. He reaches for the salt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f0547a39-8dc4-4769-aa0f-1382095cb79f">
      <Text>The cap isn’t on tight. Salt pours across the eggs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="93a27f23-7969-4d34-adf3-acdaaeea7e50">
      <Text>He watches it spread. He slowly pushes the plate away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cbd5d880-21c5-4d06-9355-adfaf623e52e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ee7e7950-bdca-4e04-aedb-42091e4fd0f9">
      <Text>Yes, ma’am.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ca351482-eed3-496b-818e-2b15c1058b84">
      <Text>Miss Adele smiles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5c12c2aa-9f70-41c2-9b90-3831e2eb6578">
      <Text>MISS ADELE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b67ade64-b323-4e1f-aacb-d7bf60e23f87">
      <Text>Proud of you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f0a90a97-e2b8-49e4-a322-5cbdf737dade">
      <Text>She squeezes his shoulder and heads for the door. The bell over it jingles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="462159b4-1f42-4f1c-b909-2bdb4e9e5581">
      <Text>The waitress tops off Rucker’s coffee without asking. He never looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="efe2f80d-c57e-498a-9183-7786e7850d6e">
      <Text>On the television —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="44c527d7-a786-4ba8-8f02-cfb2396fe3ca">
      <Text>NEWS ANCHOR (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="47bbc11d-5575-47dd-89dc-6ec1f833d0a6">
      <Text>...execution date has not yet been set...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d008b76a-6c78-4602-ac1d-ebf6ba9c6340">
      <Text>Rucker lifts his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="19dcb120-6f4e-49c7-aa04-aec45ca8fee9">
      <Text>The television reflects faintly in the diner window. Inside, somebody asks for more toast.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ab958039-5c0b-4a46-8b1d-e146e98e6ddd">
      <Text>Rucker leaves the plate where he pushed it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="15564bf8-6a26-455c-a184-7ca450ce56f8">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="65" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fa318a29-0a90-417c-8808-2c233a74f618"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7c204c65-e1e3-48ec-948d-b0593160274a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a152cc0d-ce6b-44e1-b507-7c5216ebda0e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="356d4984-a27a-46b0-b6f6-a8b60ad303e7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HOYT HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c7981a63-80c6-4c94-998c-97aa7ae04e1a">
      <Text>The pickup’s hood stands open in the driveway. Beneath it, a droplight hangs from a loop of baling wire, its beam two inches too high.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ee11f60-47fb-4685-8a67-3e7b0bb24b4c">
      <Text>KENDRA HOYT, 18, leans into the engine bay, wrenches and sockets arranged in a straight row on a folded shop towel. She reaches deeper, pulls back to shift the light two inches, then goes back inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="19dc006d-d956-4e65-9517-959fb8efa587">
      <Text>Kendra gives a rocker bolt half a turn, checks it with her fingers and wipes her hand on her jeans.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4391b32e-04b9-497d-9f19-ab871f72a308">
      <Text>Her phone BUZZES on the fender: HOLMAN CORRECTIONAL FACILITY. She answers and puts it on speaker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ec3b6674-ddee-432f-92be-537001cfd66e">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7f3eaa28-2b9c-48d6-b0b7-2b6950323c34">
      <Text>Hold on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a79b4604-e20b-4ad1-9773-06b169f069f9">
      <Text>Kendra gets behind the wheel and turns the key. The engine catches and settles into a steady idle. She closes her eyes and listens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c1633aa6-9d61-4f82-95ea-a5e436889677">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dba40887-bc10-491e-b2c7-f1a36923441b">
      <Text>Let me hear it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="53cd1fb0-9d94-4ec6-97cc-aada914ecbb1">
      <Text>She places the phone on the dashboard. For several seconds, neither speaks. Only the engine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0573c7f5-079e-4eb4-8eda-4412ee118fa0">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2cb4f13b-dd30-4f9b-b8f5-2a55926b30aa">
      <Text>Tick’s gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a879bd69-5ec8-41d8-a63c-dfb2cbe51785">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="760c7c04-a27a-47ab-b4db-b9226abb9623">
      <Text>Rocker. Half a turn.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="49d46afc-5c18-4170-9414-99c5164a07f0">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c8d40e76-ee28-464e-9975-4bbf4215318e">
      <Text>You check it warm?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="59b2e522-d000-4df5-b176-074ddfc8ce08">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a2cf5b87-da4b-4cbf-a533-a3cef3b1df93">
      <Text>Doing it now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a72fe3e4-9ca4-41c6-9c75-33eab07b35f2">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="12ad0aa7-5fa2-47f4-ab2d-2a7f1278cc76">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="30c32563-df8e-41c1-a4e1-6e15b3bb0a73">
      <Text>All right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ba287d62-046b-4075-97a2-ca284aba9093">
      <Text>Kendra looks at the empty passenger seat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f69192f3-8cba-4577-a5a2-2d25dd50191e">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8aaeff98-dd48-47b7-9486-8e6652cffad3">
      <Text>Daddy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e399111e-9a55-4132-965f-014ab5694df2">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ce19a684-795b-4682-b0ad-c08669963f88">
      <Text>Yeah.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c92f11a3-eac5-461a-a74a-a97265785d98">
      <Text>She has something to say. It will not come.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="23a05440-bd62-495a-8d87-edb585f6e917">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0423a25f-1790-4965-89e7-81641daab025">
      <Text>Nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a91ba351-1038-473e-9bea-9c88689b4131">
      <Text>Another beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d48cd48-69f9-41f8-9b7e-394f11adcfab">
      <Text>HOYT (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0c70ae4e-e82d-47e7-99bc-84b886b8e2b8">
      <Text>All right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9803569b-59bb-4d03-984d-3823c409dd46">
      <Text>The house fills the rearview mirror. On the dashboard, the call timer keeps running. Neither hangs up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="443d9aa6-8eea-4daf-8316-f618648af46f">
      <Text>The engine holds steady.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="06b650b5-e924-4b86-a002-4052c21a0661">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 4/8" Page="66" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="35bdee97-892f-4f5b-8e92-21b2282714a4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LAMBERT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0f04e86b-2e6d-40fd-b620-b7787467874d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NEWS ANCHOR">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5780f2fd-e72b-4e2f-a380-525467f737f7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7e37fd01-4f28-48da-8a4a-59a6c5cd982c"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. RUCKER HOUSE - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4232a096-07b7-5157-8037-008a9f958e07">
      <Text>SUPER: JULY 2026.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6e1e2067-7207-4442-a354-0ca15bde1818">
      <Text>Morning light in a wood-floored hallway. A television talks low somewhere ahead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1bd27337-e61a-423e-a652-53ddfc4a646e">
      <Text>MOVING along family photographs: Ty at sixteen in a varsity jacket, Rucker’s hand on his shoulder; the three of them in church clothes before a granite wall bearing nineteen names; Ty in a cap and gown, then in a suit beside a bride; finally TY, 28, broad as his father, holding a baby beside a gray-haired Rucker, one hand beneath the baby’s head.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5a0572ad-8046-4da0-b23a-31e7243a742a">
      <Text>The hallway opens onto the kitchen, where ELDON RUCKER, 58 — the same square build, his hair gray now — sits before a half-eaten breakfast, fork stopped above the plate as he watches television.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="168fa341-cd7a-5977-9be1-4053b5a3dae4">
      <Text>ON THE SCREEN — NEWS FOOTAGE: rainwater runs across the name PETER TILLMAN carved in granite.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="437156b6-c292-5bfd-aea0-73caa7ea3eec">
      <Text>A LOWER-THIRD beneath it: 34 DAYS TO EXECUTION — MAGNOLIA CONVICTION CHALLENGED.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e7052d69-5ef0-4a60-a7f5-17906f1b749f">
      <Text>NEWS ANCHOR (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1bac4f0-594b-4a4d-82b1-878be1991fd0">
      <Text>The Southern Mercy Defense Center filed an emergency petition this morning challenging Amos Hoyt’s conviction — claiming the fire that killed nineteen people at the Magnolia was never arson at all. The Attorney General’s office says the State stands by the conviction and will answer the petition in court. Hoyt is scheduled to die in thirty-four days.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fdc9478e-c9ee-40d1-98f4-ae31d78f5501">
      <Text>On the screen, archival: the 2016 courtroom. A younger Rucker on the stand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7f396175-e23f-4d39-8247-51ef061698ed">
      <Text>RUCKER (ON TV)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bea07417-ec3c-4176-9494-30e34ab5b23c">
      <Text>Incendiary. The fire was set.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="765e836f-b6b9-5bae-9cc7-d57d0f903edb">
      <Text>Rucker watches his ten-years-younger self say it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d2f7fe49-5238-42c8-bf65-e5f5cb26fb32">
      <Text>DONNA stands at the counter with a dish towel held motionless between her hands. She watches Rucker, not the television.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4adf9538-c8c5-4fd6-b3be-32ae509fc56b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a4e6653b-aa38-48a1-bdff-ec416cd47240">
      <Text>Never arson at all.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="80bea832-bf54-411a-b470-e290a0a93662">
      <Text>He says it flat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e92206a9-1348-4b7e-8ac2-9fccd81eb096">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="abaadec7-3eb7-544e-8db2-98223b5462f8">
      <Text>Eldon. You’ve been out six years. Let the office answer for the office.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="14e2bb2f-2bc0-41fb-b87a-f7b1e0a7e206">
      <Text>Rucker’s phone lights up and BUZZES against the counter, vibrating half an inch.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1aeeea73-7e89-49ea-b192-6970b05dc36c">
      <Text>CALLER ID: STATE FIRE MARSHAL.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d273acd2-330f-40e5-9bd2-6e698b1cea51">
      <Text>Rucker and Donna look at the phone. Donna turns to him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b3e88815-87b1-449b-a847-5fce4df3de25">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1658b22a-1ab0-4a1c-9d03-d1a5638d8e8a">
      <Text>You gonna answer it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e0a7515b-b025-465e-a026-98086203c85c">
      <Text>He picks it up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="243b5e98-b3ad-48bd-8d4e-206a4ce85594">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5404c895-06b3-4cfc-9976-0a25ad319ebf">
      <Text>Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1477e649-5134-4d2a-be6d-a480126f5d77">
      <Text>He listens. Donna watches him listen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8428c7e8-481a-4e4d-b340-de9d5946bc10">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="156dd257-9edc-4466-98ca-f34fb15681ec">
      <Text>Two o’clock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e2863ced-6912-4843-be08-4b1d09722a40">
      <Text>He sets the phone down. On the television, a weather map has replaced the Magnolia report.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="b9b3e2c6-3dfa-4836-8392-fe10dcb7592b">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="68" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LAMBERT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0bee0ddc-dce4-4ce5-b51e-24e0a7223cdb"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="86eabd49-21fb-43a4-adc8-9c89cd33dc45"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="578859a2-871d-4c0b-a8ad-a46ca1eb5a91"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4a8f0f5d-3657-4cfb-bac4-2cf3ca5b0398"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ATTORNEY GENERAL’S OFFICE - LAMBERT’S OFFICE - MONTGOMERY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0ea24075-bb36-49f9-8f01-7cfc4f242e02">
      <Text>Lambert’s office. DELL LAMBERT, 50s, Chief Deputy Attorney General — lean, close-barbered, a suit that fits — sits across from Rucker. Three State binders stacked between them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="81817cea-03ec-4b80-b44b-60f5e4a91961">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="935fae98-cb9b-46a8-a4e7-c2e539546aa6">
      <Text>Their petition says the Magnolia was never arson. The State wants the man who signed the report to answer it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bde84358-849f-4f5d-b878-6b58b709465e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="41e8a0d3-16fe-4f58-aa43-abb16e1f6363">
      <Text>Answer for it? I answered for it under oath ten years ago. I’ve been retired six years. Mercer has my old district.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ceaac726-4bc7-4032-be48-187ab04bc568">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4aedc5b2-9495-408a-ab2a-1ed3d75ae0bd">
      <Text>If the court grants a hearing, they’ll subpoena you. You’ll answer for that report under oath whether you take this commission or not.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9ba201e3-fdb4-42b5-bb48-5d2907a055e0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="81aa780f-6823-4b72-9dee-1e1822ad6705">
      <Text>You’re asking me to defend my own work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d50e3fe8-b2c8-4307-9fec-c23de248ccb1">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f77f05a9-1bcd-48ba-aba6-4b2a840de2a7">
      <Text>I’m asking you to find out whether it can be defended.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="130925f9-ed67-473c-a7f4-290b0afb9b85">
      <Text>Rucker looks at the binders but does not touch them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="93758629-0610-465d-8b53-58928cbb7455">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c6f42a1d-5f3e-4b05-b5ca-2f0841e4e281">
      <Text>What do they say lit it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b49d2f7e-cd95-40e3-ba1c-51a968e8fa15">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="003dbbfb-5b78-4fe2-b132-22905c03b20d">
      <Text>They don’t. That’s their point. The damage gets you to the foam corner and stops. No competent ignition source. Nothing scientific that makes it arson.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4b9b2dd7-561e-48f8-9ae3-2a10625c12bd">
      <Text>Rucker turns to Lambert now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b1c58922-654e-4809-aa10-14287eb0f9b1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e98c27d9-7a64-45fa-88e7-5f4abae06fcf">
      <Text>Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6b14397a-e0e2-4427-aa85-8c2807326c61">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c41c9be7-774d-4b5e-a400-087d7e38a59d">
      <Text>A man isn’t an ignition source.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ae25c79e-d58e-4e1e-930f-2de03375b321">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d4599dcd-bcb7-4b15-851d-61957f7a6ef1">
      <Text>He’s the man who struck it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2638328d-52fc-499f-9001-8c2f822519fd">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="60a96e52-f4eb-4320-8dde-7b0bb49075df">
      <Text>Only if somebody struck anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1ad36292-388b-4f38-8a3a-39165738c4d5">
      <Text>That stops Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5fb3f60a-9edc-4b77-9e18-7520e0df4120">
      <Text>Lambert lays a single-page commission on top of the binders.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="aa1cdb37-95c3-4a4e-9aa4-93950a966cff">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="69" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RECORDS CLERK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="8c7ced75-cbcc-4a08-aebb-37a93398e7ea"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COUNTY RECORDS ANNEX - MORNING</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ab7178fb-94d8-456d-85a1-ae66433029fe">
      <Text>A windowless government basement. A RECORDS CLERK, 50s, slides a sign-in log across the counter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8317c2f7-2a3f-429f-b1a0-2dfbe440dc9f">
      <Text>Rucker signs beneath the most recent entry. It is dated three weeks earlier: SOUTHERN MERCY DEFENSE CENTER — RECORDS REQUEST.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="11afc18d-c903-4224-b5e2-154acb3bc659">
      <Text>RECORDS CLERK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba410d72-647f-4314-8771-0083379471da">
      <Text>Ten years, nobody. Now it’s a popular file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="62cfdb95-4372-4b33-80fc-227157bcc89e">
      <Text>She wheels out a cart. Four boxes. MAGNOLIA — CASE — EVIDENCE — PHOTO.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="479bb135-1edc-4379-90e0-62e0b8bf4450">
      <Text>Rucker lays out the contact sheets, negative sleeves and original diagram. Through the loupe: Frames 54, 55 — the foam corner repeating. Then Frame 61. He stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ab003565-14ce-43ec-b53a-ef8f21292c2e">
      <Text>Frame 61 continues past the origin corner to the full west wall: high window, compressor, shelving, louvered door and foam rolls packed beneath them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ee7bf8c2-1221-4096-99be-8d92db012fc8">
      <Text>He traces the corresponding photo-log entry: 61 — WEST WALL, ORIGIN CONTEXT — then pulls the trial exhibit list. Nine photographs, all stopping at the foam corner. He fans them beside Frame 61; none holds the window, packed rolls, door and compressor together.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b6c5026e-c54e-49a5-8884-3a25fd5f6795">
      <Text>Rucker carries Frame 61 to the counter for a full-resolution scan.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="9c399e3e-acba-416c-a91c-b208718d28fd">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 7/8" Page="70" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5fa0e16d-fa87-4795-88df-7b9468c4d084"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5f290f8f-f1a6-4b6b-8a36-772573d7d175"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL - HALE RIVER FIELD OFFICE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9257f499-60e3-45b3-838d-1afbec3ea515">
      <Text>A state-issued TAHOE pulls into a row of spaces outside a low government building.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="94236dd3-804a-4a82-81ed-7f050c2cd617">
      <Text>DANNY MERCER, now 37, Deputy State Fire Marshal, gets out in his marshal’s windbreaker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9c7f31e5-a73f-4fd9-87ab-58d86d793e9e">
      <Text>TESS PRUITT, 24, wiry, hair pulled back, climbs out of the passenger side carrying a camera case.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2da2a5f8-d982-4dce-ac92-0ecd48d44514">
      <Text>RUCKER waits beside his Suburban with a folder under one arm.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f9fec36e-92c2-4eae-a461-e52e25139063">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eb84dc6d-4957-447e-8162-f2d3fe170d0e">
      <Text>Download the card before you get lunch. Wide shots first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d83a17a2-1d73-482a-89c9-ad30877deb7a">
      <Text>Pruitt heads toward the office.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0c3857b4-2380-4682-a3e0-8bc85ba8a177">
      <Text>Mercer stops in front of Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1e4ee95f-1ded-48ec-b3b7-cda07b82fcf5">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f93bc158-022f-44db-969f-bd16e122240a">
      <Text>Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5ef752a1-906f-428f-bf7d-bee3e2cc726b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="04fad834-b158-4337-896d-d1cc4bcda751">
      <Text>Deputy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b1c50d80-c5fb-4ddd-831d-22a1e54945eb">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="71d3d0b3-188e-4d23-aaf6-a073361b9f87">
      <Text>Six years. I had you on a lake somewhere.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="15b2f3d9-e533-490b-b7ca-52f2f74bd00f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="468c12a5-4d43-462e-b467-3086a9078b83">
      <Text>Donna had me painting the porch.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="29a87b9d-36db-4080-b167-f664ab293987">
      <Text>Mercer grins. Then his eyes find the folder, and the grin goes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0de04d21-8f6d-44fa-8312-f1ef1f46ade2">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0ca896b5-76c7-49de-a468-12f1c3b5ad95">
      <Text>But you didn’t drive an hour to show me paint.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="03977429-6947-4c77-ba63-ca1ea1ca7b35">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f00f7472-825c-485c-9701-2190e65f9852">
      <Text>Montgomery put me on Magnolia. Hoyt’s lawyers say my cause finding won’t hold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="78554875-40bb-4372-8a74-71aa69118925">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab773865-3a22-48b0-be5d-9c947178d86b">
      <Text>State wants you to defend it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="03f97387-3ddc-4959-b6a7-03c14725514e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fa8c35bd-9322-4ee6-be58-8cfaa459ce04">
      <Text>State wants to know whether it can be defended.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e2754a33-6fe6-4b82-80c3-5fe0ef4fbfa0">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b56f939e-e145-48fa-b61b-a5212d19bde5">
      <Text>And you came to me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff19d8f0-1618-4e53-b96e-c2e264e626c4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="98a5b7c2-96b8-4ede-98cc-7b594cc90e51">
      <Text>You made the photographic record.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ed55018f-352b-4ab1-bab7-34e3d74720ac">
      <Text>Rucker opens the folder against his forearm and removes an enlargement, folded once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="701c1045-2511-4ebb-bc8a-d5a8bc27d0a5">
      <Text>Mercer takes it. Looks a long time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="28ce4724-3456-44b8-90d7-87039d2c1195">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="330afd17-ebab-4e34-8df3-24a12bdb23d2">
      <Text>West wall. Edge of your origin coverage. Frame sixty-one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d02effc-6c50-41dc-a658-dcc2294dd925">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d87466d1-50ba-4978-9c1d-f16e2e7d6ed7">
      <Text>Sixty-one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0f3ef83c-79ef-4674-8351-50faff1323ec">
      <Text>He turns the photograph toward the daylight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="22f922d0-e47f-4632-8a07-8fdcbe7dcc14">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="588f891b-9176-4a0f-9397-bf942f576258">
      <Text>Look at the stock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1b863542-c75a-4f66-be63-548449842c93">
      <Text>Mercer studies the lower portion of the frame.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f09672a3-6392-482c-9a52-3a85b5c9b5fd">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91f6123a-ca9b-480a-9c82-07ae9a8fd8db">
      <Text>Packed beneath the west shelving. Rolls compressed together.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6dba55f7-4844-4c95-911c-f1fb58f33151">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="66ee0d69-5b90-4c37-b467-1004d6ee521c">
      <Text>Not lying open to the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="531a1a79-ad5b-441f-8839-4036d0100e94">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="249dcb1c-6eba-445c-9c45-b2b1c7d956c6">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cb5b365f-08fc-46bb-bb98-4fda8b946d37">
      <Text>Pruitt pauses at the office door. Mercer motions her inside without looking away from the photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a13a6827-1b95-41c4-87c9-5a7e70c603c8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c454ee1a-0453-4b06-997b-af1881e3b345">
      <Text>Did we write down how it was packed?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2ebea4ae-83d0-4707-8fb1-ac7118edaa90">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="246c633d-c0f0-4d29-9d84-d52509926904">
      <Text>We wrote foam stock. First fuel.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="55a92d90-fcb7-462f-8e58-4731d406f722">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9d90b9ad-af74-4279-a6d7-80d7ab31b5d6">
      <Text>That isn’t what I asked.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cd4f326d-928e-4a0c-814c-899ccbd0b4e0">
      <Text>Mercer looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0ff4eb5b-1c0f-45a4-a098-8551cf0c3329">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fda38c86-9f1b-47db-82c2-d17b77fd7bf8">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3bdfcf8f-09db-4756-be8c-c673305db431">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="93c48e53-dd07-4b3e-a311-4a0a76df2148">
      <Text>Hundred forty-two frames. The jury saw nine. Every one of them ended at the foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="37b1a1b1-81fc-40b9-bcc2-d1fd53e15d8e">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8852753b-3eac-47a5-ae79-e08f08524c65">
      <Text>You told me to go wide.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="28a02517-1479-44ca-8b5d-f75ecfd9bb0a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="069228bc-8a8a-40a1-bfc9-1b30f6f7119c">
      <Text>You did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="407d4d52-88f5-4cea-8cda-770f2ee9c71e">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d979b280-1b7b-45a6-bfa1-c00c582ad63b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6c57a558-db04-4bde-998e-1ebf04be6bb5">
      <Text>I chose the nine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2a107724-24be-4719-8a60-e210ecfe5ad3">
      <Text>Mercer looks back at Frame 61.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ed74c6c9-4a15-418c-98ad-6ca495c0fff8">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ea4d46b3-fcf8-4933-ac62-786391d6129a">
      <Text>What do you think this changes?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c03d9e52-718b-498c-a28f-434c97ee1089">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="50a0e888-5e0a-49f7-8c42-b2f6b0c5107c">
      <Text>I don’t know. I know we never asked what packed meant.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f2c20fec-3c64-43f6-aa5c-6c312b5e83a9">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da80977c-3b8d-45b3-8897-83ff9abb0d35">
      <Text>We were looking for what lit it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2e3fd0bf-8f68-490d-a609-2b834e74cc74">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6a5496cb-d44a-4d4b-8e31-8236f0e02830">
      <Text>We never found that either.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6f959dd8-ae62-4c84-bd9a-7cc8193c5036">
      <Text>That sits between them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5b35f13d-3ca9-47c8-8175-8aac05bfb8ba">
      <Text>Rucker takes the photograph and folds it back into the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca197bc0-ae4c-46cd-bb33-d387a8247303">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e43dd9ed-0860-472c-833e-3eb91ab4ca59">
      <Text>I need to see the room before it burned.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="12aaabc3-0739-4985-bf97-81d32eecdc1c">
      <Text>He gets into the Suburban and drives away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="95f6d474-b7c9-4760-a86e-2f489561c755">
      <Text>Mercer remains outside the field office, watching him go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="619f5873-d742-4801-90fb-a00927b15743">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="72" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. COBB HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1cfaf74f-1b76-40e6-82ac-8ec0cb0ca980">
      <Text>Rucker’s Suburban sits behind an aging pickup in the narrow drive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="586e925b-6e96-4011-8798-6fbaf0238427">
      <Text>Through the front window, Cobb sees Rucker coming up the walk. He looks toward a battered MAGNOLIA banker’s box already waiting beside his chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="87e89442-1b51-4e4f-9943-51959631232e">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 2/8" Page="73" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COBB">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bee316c8-bf90-4b60-b11f-091ffaa9092d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="aca8ba2d-e734-4d87-894d-88586236090b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7a3f48c5-12e6-4e1b-b776-ff58feb5f05d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COBB HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="788af01c-c717-4390-9703-ffcfe9c12797">
      <Text>The same room, twelve years older. The television is off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c6570913-8688-4764-8a9c-7e66a4c96417">
      <Text>Cobb opens the door before Rucker can knock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="33641ac1-f6b0-4810-a089-7c81e61d4556">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a0811d9c-5c1b-464d-864a-ad6651f65148">
      <Text>Saw the news.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="80ec5675-b2c7-4b17-aafc-45666c079f3f">
      <Text>He turns back into the room. Rucker follows him inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e2ec41e7-cfc1-4e33-991b-c4e4c361ba0c">
      <Text>MERLE COBB, seventies now and thinner, lowers into an old folding chair and wraps electrical tape around its split rubber foot. Rucker sits opposite, hat against one knee. Between them, a Magnolia banker’s box holds twelve years of paper Cobb never threw away.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4068df8e-db1c-40fa-9f41-0bba065529ce">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e2db9bd0-c814-4719-833a-006205c1c025">
      <Text>Lawyer said I could quit keeping all this after ten years.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1f0f4405-9fd0-4fc5-a4fb-fb8c3a2581bb">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="574207d3-cf6c-498d-9d11-5744778c32d5">
      <Text>But you didn’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="884d2208-f072-4523-903e-3a185c420c67">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bc1bec9c-961c-422b-a3f4-0f0601c5ed74">
      <Text>Every time I carried it toward the curb, somebody put the Magnolia back on television.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2271c608-fb0d-48cf-a5e1-6028f0d4ab6a">
      <Text>Rucker opens the box. Works carefully through the files.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e8de51aa-4ed0-473c-9c9c-7b47af294d57">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="258f0280-95c7-4450-bad9-bf056333af5c">
      <Text>I need everything from the renovation. What came in. Who supplied it. Where the crew stored it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9deb77aa-5d44-4ed2-84c6-4469695e0c88">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d564b93a-9a11-4b91-98c7-600dbd61cb8e">
      <Text>County had all that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f8cda7ea-3b74-4d15-8c8c-aeec367c953e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9dca267e-9dd8-4a6a-bbac-05f96887d8da">
      <Text>County had what it asked for.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cf6a03c9-fa76-475c-9638-6f6dc00cfec6">
      <Text>Cobb stops winding the tape.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="eaf1fac8-a456-446b-9786-0a912a383a19">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f9d1dd3e-54ac-424b-acec-ddef5a98807d">
      <Text>Last time you sat in that chair, you laid a picture of the chain between us and asked me about Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a1180b75-ef39-4c39-b13d-6e372b14854a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56f5127b-d4f6-41b7-998f-5429978de948">
      <Text>I remember.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7e52bb7d-e1e8-46f9-9690-1bebfa100a95">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="94b74a85-69b9-476e-8d3e-eac9de95962e">
      <Text>I knew who put it on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="80eb37f1-2fb6-472c-8a98-e75537ae0b00">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="77ea308b-e3a9-4639-91f0-bc71761bcf54">
      <Text>Who.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="318556f1-32f2-4259-b040-71a930fd19c0">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bc298a9a-d1e3-4baa-8c94-e37d07caaeeb">
      <Text>I told Pete to chain it after dark.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e14849a9-cd65-489b-b509-60d2afdf7799">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="81bb579e-2517-4a4a-bccc-7ee9863fef95">
      <Text>You told a jury you didn’t know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9603c6c5-221e-48a3-8cd3-6e68393a6d2f">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6355de7c-c545-4a23-812c-a3b03f7caeb0">
      <Text>Five people died against that door. Y’all came asking how Amos’s hands got on the lock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4f3ab8d0-0388-4d91-9220-997c5d4de4de">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5dbafe48-2521-4815-a505-00296a30c034">
      <Text>I asked who put it on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e00f9708-f46d-439c-9846-923a7a2d7c21">
      <Text>Cobb looks down at the taped chair foot.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6ea4206c-a0f9-4570-a646-629e4cd90aaa">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0c4d5edd-e5aa-4feb-b48a-f23aeb6cdc52">
      <Text>And I lied.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="90e0850c-a114-43e3-9724-ad733c2ba85a">
      <Text>Rucker opens his notebook to a clean page and slides it across with his pen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="54e470af-259a-449f-9ea8-2438fc99b84f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="863370b5-74f1-46c2-b43e-0e9778281ffd">
      <Text>Write what you told me. Then sign it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="85977a3c-a143-4af0-86a1-6ee6f8c3f25d">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="89fddd3d-b45c-44e2-b277-f5e81d8e94c5">
      <Text>You never asked me about the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fec639c6-af16-4b07-bad4-911ce646c1d0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="26c913ac-e245-4972-8699-430a1377dd0e">
      <Text>I’m asking now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="36412e24-ed20-43ad-ba5b-19001965a668">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d5c926be-1392-4218-8059-f3aa43f73544">
      <Text>Twelve years late.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d547b679-7d59-4ca9-92de-693ccf2aa910">
      <Text>Cobb takes the pen. Rucker returns to the box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1d583531-0d76-44af-8bc1-b39d2e52f768">
      <Text>Rucker finds a JULY 2014 insurance envelope containing room-by-room photographs, including the intact storeroom. He sets it beside Frame 61 — the room before and after. An </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">OPELIKA</Text>
      <Text> FOAM PRODUCTS invoice provides the product number and delivery count.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9f916fec-3f44-41ef-826c-49cef277f7f7">
      <Text>Cobb signs the notebook page. Rucker tears it out, folds it once and files it in the Magnolia box. Cobb tests the taped chair foot against the floor. It holds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1a6fb705-5ae7-42ab-aa16-6f4e59a39060">
      <Text>Rucker stands. At the door, he puts on his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b4dc493c-c1d5-4de1-9280-b86f6e43c0f0">
      <Text>COBB</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="844986d0-93de-4c69-b6c0-bf02dd3614db">
      <Text>You’d tell me. If this was going somewhere. You’d tell me before the television did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5ed79b59-60da-4bbd-ad71-db05cdd57215">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a8d85d4f-4bd4-4f5a-8869-f7720364f64c">
      <Text>I’d tell you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="68284167-2744-498f-8473-e1f1e0a53397">
      <Text>Cobb nods. Rucker carries the box outside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="be0c71f7-1781-4ed6-a189-de1fd9598794">
      <Text>Through the front window, Cobb folds the repaired chair and leans it against the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="56c33a3a-4b64-43f8-9bf8-573019e574a2">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 2/8" Page="75" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="74805792-dbcb-4de9-8498-7896e50fa5eb"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="323e787d-79ad-4591-9d99-303b6b1b6d08"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="892372b1-fa28-4b72-8d95-5ef51aff7595"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="05ad7a82-216a-4243-b2e1-195d3e0eacbd"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL - HALE RIVER FIELD OFFICE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d53cea9a-c8d6-4629-b31b-cc63341d03fd">
      <Text>An enlargement of FRAME 61 hangs above the desk, where Rucker compares it with Cobb’s photograph of the intact storeroom. The foam invoice lies beside his notebook.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="946ddcf4-c8e6-4857-96ea-7984778d0fe9">
      <Text>One knock, and the door opens. ADRIENNE VANCE, 40s — thin, short dark hair, an overfilled leather bag — enters carrying a photocopied records sheet. A capital post-conviction attorney with the Southern Mercy Defense Center.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d8a68f63-03f7-4cd1-91dc-809bb1b66e0b">
      <Text>Vance clocks the enlargement as she enters and sets the records sheet on Rucker’s desk. He does not offer a chair. She does not ask for one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2ffbcfc8-f6b4-4f4f-a5f5-21d3b8f1a259">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="41701619-df7d-4d84-a20f-436f2c9184c7">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker. Adrienne Vance. I represent Amos Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ccc1ea40-e3fc-461b-a51f-503e83910738">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="634cae7c-38c0-4614-862b-66dfd47d9c32">
      <Text>I know the name. Been arguing with it all week.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="42575496-56d1-4800-8f23-826f03020663">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4d12acf3-f130-4e5c-b498-835f8c8d664a">
      <Text>Good. Saves us ten minutes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e9e52c30-96b1-4af0-a3ef-e585a8c804b4">
      <Text>She taps the records sheet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9f2afd62-a4d0-4f35-9bbd-c36b41cc9317">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="779f44ef-baed-477f-b174-fa45750bf37b">
      <Text>Trial counsel received nine photographs. The county index lists a hundred forty-two. Wednesday, somebody working under your commission ordered Frame 61 at full resolution.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ebad302-e116-40e7-ad88-0dddeecc8324">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5b8d4f21-5227-4892-8a98-58b0b8dd5947">
      <Text>That a question?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="16e7399e-6c4a-435a-8122-e6ce27fac827">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8d4d63ed-1ec8-4bfa-8db7-07a39c835d23">
      <Text>No. Why sixty-one?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="15116f62-8e1b-411c-92c8-f3257805fd3f">
      <Text>Rucker crosses to the enlargement. His finger stops at the origin corner, then moves beyond it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b8e12857-fa37-4acb-90a8-72e432bdb68f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8875b689-77b7-45fa-b0b6-7a0646c78f45">
      <Text>The nine stop where the burning stopped. This one keeps going — west wall, window, glass beneath it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0e368d45-2738-4caf-9b2f-af47b8402bc5">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="724d550e-bc7a-4b3d-96dc-d2612c32f635">
      <Text>Move the origin?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fb1683a2-02c6-4017-834a-a0864d0a5296">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d895d4e4-64cd-49aa-bcb5-675bd6ecaee8">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3fba01e0-4432-495b-851b-db6804322334">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="66e014af-8b9f-4c06-bced-bff9bf59b8d1">
      <Text>Establish another cause?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9558df12-bb9f-43e0-b275-b92e7f911371">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="42996bb8-20a4-4451-b145-5c118889ed92">
      <Text>Not by itself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5dc339b9-109e-4a3e-b5e2-b78a3d0b0bf9">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="61c32a28-df27-4114-b395-5d11b322f5cc">
      <Text>Then—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dc86bf18-2458-4081-9392-f3adb578562b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="920388c8-7ece-49a1-8d57-4580199a0d18">
      <Text>It gives me the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c5ca025-cec6-44a0-afc7-85e2ee4ad6c3">
      <Text>That stops her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a85558af-f703-483d-a50a-944e6855a1e2">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8225fac4-f2c1-45d3-9caa-2cd1ec7631c7">
      <Text>Ten years ago, I showed a jury where the damage ended. Never showed ’em the room it ended in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="95901ad2-f24c-4d1e-bd03-90ba9cf504b8">
      <Text>Vance looks at Cobb’s insurance photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="257f969c-4fcf-4ac9-9414-28015f28886a">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f6ae547-4439-4616-945f-54921f7a9e40">
      <Text>Hoyt met his appointed lawyer four times before jury selection. The State made arson the predicate for nineteen capital counts. Cause fails, convictions fail.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e4cc4080-2180-40b6-9d2f-7afc4c879075">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="61b56f85-8642-4428-9f4d-2a3a72fd680f">
      <Text>A photograph doesn’t make a report wrong.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a26c6ae6-0ed9-431e-8ccc-0c9cd95e0518">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="20d46a33-b488-48a8-8057-e0915226971e">
      <Text>No competent ignition source does.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d13ac02e-f101-4ee6-9299-42cea66826e2">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bff1160b-d4ab-42ee-be4c-10b43eeefaa2">
      <Text>Your experts never stood in that room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c66e9fca-ffa1-47a1-a45e-30ea546e659c">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aa6961fb-9c41-4f22-b20b-3008734dc7ba">
      <Text>Neither did the jury.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bfffaa2a-1d00-451c-9e1e-9cc46f7fedf5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="40f1680f-8938-4080-aa50-6b9f22582bd2">
      <Text>Every frame was indexed. Trial counsel could’ve ordered them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="12213e1e-ae51-461f-8e72-fda93842b7b3">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a46d585-72fb-42d1-9d10-29a9a4ce0235">
      <Text>He could have. He didn’t. You want me to defend him, too?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f8574c28-e462-4fc8-8593-b18a37a3ba95">
      <Text>Rucker takes the enlargement down and lays it beside the insurance photograph.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24f055f6-5794-4011-adc1-9f3db1adcf30">
      <Text>Rucker holds her gaze. The drawl is gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f8ed09d2-1987-48ed-bf64-d047f222238f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ba57ed63-f47b-4191-9bc6-2fa5d9f1d073">
      <Text>I have not reached a conclusion.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e056afba-0050-4db7-abe1-d21618e24138">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2032510c-f2d8-4615-94e4-30f18d11980c">
      <Text>Then stop defending one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dd97c509-c174-44bd-b780-a5b3933af1a0">
      <Text>Silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="97df81e6-0fb1-447b-9662-a024b854f374">
      <Text>Vance finally takes the chair, the overfilled bag across her knees.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="761b6fac-af3b-4b77-9950-74acfbde8e6e">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a5eacc1-015c-4a35-9566-ed48842be4ef">
      <Text>My office gets a file when the appeals are gone and the warrant issues. That’s what we call enough time. The State answers in nine days. After that, Frame 61 becomes my exhibit and you become their witness against it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a73fd29d-3684-427a-a0a9-145c29091291">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bc7c83ae-5f1a-458f-be7d-d5fcca69ff4d">
      <Text>It goes with the evidence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8e8780be-0efd-4b84-9f67-0aed9f69f24f">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8e22f598-ce26-4605-94b9-7e825654e0e0">
      <Text>Into a State file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="921c6a96-4699-4113-883a-f926111d2318">
      <Text>She opens her bag and searches through the disorder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d21e1a04-1f21-4e2e-945b-9064ed05c11b">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d316ce9a-b839-472d-ac62-e363ea044872">
      <Text>I have four experts saying your cause won’t hold. The State will call every one of them paid. They attacked your cause. None tried to establish another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f112e1bc-8b0e-429a-8bb4-9164f8155dcb">
      <Text>She finds her card.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d0e27846-d472-451a-95f8-d1bd1d4ca338">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9cf46428-0a49-4139-b7b6-d8d58e7a7acf">
      <Text>They cannot say that about you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aaf973e6-226e-4172-a77e-5fca424fdbce">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7725e5d8-84be-4d9b-9693-02abba090c38">
      <Text>You came to make me your witness.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8dd5c27b-728d-4670-9200-d9365e064ac6">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7dc71d38-d0df-4daf-a1e9-a81bbaa718df">
      <Text>I came to ask you to defend your report.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0d7bd830-3565-469d-a172-36216afe6269">
      <Text>She places the card beside the foam invoice and stands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7e911082-3bd1-4433-8f50-bd803bf26c3e">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c3221ae0-3b8a-4215-9570-1da256d37b78">
      <Text>The court decides with whatever we manage to put in front of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e58ed1aa-0fd9-4373-a6bc-69d42eb1f2e3">
      <Text>Vance leaves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="897ac899-6611-440b-a825-625d6fb207d0">
      <Text>Rucker looks from her card to the intact storeroom, then to Frame 61 beside it —</Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft"> </Text>
      <Text>the same room after the fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="da939c2c-0a98-435a-bf34-078145d08b58">
      <SceneProperties Length="4 7/8" Page="78" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e0107dc5-e078-4a25-b224-76b584b606ce"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="OFFICER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="668cac53-0b93-4bec-85eb-21274ff78bc8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="adfd4939-b70e-4d92-818b-10bafc8a4a91"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SERGEANT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="68d6bc26-ec82-4385-b4b0-84e0cc82ef8b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="afddb8dd-a1aa-4b41-8099-cfc0d7b40845"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - VISITATION - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="29a6e4f5-d6e0-4e72-91aa-7bdd1a017cb5">
      <Text>A SERGEANT, 50s, runs the desk. He examines Vance’s credentials. At Rucker’s identification, he straightens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="93783924-b54e-494a-8cc8-f928f2ce4617">
      <Text>SERGEANT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6ecc0b25-160b-4a9b-afea-bf5edc026e3a">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker. My daddy rode an engine in Selma. He’d talk about you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9d2f6581-958c-44b0-b9fc-5b22dc78b384">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="653eabb8-80eb-4f5d-ae19-b897b06538f3">
      <Text>Appreciate that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="666366a5-5df4-412b-a5a8-f08576169520">
      <Text>Rucker empties his pockets into the tray. The sergeant returns his identification with both hands but slides Vance’s across the counter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4fb74819-c514-44b7-a175-921d6ce97055">
      <Text>The visitation booths have cloudy glass, palm marks at hand height. A cartoon-dog sticker clings to the middle pane, where Rucker sits with Vance behind him, legal pad open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ad05c163-10f7-4eb0-9c89-2d0da88a411b">
      <Text>The far door opens. AMOS HOYT, now in his 50s, leaner, his prison whites washed gray, stops at a painted line until the OFFICER nods him forward. He sits across from Rucker and studies him, telephone untouched.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="49d17d60-59b7-47e3-95fd-be91bd26d160">
      <Text>Rucker lifts his receiver and waits. Hoyt glances at Vance’s blank legal pad, then picks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="37fba4bb-172e-4f31-a1d8-c69d315cd474">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f84c8cd7-d560-4ad8-836e-9608dd71cb3b">
      <Text>You went gray.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f2a5898f-e237-48dd-a641-8a9c0a080ba6">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f62cfa7f-aef3-480d-b2e8-a43220103ed8">
      <Text>I did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="392a9a86-95e6-4623-8bf8-02ec1bb2d861">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="75f564a3-9466-4e1e-bf49-972d692d0952">
      <Text>It suit you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f9e29375-2a17-4670-bd75-ca94d0768fa9">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="104e1666-8823-4db6-a1e0-3f0425848a74">
      <Text>(to Rucker)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d03b389b-bba8-4978-9b18-aa0c7f224676">
      <Text>Amos agreed to answer your questions with me present—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb6877c5-a215-437c-893a-8c9aa57b7a58">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="15e13b06-543b-4f24-bcff-85706b1ac14a">
      <Text>I can tell him what I agreed to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9a17eaa4-194b-4246-bdeb-ba6bddf10b06">
      <Text>Vance stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6fa1cdf9-500b-4b19-a9bb-0eea7e8f7cbc">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4ee6c07e-d7ea-4a32-a055-7104beb60342">
      <Text>(to Rucker)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f8d231de-db59-4d86-9025-08107cadc71c">
      <Text>I agreed. Go on, then.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="285e8956-84f3-4b69-b347-84db35770e8b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b35da631-9322-47af-a978-1504fc88c3a1">
      <Text>I need the storeroom. How the foam was packed that Friday. You’re the only man left who stood in that room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="297ae1a3-6a44-479a-aa93-330ecd47d609">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="922ca0d1-5c72-4e68-baa0-50488a309ff9">
      <Text>I know what you need. She told me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c2990e60-28a6-489f-afff-81aa060e51b2">
      <Text>Hoyt sits back. Studies him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a733a08c-d9d5-467e-86ba-d8e2b2ebeda5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cde5edf7-195a-4744-98a5-d9be85b08f24">
      <Text>Twelve years, you don’t come once. Don’t ask one more question. Now the man who put me here needs my memory to check his work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f9274a88-02be-4b5b-ab6b-cb46556d76e0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bcf76ce2-6f8d-46fb-b770-dde5fd029be7">
      <Text>I do.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="addb2aa1-c271-430f-b816-80f7d1741e39">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b36045cc-3464-476f-8079-33314d625a0d">
      <Text>Nineteen people, Marshal. You don’t seem tore up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="9548013e-e1aa-4527-8410-e8882da05e59">
      <Text>Rucker recognizes his own words. Hoyt lets him sit with them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="32c4cd15-573c-400c-a017-0c5b88d7e578">
      <Text>Rucker sets the Frame 61 enlargement against the glass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b9712ac8-ecf1-4f93-8016-02f25d18cf9e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="930b833e-23c2-4160-8732-e5a7891f445a">
      <Text>This is the room. This is what I reduced it to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a23bb4c5-9deb-42d3-9188-426d34c9c093">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d1d82971-6f16-465c-8f15-5106848137aa">
      <Text>You ever charge anybody with those other four fires? Anybody ever stand up in a courtroom for those?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="279dcc98-1b59-4902-b4b8-fed6ba4f93ae">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="05748ec5-798f-473b-8693-cdaa542125a4">
      <Text>No. They stopped six weeks before the Magnolia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="35770ba2-448f-4a45-a736-4fef2c3ff0d5">
      <Text>Hoyt’s expression changes. Rucker lowers the photograph and holds an old legal-pad sheet to the glass — dates in a column.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3345f532-c997-4fc8-92b8-dd4e25db4901">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f7f29253-33f0-444f-b134-4f4319f1cb1b">
      <Text>The county’s fires, in order, and the weeks between them. I wrote it the summer we arrested you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="42914ff4-f5e9-4a5b-ab32-2186947c2bf6">
      <Text>Hoyt reads the page. Reads it again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f2a110b9-390d-4cf2-bf40-451e6c13a43e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0a233eb8-3f3a-44f1-b5c3-311fccbb0469">
      <Text>You wrote this when.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="06bbe8b8-56ea-4b8d-abc3-84647e34b39a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ec8edd6a-b9c7-45bf-989c-878f3475c6d0">
      <Text>Before the trial.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bb48f1df-4de0-4fc0-ad4d-31a4e72a8516">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a23ed497-a09e-4d51-8869-190ea4ccd277">
      <Text>Twelve years. And it was in your desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="de6a88cf-ccf5-4b78-b005-22e13b090de7">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32d4b653-add1-4cce-8122-3e467922701e">
      <Text>It was in the file. It’s been in the file the whole—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fc0a6ad1-1894-48c3-892f-4ce47c0d4ef6">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="75ab03ed-b0b6-4619-9a6f-ac490f412a33">
      <Text>In the FILE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11899294-566d-4906-a805-c95e0630cd17">
      <Text>Hoyt grips the receiver.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8931c852-e973-43f4-a0f8-a319a6f9ed4f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="80216386-a89f-4e56-ab1a-f1dbcd16e603">
      <Text>You know what I had in my file? Chaplain kept me a list. Who got buried when. Deena went on a Thursday. I know the hymn they—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0a89e2ca-f14a-4d55-a39a-9e737268ff11">
      <Text>He stops. Puts the receiver flat on the counter. His breathing settles. He picks it up again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="62034502-90e2-4c92-9de8-23e6b8859068">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8a26f882-2255-4be9-a5ab-3d25b36d144e">
      <Text>My girl was sixteen when they took me out my yard. She’s a grown woman now. When that date comes, the one thing the State of Alabama hands her is a piece of paper says her daddy burned nineteen people alive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b24d2e0c-0cc5-4ad3-9712-ea000576bd02">
      <Text>He looks at Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1727ddf3-f43b-458e-a662-7d26f02de5b2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9e7d2d35-aae6-40ac-9a60-d1f014dcda90">
      <Text>That paper outlives me. You’re the one man whose name can fix it. That’s the only reason I’m holding this phone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0a99435c-c21d-4c2f-b42d-0a1cc3d5b074">
      <Text>A beat. Rucker takes up his pen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="361e4023-28b3-4468-b400-29c63561517e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="642ee219-3fc9-418c-8c06-bc730e5e40d2">
      <Text>The foam. That Friday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d259d313-40c0-41bf-88ff-d6953de4fd8e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="deae7226-06d4-4803-8ff9-0085cf03cde5">
      <Text>It was a storeroom twelve years ago, Marshal. I couldn’t tell you what I ate Tuesday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7ca6d261-42dc-4ac9-88d5-c4adbe1fe057">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0fab2f5c-29f1-41bd-ab5b-eb31fd0ffead">
      <Text>Don’t try to remember it. Stand in it. You come in off the rear hall. The cooler’s at your back. What’s under the west shelves?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4bda6e81-3e45-46fb-a386-c7b2e767e237">
      <Text>Hoyt looks at him. Then closes his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cd2698db-48f6-44e2-a499-381f4f8206ce">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8d036bdf-6099-497d-8792-a777e02cea0f">
      <Text>Door swings left. Mop sink... crates...</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e08351b4-7925-4cac-a5de-a485e0b79e4a">
      <Text>His head moves slightly, walking it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="75d3db24-40ee-46c6-b210-a49198d23060">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="157de727-1f03-4fa9-b92e-bb7add860f0b">
      <Text>Foam. Rolled tight. Three deep under the west-wall shelves. Crew kept bringing more till there wasn’t room to walk straight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0aab9cbf-3fa6-4194-b3a1-1c9881db97c9">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b846516c-4992-4527-b0d5-43a92182efe8">
      <Text>Anybody open a roll? Move the stack?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8ecba96f-4a30-4dc5-a513-4aacbeea1ef8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="c8818264-cab5-4c0d-816a-3442f53f82e1">
      <Text>(eyes still closed)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dd8f8436-d343-4c3c-b63b-65464530e62f">
      <Text>Not while I was there. Stacked it and left it packed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0c11fda4-d979-4268-b818-15ff033010e8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="18f02ae2-9df8-472f-b69e-261834fea98f">
      <Text>The jug on the sill.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="12cf973d-313b-4b6b-9eef-47772ad5b2b8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d55ecc3d-24ea-4160-83b5-e02968193fa1">
      <Text>Crew was about to kick it over. I set it up there myself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9c66b280-a2da-4f14-9025-4c6ce6f5e155">
      <Text>He opens his eyes. Rucker writes. Hoyt watches the pen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9cbe5a4a-7486-4998-920c-402f394f0153">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3e629f20-939d-443f-b4db-9b11594585f3">
      <Text>You writing it down again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="49126a67-e0c1-4d3c-b280-ce3cbe8abc0c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="10e80905-5026-4af4-aee0-c2dee2454fa5">
      <Text>I’m writing it all down again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="95a4544f-8b24-42a5-9bfa-dd03f193232f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0957abc6-a0a7-4d15-8b71-86a3035410f5">
      <Text>Say you find it. Say the report’s wrong and you say so out loud. What does the State do to you?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89d1716c-7fe3-4f6a-881f-668fa1522520">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="881232cd-7f52-43e8-9df6-2fa812868a81">
      <Text>Nothing. There’s no law for being wrong.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2e6cc83e-847c-44e5-ad38-a94390bc6868">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1527f033-c6c6-4736-ba4f-c75f0b1b45bb">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a10ffef7-069a-49dd-b2a9-640de5cfbc7a">
      <Text>No law for you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7ded9b64-b7b4-5495-bfe2-e6ebe101c875">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="eba9767c-5779-53ae-afd3-7c6d4f8f7ec2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="58a6f8e4-0b51-5073-99e7-647cde67a28d">
      <Text>You had a Black man with keys and a grudge. That was room enough.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b8241191-7502-4923-bb0d-15a45f9ccfdc">
      <Text>Hoyt leans closer to the glass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="899a2460-e40b-4a73-8e94-1d3cf03bd0f9">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3c580f30-f04f-4c28-9e1a-47a6952aa51a">
      <Text>Then here’s mine. Whatever you find, put your name on it. In writing. Send it to Montgomery — not to her, not into another file. Make the State receive it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="73a17c39-4494-4dc6-82a7-eb023a9e0340">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="262293a4-0f11-4ce3-a627-e2fb27a8c111">
      <Text>Amos — if he reports doubt before he has the answer, Montgomery ends his commission and your date doesn’t move. I don’t need you innocent. I need the cause to fail. That’s what moves a date.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b0641f20-9657-4867-9235-81849c0dbbc1">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="33b6c56e-bc6f-4164-83a4-d6adf7a04c01">
      <Text>(to Rucker)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9b9c3216-f8ca-4e51-957e-4cd7f5a2141f">
      <Text>Then you don’t stop till you got the answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="628c6f34-5640-457a-8a6f-67481772bfdd">
      <Text>He looks directly at Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a7cd7ff8-47d3-4e8c-8e27-ee566e85ea3e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="90f7493b-4b18-4731-8152-ed7add9f1f17">
      <Text>I’m done trusting what stays in the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="724fbf5d-e38f-40e2-aa27-01d38fefb663">
      <Text>The officer checks the clock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1de138db-a167-44f2-b323-8b8a80eafe04">
      <Text>OFFICER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2b845eac-6f22-490b-a1f4-a1ce4f170f0b">
      <Text>Time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cc6e25dd-b5ea-477b-ac16-0f41641554e3">
      <Text>Hoyt stands before Rucker can answer, returns the receiver to its cradle, looks at Rucker one final time, and walks to the door without looking back. Rucker remains seated, holding his receiver.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="1a027bdb-b75a-430a-8a12-12b997a8f229">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 4/8" Page="83" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="67d6aeb2-79f4-4a23-acd3-df9c94c067c3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2b0d2f15-3864-4bbe-bfba-e43a78264321"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="TIER OFFICER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="3c6647f6-30ac-45ab-b84d-3e47ae22cea8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - VISITATION - ANOTHER DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b162ec97-7f7f-4668-a9ab-375a1a790262">
      <Text>A TIER OFFICER walks Hoyt down the corridor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="31910eb8-be68-44e1-814e-a13c79bebd8c">
      <Text>TIER OFFICER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="15134867-f330-4035-b69b-140aad21dbb5">
      <Text>Visit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f177bf3c-3a2c-48ae-9d90-62f3556992b7">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cf081b59-12d1-4181-a6b0-0fc3d409de4b">
      <Text>Ain’t Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="24c4f9a0-5da2-4563-9c64-5ab362f7c131">
      <Text>TIER OFFICER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d83302f4-0d38-4288-a9a3-b0cb0f57a523">
      <Text>Ain’t legal, neither.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c5218997-db97-48c1-b2e5-baf6386761f4">
      <Text>Hoyt comes through the far door, stops at the painted line — and sees who is on the other side of the glass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5a758248-f211-4b94-ade4-76f8f9924996">
      <Text>KENDRA HOYT, 28, tall and long-limbed, sits with her hair pulled back. A bag rests in her lap beneath both hands. She does not move. The officer nods. Hoyt crosses to the booth and sits. He lifts his receiver before Kendra reaches for hers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6a44c259-b2d6-4f79-82d7-7f23fa96c0da">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="27c0f11b-a707-464e-ae85-08eee9345050">
      <Text>Hey, Daddy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="52c707a0-86d9-4cc4-ba5f-013665d95cc2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c8db1fab-72ef-4946-8e3b-a760007d8a9f">
      <Text>Hey, baby.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1ca31026-be00-4605-8fe1-d60a79d984e6">
      <Text>Neither of them says anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="06326bd2-c415-4766-8f29-1f6c86224ca0">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="17db98a1-b239-40ed-9cf5-8cfba1e413bc">
      <Text>You look — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ef08715c-4bff-402e-a913-2a0dcd5909db">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="36022e11-2e0b-4f36-8059-923e3d869b4c">
      <Text>Old?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ed245eab-6dc7-4c95-b570-56eaacd8d024">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d4de3d19-90d6-4064-98ec-b767899b3d49">
      <Text>I was going to say tall. You been getting taller?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="06ceb4ba-fa74-4411-b0b0-9510216de236">
      <Text>She laughs — quick, before she can stop it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="11c889ce-2fdc-48fe-85a6-0562a4a71ccc">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="449442cc-d367-425c-a685-be484d754885">
      <Text>I’m the same size I was at sixteen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cc68fa89-48cc-4990-991b-801b279ee9af">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="830f0562-1818-43d9-b5ab-0b095962a757">
      <Text>Well. Everything else in here shrunk, then.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cb0297fc-0709-4765-8f95-6db1b6a25bbf">
      <Text>She looks at him through the glass. The gray. The lean.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="68fa68d4-04c5-49bd-99e2-0d18ffdab59c">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8c9ee020-49a8-45f3-879a-c794c7d91590">
      <Text>My car’s making a noise.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89ab0df4-ac6b-4ce2-9ef8-c55aed590686">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83e8dd84-1038-4d5e-bbb1-5782a61fe9a9">
      <Text>What kind of noise.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5892c697-ed18-4d82-81f1-caa88ad489b8">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74a66fa9-f59f-4323-b6e1-73f30fa8a52a">
      <Text>Front end. Left turns. Man at the tire place says it isn’t the brakes, which is about all he told me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="86963e0f-ab5a-49c7-b117-1121cae578ba">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="733dee03-e147-48c4-af07-88448f543af4">
      <Text>Clicking or grinding?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97b3b925-f30b-45e2-bf86-3e336391db53">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="08f5973f-471c-495e-a1f0-210ebe2294ef">
      <Text>Clicking. Like cards in spokes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5b3b1dd2-c1f2-433b-8605-9213c2e835c7">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="498aa8c0-5018-4cf1-ab64-67b758e7927e">
      <Text>That’s your CV axle. Outer joint. Part’s about a hundred and twenty. Anybody quotes you four hundred, you get up and walk out of there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8d51011d-308a-4a4a-8b26-1b52e39d8a25">
      <Text>She writes it on the back of an envelope from her bag. He watches her write it. His eyes stay on the envelope after she’s done.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8782084c-8163-4a24-a3d5-a53a569acf09">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6e46003e-0950-4aa0-bf4b-2a15155e6638">
      <Text>Okay. Axle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cae54ce6-683c-4efe-adc5-52fa7b3c59d9">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e3cf4742-5af8-4158-89d0-d29391f0266b">
      <Text>CV axle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="22c2a2a0-a93a-4fbf-b9b9-36e5f91e716d">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="227fad24-0b0c-4ff9-b13a-a363c17b96eb">
      <Text>CV axle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0fc731ac-7fde-46ed-ae6c-5d60eda01530">
      <Text>She puts the envelope away. Takes a breath.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2364a7ef-6e0a-48cd-890e-207a4362ee89">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="aec0ea7f-ae37-488a-956f-780cede983a9">
      <Text>They’re talking about you again. The lawyer lady, and now they’re saying some state man’s been — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fc1d421f-3b6e-45ec-80ea-ea7eb2bf2216">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a5244640-e3b8-4d25-8c9b-c7f505dee00f">
      <Text>Don’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b4dfafd7-0d42-4aa8-90d1-e386b072c258">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2d55d97b-6c9c-48e1-bf95-eca5dd730da4">
      <Text>Daddy — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="02ae4e27-53a3-40f2-bbec-d8a42c29593f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8cfebcef-f195-4cf8-abac-e6285a5b0e45">
      <Text>Kendra. Don’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7bbd5b27-3a1b-477e-815a-d3241ebff0fe">
      <Text>She looks at the glass between them. Then straight at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca092651-0075-4178-a729-6ef4e999d43f">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bcbfa3cc-c5fd-4b65-81d3-f15762732a6b">
      <Text>You don’t get to tell me that. You don’t get to — I drive four hours and you get to say don’t?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="44b92f03-8df3-4fb1-8e68-0e07f3c3c064">
      <Text>He stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="50f2b72a-9aa9-4f24-bee5-ff83e2a7103e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="9a966369-c871-408c-8f30-1ae268f9f388">
      <Text>(quiet)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5151d447-f8c2-4b3b-8071-40df34a63f41">
      <Text>No. I guess I don’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="16e3acee-8290-4e19-abf0-2a7e41d376d0">
      <Text>She puts her hand flat on her bag.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="48fa905c-b030-47bb-ad11-f20a489c1550">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c3eb6e2-8c76-4dfa-a3fb-9f9562653492">
      <Text>I’ll come Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="068f8a5b-6472-40d7-85b9-85fb06c0848c">
      <Text>He doesn’t answer that. She watches him not answer it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="233fe632-e018-4e06-a1fb-cc3d19feafa4">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0f328da2-6ff3-4a69-8e68-5a0a0daf343b">
      <Text>I’ll come Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="25ed0b50-4d8e-4027-9411-f5a83c85d469">
      <Text>Firmer. Hoyt nods once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="74d13459-5d81-42ae-9027-d0d6f56af9e5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ef13f2b8-75b7-4e18-b17c-23424792aaf1">
      <Text>Write me what the mechanic says.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="634baa32-5dce-4a7d-9bb0-99c7b64cf1fc">
      <Text>She’s the one who hangs up first. He sits there a moment with the phone still at his ear.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="dcc4022d-7e6c-4e5b-9226-b303ee1bd9c4">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="86" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LAMBERT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="23f83c09-dfab-4571-8686-f49498df0e59"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a5452852-10db-42ec-be5f-7f69b4c3d500"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fdbede36-9a07-4168-a934-f2871c1b285a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. ATTORNEY GENERAL’S OFFICE - MONTGOMERY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="76044fcb-4610-4da5-bed8-24cc338225b7">
      <Text>A conference table large enough for thirty. Twenty-eight chairs empty. Lambert reads Rucker’s three-page memo twice, aligns it and looks across at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="57c8c3b6-84a1-4441-b79c-584c12d9d780">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2749cf16-854c-4261-8097-20c519e7f3cb">
      <Text>Who else has seen this memo?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9de3aa01-cb29-4f73-b6ad-e83052af35b3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7067aa46-d07e-4587-ac66-989fa7bdaf77">
      <Text>Nobody.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8ca25683-902f-4ee8-92d2-6149eb33a918">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5542782b-dbe6-41e5-8090-21d0ca7a1d21">
      <Text>Ms. Vance?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c9315e64-e427-4223-be13-7203f6730dfa">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da9fb933-31f6-4b75-81f4-f90c97ac4210">
      <Text>She knows the questions. She hasn’t seen what I wrote.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ef5e507a-76a6-43e0-aaf3-aec898da781f">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5bb2985b-a274-4422-a8e5-55b85ebbb2c3">
      <Text>Hoyt?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff90a48c-6513-4d02-a8d4-023b0e14c782">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="42cca915-eba2-42e8-b1b8-5fc155b7489f">
      <Text>He supplied one of the facts.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="04feebf5-ca55-4ea6-815e-40ef385be940">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="57d8a0bb-1002-41fb-b46a-ffbe930886a9">
      <Text>The packed foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a87ffe2b-c5b9-42c9-8eb1-68dcd8389bff">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b7e4d8bf-a11d-41fc-a9d4-07b4154b0403">
      <Text>Yes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3d09a336-a48e-4f74-8657-61c1b7271cc4">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="77adae13-9d4b-4114-972a-ab6baaffa227">
      <Text>This office hired you as its expert. You’re generating material for the defense.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0deb448a-ffab-46a4-8e98-71b4a24fdf04">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1a8f3a71-3be5-4dd4-86cd-3bdf75039e37">
      <Text>My client’s the State of Alabama.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4de30e55-4615-4ce7-a20f-62b4ce70d840">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a4c61782-ca1f-409f-9176-0b4c26a7247e">
      <Text>That’s what I said.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="197e7fb2-c752-4baf-b29d-8bbf50f022d2">
      <Text>Lambert places one finger on the memo.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2b6b5ae0-e83a-4f15-8579-88e21d1c4309">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3f4315cd-5414-454f-a967-6600c4b0df11">
      <Text>That’s something, Eldon. It isn’t cause. And it comes twelve years late, through a door this office paid to open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="941e956c-a617-56d6-8d4b-84a7c9ff3e23">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e21c5e9-222c-58e8-9692-70416cf2709c">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ec7fe66a-5244-523a-b18e-62406055c10f">
      <Text>If this office calls its own cause finding unreliable, every capital lawyer in this state asks what else we certified on less.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e1f720d1-71f0-46bc-8d4c-66bd27cfbf75">
      <Text>Lambert slides a one-page termination notice across the table. Rucker reads it without picking it up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7d19a5bb-4db1-46c7-927b-5f51cf488d15">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cadaedc0-6cfe-4d02-8273-7bab3c96c30f">
      <Text>Your retention and commission end today. Everything generated under them belongs to this office. Before you use those notes anywhere else, talk to a lawyer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2b16d214-2e55-45a8-abf9-58158fbc36c0">
      <Text>Rucker closes the notebook and keeps his hand on it. Lambert makes no move to take it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ab217c5-55be-4a29-a26e-70ccddc36e32">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c15bd273-3524-441e-94d0-a4c13ad304de">
      <Text>The execution date.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="28f27af9-1501-40ef-8206-ad62910ed102">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0677b540-0297-4f89-b23e-25a55aea24a6">
      <Text>Your memo says more work is needed. It does not say Hoyt didn’t light it. Nothing in here stops the date.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2e639907-e9e3-4333-8c7c-bb97b9b3f9f3">
      <Text>Rucker picks up the termination notice and signs the acknowledgment at the bottom. He puts on his hat, takes his notebook and walks to the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aa9f59bb-345c-4a69-b62d-57b67cb3dadf">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fa9ca49f-db21-432c-95e5-3e2466115d42">
      <Text>You want my advice—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="322b272d-afd2-4433-9e39-608340327c31">
      <Text>Rucker stops and looks back. Lambert holds his gaze.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d5662c7d-17c7-4366-8ae9-19662a19f417">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="84bb4d7a-79c4-4dee-891f-30be616435e3">
      <Text>No. You don’t.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="61ee3586-906f-4889-bb94-2966f766e58b">
      <Text>Rucker leaves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="aa6d4f9b-595d-4015-908f-009de6c32f23">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 2/8" Page="87" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0d33c1ab-0de5-4c07-ae91-4e0f5dbb407f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bc415d9f-1ca9-455c-989e-1740ee8080b0"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0b030f28-a32e-4fe3-a63f-1d07c6fb62fa"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. STATE FIRE MARSHAL - HALE RIVER FIELD OFFICE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="55180c8e-93f8-4afb-beb1-4aec4a07ebb1">
      <Text>MERCER crosses the bay toward the office. His phone rings. He answers on the move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca41f63d-df33-4bc8-8fa5-62bb53b67894">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="caf0f8e3-bd0c-4487-b858-78bb153d3b87">
      <Text>Mercer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="830fc2c2-c28b-411b-b923-40b2a503a46e">
      <Text>RUCKER (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2a0aa7ab-4089-41aa-85bd-6185cfc0c328">
      <Text>Montgomery cut me loose.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Shot" id="c3257f62-2118-4883-b162-17449679118e">
      <Text>INTERCUT BETWEEN RUCKER AND MERCER.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e8049319-6018-4332-801e-7f37ad5e2cba">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5331b50e-1470-4f6b-b0d0-a71d5d2616d7">
      <Text>I heard.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d736c4c7-1133-4621-99f9-b5f80b86a90b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="481b4b99-69b7-4a09-88d2-126131fc06e0">
      <Text>Paper’s taken us as far as it can. It gets us to the foam and stops. I need to know if a flame buried in a tight roll can stay alive where nobody sees it — then open up hours later and take the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="55687886-ed04-4348-83be-c9115e90a955">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="10ed5b85-2d02-49cb-bc05-3066210242f1">
      <Text>You want to burn a sample.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7e050218-3ffc-4b5d-b333-ccd79216b247">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d12e06dd-50e9-4b02-a6cc-72b61751b67e">
      <Text>A sample won’t tell me what the room does. We build the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d8ad8e0a-2796-42f9-9285-33aa046d7409">
      <Text>Mercer stops in the bay.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7f55758f-4da4-4c17-a32c-6f793241e5dc">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8ef65b1a-a63f-4348-a5a8-618512df9d77">
      <Text>Build it. The storeroom.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="637e3ae8-d867-4ac8-9f00-c749819f63bf">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2daeaf21-aaf2-42c2-b0d7-0a798415d9da">
      <Text>Same walls. Same window. Same foam where the foam was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="18d7e1d0-35a2-4171-8b66-64dc3a6dd254">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1b2d0092-11ac-4fa7-a66c-83d483a4215e">
      <Text>Eldon, that’s a structure. Framing, rock, shelving loaded the way it was loaded. Then it sits till it’s the Magnolia and not a shed that smells like new lumber. You get one burn. It goes sideways, you’re framing it again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4c557a41-d49b-42f9-a4ef-261e974d4bbd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="58dea11e-e199-46e3-a9f0-200226a0e037">
      <Text>How long.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="18bdec5e-88d4-4fff-b890-c216a1893f45">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="508cf509-d9a3-4e4a-b5bd-3b3fcfdb399d">
      <Text>Done where it holds up in a courtroom? Months.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8660dbd5-8a36-4170-a171-a8ce2456a2c5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6977d3b1-02f0-4610-81ae-92e59bdb36d2">
      <Text>He doesn’t have months.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="20cd443f-bed2-4eb0-aa7c-ccc8420bfaf8">
      <Text>Outside the Attorney General’s office, Rucker looks back at the building that just took his authority.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="865acb9b-2421-4a12-8102-de43915404fa">
      <Text>At the district bay, Mercer unlocks a metal records cabinet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="084557a4-25de-4f31-b1b2-8175bdc03e11">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b40dddfe-0b00-48a1-83ed-e2742877c056">
      <Text>You kept your scene book.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="61033bd2-e427-4c20-93c9-ea9c94ea6a19">
      <Text>Mercer pulls out the worn MAGNOLIA SCENE BOOK. Opens it across a worktable: measurements, diagrams, shelf runs, window height.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="19e4005c-8ffa-4230-93df-38980811ec55">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6ca2bbc7-40e0-48a1-b74c-91d2aaada362">
      <Text>Every measurement. Walls, openings, sill height, shelf runs. All of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="64a41b75-9532-4d79-9f21-41c48c50b8e4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="30152336-fd13-416e-aa3a-f645e7fc9b4c">
      <Text>I need a site and a crew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="347d5f1f-3050-478c-8160-441b94073666">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3f3ea3ba-6fb6-416d-a47f-9ae20500f91b">
      <Text>I can get you the pad, the crew and the cameras. County money can’t touch the materials.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="55c4bbc4-15d8-4648-ab0f-d6247b77afb5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5411e8bf-02c8-4ca2-b5ac-cc766736c653">
      <Text>Send me the list.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6ebb958a-396d-4e43-9030-6ebc96bd8e51">
      <Text>Mercer takes a COUNTY LIVE-FIRE TEST application from a rack beside the worktable and lays it next to the scene book.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e52ada04-615e-42d8-85fa-fce3700a1b54">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a3be6bcb-870a-44b1-bf5b-17dd1250f2a5">
      <Text>County training site. I can carry it as a live-fire test. My name on the authorization.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="01984e8a-f232-42f9-ba2d-472154548a78">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="899e1928-3d94-463d-a6e0-a4601dfe5636">
      <Text>They cut my authority, Danny.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ab2d2e4c-5443-4907-9d1c-a9c07b0c0e6b">
      <Text>Mercer looks at the blank signature line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="609997ec-df4d-47e9-8e35-fac451e9d91d">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="72d5cffd-f07d-4b4b-8d2b-7ed9da2f1b32">
      <Text>They didn’t cut mine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="3f544207-bdf5-4685-b18a-81edbc985c9e">
      <Text>BACK WITH RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="099a8b77-07aa-498c-9ed2-c65f4f493bff">
      <Text>Rucker ends the call. Finds Vance’s card tucked into the notebook and dials.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5af0e354-f31e-4907-9e9d-7c3083930ad2">
      <Text>VANCE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9f6f8d06-e704-487c-870e-f85044da65c3">
      <Text>Vance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="274c5834-68d3-42f8-877d-408a17ce5a69">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0d1c798c-d14d-4178-9bf4-790788691067">
      <Text>Montgomery cut me loose.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e73cd3c6-a1b9-4ddc-81ad-f66790b4896a">
      <Text>VANCE (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2b005a78-a2d7-4ecb-b70e-88364ba132f6">
      <Text>Then what do you need?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc65f341-ed25-4527-8666-db4b6ee34bd8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eb0d60a6-9eb9-43b4-a4c5-c8eb22c29bfa">
      <Text>Find Lacey Stroud.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fab5bf17-cd13-46bd-8c79-d6dff4e7037a">
      <Text>Rucker closes the notebook and gets into the Suburban.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="3a2158de-f29c-4526-93f5-e3c52fafa66c">
      <SceneProperties Length="2 1/8" Page="90" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LACEY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="dd3a36e6-a3c5-4e72-93ff-6869e59151b6"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="fabece5d-3215-4b6a-b242-b09e282a07fc"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6aeff304-06db-47e2-9c1f-046ddcf948f6"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. DOLLAR GENERAL - REAR LOT - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ffa0363-65ba-4448-bc05-ac01da1de295">
      <Text>Pallets, a dumpster, a milk crate by the back door for sitting on. LACEY STROUD, 29, in a yellow vest, is on the crate with a phone she isn’t looking at.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f0566256-4787-4b14-9cc2-f5e6adfa98e5">
      <Text>Vance comes around the corner of the building with Rucker a step behind. Lacey sees them and stands up like the crate was never hers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="051053de-17c0-49fb-963b-906d6f36563f">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2232124f-d901-465d-ad61-434edf0911dd">
      <Text>I go fifteen minutes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6a2dcf1b-c87b-4113-9c0e-2b6bdb037fbb">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4fb59b65-1375-462c-9362-b5daef2cdf69">
      <Text>This is Eldon Rucker. He led the Magnolia investigation.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ab055cf2-24e1-4171-8bcf-9aea1665ac90">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5ca9d4b8-5c77-4740-be13-f57d6da83ed0">
      <Text>I know who he is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3851d18c-49e3-42cd-bcdb-4315b2b9f2f6">
      <Text>She looks at Rucker a beat too long.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0a05b730-c70e-4812-b528-3ceecd39a58b">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8b442e7c-4f9e-4eb3-bb91-3e162fd33389">
      <Text>I already told y’all’s people, years back. I got there at midnight, I was in the lot with everybody, I didn’t see — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="37ca9d55-a0be-4304-b746-1e6dcb4518a8">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="006d1a7b-d089-4856-8676-c5f76a4016bc">
      <Text>Lacey. Three people put you inside before eleven.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2d35c13d-5793-4cc6-9f74-8e4e61ab0e83">
      <Text>Lacey goes still.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ed04038-9faa-41d8-a841-a52cd8deb3a3">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c6ef611e-8617-4670-9e24-f245c65d20b7">
      <Text>Nobody’s in trouble. Everybody who could’ve been in trouble is gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8767ffd5-4b6d-453e-89f7-07bfffbabcea">
      <Text>Lacey sits back down on the crate. Slowly.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1c162e10-6e4d-4777-95fc-7d017d546b53">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5804c7ea-4e9c-467f-adc9-48ee4955fd09">
      <Text>Deena signed for me. Told Pete I was her cousin. I was seventeen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="983e6d17-c02a-4d87-87fc-d0ec807775de">
      <Text>She turns the phone over in her hands. Over. Over.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7b9b0fcf-45b1-42e3-ba5c-4c1436e92587">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a50698e0-e801-46c6-82e9-dad11b18efbf">
      <Text>I was in the back hall by the payphone — there was still a payphone. Waiting on — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11d3f86b-8f8b-4b92-acd5-1455680d9338">
      <Text>She doesn’t finish that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c3a8ff94-44fd-4e10-ad69-b8252a83cc0b">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fbf725fa-3206-4ea7-b8fe-599be1472f81">
      <Text>Had to be ten thirty. Ten forty-five. Before June’s second set. And I smelled it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a426c4fa-93a0-41b2-a469-8c6f2377cdd6">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="493be289-a3d5-4885-8657-b86e2ea9c191">
      <Text>Smelled what.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3fa07a32-abde-408b-bf75-cbc498b773d7">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="27ffd1ce-a996-4ae1-8a4b-a76e6b4312fc">
      <Text>Like somebody left something plastic too close to the stove. I looked down the hall. The storeroom door was tied open. But it was dark in there. I figured it was coming from the kitchen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fb8c99be-a510-4e8d-8ce8-fa64900147ec">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="73caadf2-41ba-45ed-b33a-6ee1e751d531">
      <Text>Smoke? Or smell.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ce920121-b7b1-4a66-a8a5-b5a0ac2b69f5">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="baf367db-c724-482c-b85a-c34907322563">
      <Text>Just the smell. I didn’t see any smoke. If I’d seen smoke, I would’ve—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dbc93c26-5cae-43b9-aef8-780c3a4b9caf">
      <Text>She stops and looks down at the phone in her hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cca30989-77c8-4202-a151-247139987aff">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7a069414-5f8e-4f3a-bb5d-673876761a20">
      <Text>I told the deputy midnight because at midnight I was in the lot like everybody else, and that part was true. And Deena — if I said I was inside, Deena’d have caught — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a6cfae56-d052-4da7-b2e1-e37608151b4e">
      <Text>She stops again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c9a8003b-980c-4cc1-a5ad-0335fc1a950e">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8f2b2150-d03d-4381-89e0-27bcba553608">
      <Text>I watched them carry — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dd24898d-b67a-4b4d-9230-fc715067274c">
      <Text>She doesn’t finish that either. She looks at the pallets.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8f23f20a-52ee-46a2-b5b4-d4b9cfb55b01">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="71b9c29b-46d5-4287-959f-bf85257021ea">
      <Text>You were seventeen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ba23ce43-13a8-4f57-981c-8399260fe300">
      <Text>Lacey looks at him, then back at the pallets. Rucker hasn’t been writing. Now he writes fast — a line of times, the pen digging.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="07007427-cfe7-4bcc-a8e3-57136df76999">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f8962d3e-0af5-4bbb-bb16-bba5b9ceb985">
      <Text>Ten thirty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5a081c1b-07d8-4602-93af-4a9e530ac667">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9ca843b6-64ae-4cbe-bcbe-da677614d5c3">
      <Text>Before the second set. June opened her second set the same way every — </Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="329b4393-412e-4ac9-a923-cdb9fe627acd">
      <Text>She stops. Looks back at the pallets.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c84dc5b1-4afc-4852-a5e6-983ddd0108d8">
      <Text>LACEY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="739d3d19-a95d-446a-b2e7-4539d33b63bd">
      <Text>Ten thirty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="8c989ede-baeb-4436-9d9d-84da44136984">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="92" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d890dfe6-3f54-4cd2-9b3a-5353b6806c15"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6b35036b-0469-44d9-b12c-9e3305566ab4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PRUITT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a0dd59b4-448e-49d6-a00e-e15de15fe767"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a6422fe3-7352-4a86-82e0-b91d4c405caf"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HALE COUNTY FIRE TRAINING SITE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="894430dc-6a37-4552-8bc9-eeefa94a8d5e">
      <Text>At the county training site, a live-fire authorization names Mercer technical officer. A crew unloads lumber beside the empty burn pad.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="68cbbf9c-9f7b-4ead-980f-1516370842cb">
      <Text>On the concrete pad, Rucker checks a compass against Mercer’s scene book.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cb594b34-2d85-4aa9-a2ea-1bcbcc5ad441">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2654965a-d7c2-45ef-8ce0-2fe6f2a8fd3d">
      <Text>West wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ca5427fd-2c52-4a9f-8791-5d1c2254ef1b">
      <Text>Mercer marks it and snaps the first chalk line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="7e914321-aba9-4795-b093-227b7c1f99da">
      <Text>CONSTRUCTION MONTAGE:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="82fa57ff-bd8a-49a3-800d-cb96885b8ddb">
      <Text>— Chalk lines establish the storeroom at full scale as the crew anchors floor plates and raises the stud walls.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5f20cffe-d64c-4b45-9122-06c8a8d98bf4">
      <Text>— The west wall rises with its high window at the recorded sill height, aligned to the Magnolia window’s compass bearing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="ae69de11-a281-4202-8304-7e0f528910a9">
      <Text>LATER:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eb3b8df1-f75b-454f-8737-923c2c3e8ce1">
      <Text>The finished shell contains only the Magnolia storeroom and short rear hall. On the staging wall, Cobb’s pre-fire photograph sits beside the gridded fire photographs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ad057094-310b-459d-99be-9b6cfb9d1cc3">
      <Text>Pruitt carries in a roll of FOAM STOCK, sweating under its weight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d32dac65-777d-47b3-97eb-69e39815812c">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d01a2e16-3f6b-46d9-8ba4-4028ad85bc7a">
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Opelika</Text>
      <Text> still runs the line. This is the closest match to what shipped in ’14. I logged the difference.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0cb567b2-b776-4504-abcf-cf344905744b">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="24d779c3-3a4b-4de3-b108-82aab2e3c2d7">
      <Text>Match the picture. I don’t care where’s easy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cba53ae6-2799-4c94-a819-ec9fcd6d306e">
      <Text>Pruitt works from the pre-fire enlargement at the center of the wall. She stacks the foam beneath the west-wall shelving — where Cobb’s photograph starts it, the </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Opelika</Text>
      <Text> delivery count fills it, and Hoyt’s memory packs it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5fd3707f-8d6f-480c-8243-368dd156d913">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="74b78c47-80d9-431e-a81f-c8eab83bfc4d">
      <Text>Then hang the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c29d515-dfca-4863-93a6-b6f1d53ab9bd">
      <Text>On the staging wall, separate from the photograph grid, Pruitt replaces a legal-pad sheet marked 26 DAYS with one marked 25 DAYS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7441bbdb-2e55-4969-9d8f-06bed0886f8e">
      <Text>Across the pad, Rucker installs the shelf standards, checking each position against the pre-fire photograph with a level in his other hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="de9616db-ab09-4a86-8d72-6ad9a6dde906">
      <Text>Pruitt hangs the salvaged louvered door between the storeroom and reconstructed rear hall. Rucker wires it open, checks the photograph and adjusts the angle two inches.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d4a0deb7-ce22-4239-b616-e047ffcf492c">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0fd192ed-c53a-4302-8411-c48a0f0b0365">
      <Text>Does the wire matter?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c0a47e26-1285-48b6-b791-9070bb515ecc">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="33f010d7-bc01-4c33-a7ec-2187568e8196">
      <Text>It’s in the picture.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="cc20700e-b4f0-4511-a7d8-cb5c38508ad7">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="93" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b69b1a16-421d-46c4-a3af-e928195f75ce"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d317a192-1a37-404d-9d6a-9a81f3da16e1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="41dc83ea-a0ec-453f-a45f-709e1c8ccf5a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b9675b0f-01bf-49aa-99de-03442de8f6d9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. RUCKER HOUSE - KITCHEN - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9f451f6-d036-4ec4-9518-3215425310e8">
      <Text>Rucker enters late, sawdust on his forearms, and stops. DONNA sits at the kitchen table with the bank statement flattened beneath her reading glasses. Supper is covered on the stove.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5555e8ce-b397-4261-9644-e3cfcc434426">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d50f6fa4-9e5a-4a62-becd-e7824d5661f3">
      <Text>Four thousand at Hale Lumber. Eleven hundred to a foam mill in </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Opelika</Text>
      <Text>. Sweet girl. Thought I was your office.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="94a68296-51d2-4716-885f-e4bf6c346acf">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2b4600d9-75ee-4ba3-a82f-da781d440be7">
      <Text>Donna—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="420b19b0-e59e-4224-8bd7-f0e1d96e1d72">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0ac37ca4-c337-4379-a37f-8652cc3ac9b6">
      <Text>Wash up. I’m not doing this with you standing at the door like company.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8b7c8844-aaa6-4935-998a-437ac4ce1fca">
      <Text>Rucker washes his hands and sits. Donna sets a plate before him, then returns to her chair. He doesn’t touch the fork.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="30494120-a064-476f-98df-bcaea0d4dec8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3e507bb4-2ecf-41d1-94b6-63899a4ba084">
      <Text>I should have told you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d4de236-b814-4dc5-95f9-c85af5e67394">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8e7da445-366d-4800-804a-64824387f96f">
      <Text>You should have asked me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cbb0869b-27ef-4cd6-a53e-b21a002aa1c9">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="83717cdd-0cf9-4197-bd9a-99f0174f8d92">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8e30be87-f4f4-49b7-9a7e-580be129f968">
      <Text>I’m not asking you to stop. I’m asking you to be in this house while you do it. You leave before six, come home after ten. Ruth Tillman moved pews on me again Sunday, and I learned what my husband is building from a girl in </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Opelika</Text>
      <Text>.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bd9bc6e5-cd02-4096-acbb-3064674c162b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6e97ab5a-d5ef-4df8-bc42-5b80c5144f8e">
      <Text>I’ll put the money back soon as—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cbe4f748-9c29-490c-a9cd-9f5078a2a8d9">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91c5170c-584c-44f3-b356-0b2ab615db57">
      <Text>I’m not talking about the money.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="66db063b-1b5a-4916-a057-a41fafcdd3e5">
      <Text>Rucker says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bf2a6f46-912a-4f68-8da5-ebce1fb1e04e">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="21749d2b-8bdf-4d3f-af3f-619015b011bd">
      <Text>You were sure the last time, too. And I ironed a shirt for that courtroom every single—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2c8f8e17-aa87-4b93-aca5-41beb3ddeaad">
      <Text>She stops. Closes her glasses. Donna writes a check and sets it on the statement facing him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c4035347-38d2-4032-aabe-ae7cb06bbe2b">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="731e4754-bfce-4658-a37f-0ca54cd87dea">
      <Text>Lumber’s got a lien on the truck otherwise. And Eldon—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="72729108-4cb2-45fc-96ab-deb28752f516">
      <Text>He looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="68fd1963-4263-41ce-91c8-e33851d74e54">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4021dd92-a301-4ec9-8d42-7181d314c9d2">
      <Text>Whatever comes out of that room, I don’t read it in a bulletin. I hear it in this kitchen first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1abdff4a-e3a6-4f9a-b0ac-bb06bf550bfd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5496b644-cbc0-42f9-b8bb-923846ce3612">
      <Text>You’ll hear it here first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a5550d43-402e-40f9-96ae-0c3cb173ae91">
      <Text>Donna nods, then runs water over the supper pot. Rucker eats.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="504602bf-14a4-4963-b3d6-52b49c10e879">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="94" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0fc89475-9dfb-42d7-8ed6-423dafa85c83"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PRUITT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="05e12d82-100c-4d4d-888d-eab28e7ae2fb"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="961db61e-a927-45b7-bc80-029c1270d070"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="c087841e-86aa-406d-af1b-cbaf8fbb938f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. TEST STRUCTURE - THE ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="57e9fcab-0a63-4114-ab70-c188debf6dcb">
      <Text>Done.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8bb113d5-158e-405a-825d-26e10d0dda15">
      <Text>The reconstructed storeroom is complete — loaded shelving, foam rolled against the west wall, the louvered door tied open to the short rear hall, clean glass in the new window frame. On the staging wall: 19 DAYS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0e1e8d15-eb54-428f-b4d4-d41e2ae90618">
      <Text>Mercer moves through the room with a working print from Rucker’s phone, matching print to room, room to print. Pruitt follows with the clipboard, initialing each match.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8de2dfa2-ce42-4ac6-8804-46bf61db9887">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8cd06ee8-577e-43f3-bbb8-84937444812b">
      <Text>Insurance photograph. West wall. Water jug on the sill.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eed662b3-aa37-43d5-b5ce-1d96c1d4b656">
      <Text>She points to the jug in the working print.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7331ade3-2597-4e03-b30a-8ba30f76b9a6">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5971f386-6a56-42b4-a869-4691bf0c1344">
      <Text>Put it where the picture puts it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="44f83808-7d8e-4028-8b5a-e49fc9010797">
      <Text>Pruitt sets a matching five-gallon glass water jug with a couple inches of water on the sill, matches its position to the photograph and moves on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7dfde6f2-1ab0-4fed-93a7-3873b782d00a">
      <Text>The west window is on Magnolia’s bearing. A flat overcast lies across the sill as Pruitt photographs the placement and turns to the cameras.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8de1108d-b6cb-4a17-8242-b99c11b094a9">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="f00b2ecb-c896-4853-93d8-c3b1d53ff261">
      <Text>(to Pruitt)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b5b56caa-a88c-497b-ad05-d950fd1f953d">
      <Text>Cameras.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="80e7d6f5-d0d8-435d-832a-ed240853e60a">
      <Text>Pruitt mounts two small cased cameras high in opposite corners and runs their cables out the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e1f7a734-c15b-476e-aa7e-0b3af5207d2b">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3ea2e883-f6dd-450f-9e52-79748b844cec">
      <Text>Both write to the trailer, time-stamped.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f951b934-f31b-48e0-bb36-fc7f1c8f40ff">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3dc05b14-71fb-4b70-813c-6d7993611457">
      <Text>Every minute, gap-free, or it’s worthless.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c6780f5a-dd5d-4517-82f6-e995ebbe2665">
      <Text>Vance stands in the doorway, outside the room itself, arms folded, taking it in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="95953adb-a1c8-48b3-824e-ef147363d054">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56e05254-a489-4336-88b8-eeb2b2b446b0">
      <Text>Thursday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8d7c9b40-3109-42bd-b3eb-53c88908984a">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="61fdb0d3-5f9b-4ce4-9bfc-81cd18404500">
      <Text>Instruments get here Wednesday. Thursday, three o’clock: a small flame into a seam, then away. If the tight pack can hide fire for hours and open into flame, the cameras and instruments will show it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dc0a2df5-719f-4f2a-bcf4-c5b5e6bc933e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="db17fa00-e059-4f4f-926a-4adb0f78cdcd">
      <Text>Three o’clock. Same light the room had.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc1704ef-c9fb-4369-bc42-0be2267c0d26">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a363b308-c7e2-4b29-9327-70c704f310da">
      <Text>And if it agrees?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f559b25c-c3f2-4a2b-bc67-d900a0f0a422">
      <Text>Rucker is still looking at the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="53d94af1-dc75-4395-a80c-64eae0000ee0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eee6e57d-b7cd-4173-a8fe-e0b9e5613341">
      <Text>Then we’ve proved what the foam can do. Not who lit it. Seal it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="473161bc-ff36-4f28-9267-fbd529c1f41d">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="96" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HALE COUNTY FIRE TRAINING SITE - DUSK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5aac87a0-dcb2-4a78-ac36-8ee046da7265">
      <Text>The window is latched, new glass clean in its frame, custody tape initialed and dated across the sash and door. Mercer padlocks a new hasp.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cf96752e-18dc-459d-a878-eb72e2daaf4a">
      <Text>The trucks leave through the county gate one at a time. Mercer locks it behind them. Alone on the concrete pad, the test structure’s high west window catches the last daylight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="c5c177b4-aeec-48ae-a59d-62d5681228b3">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="96" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ENGINE CAPTAIN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a13d6e43-91ed-4568-b7bc-c7f95f92b606"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="cbae42d5-8a0b-4c09-aa87-85eda75181a5"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="NOZZLE FIREFIGHTER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b2a7bec5-829c-4b85-81ae-2d821e68551a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT./INT. HALE COUNTY FIRE TRAINING SITE - SUNDAY NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4da1e55f-9b47-41b2-8e72-e54732f951eb">
      <Text>Four days early, red light flickers against the pines. Engines come hard through the county gate, tanker behind them, fire showing at the test structure’s west roofline. Mercer’s truck slides in behind the second engine; he is out before it stops rocking, vest half on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fc99e2e4-b326-4db2-baec-e7a62f8c0e32">
      <Text>ENGINE CAPTAIN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9ee0306d-1eb1-432e-9685-20e147093d0b">
      <Text>Thought this was y’all’s burn —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="38c783ac-3b79-4d3e-9690-8cbf73d0e8fb">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ff5b86e1-8572-4bd6-be72-eeb8d5c4ebec">
      <Text>Pruitt looked at her phone at midnight, saw the frame lit up, and called it in. We don’t light until Thursday. This isn’t the test — run it like a working fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b7e7a04e-105d-41b9-bf00-189954890f3e">
      <Text>The captain looks at Mercer half a second longer than a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">fireground</Text>
      <Text> allows, then turns toward the attack crew as they mask up at the door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="95cbcde2-54db-42ae-97f5-f2fa1770913d">
      <Text>A firefighter levers a </Text>
      <Text AdornmentStyle="-1">Halligan</Text>
      <Text> behind the hasp. The screws tear free; locked padlock and hasp fall together. The door gives, a boot tears through the custody tape and the crew moves inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="efb78ff7-8164-44d9-8f80-9d3a5746fe57">
      <Text>INTERIOR: Black to the waist, orange deep in it. The crew advances low down the short hall, the nozzle opening in bursts. Steam SLAMS back over them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="141ab5c4-a886-4c63-873a-b403fef55602">
      <Text>The reconstructed room is going — foam burning against the west wall in sheets of black smoke, shelving standards glowing, fire running across the ceiling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="86b4e3f3-aab9-4bea-affa-f44a089ada0a">
      <Text>NOZZLE FIREFIGHTER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="4aea3d91-bc4a-4040-9694-cae045d25025">
      <Text>(muffled, to his backup)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8411f79a-4c5f-449c-9c47-a65562b8b965">
      <Text>Hit the ceiling — HIT THE CEILING —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="048e3c7f-3b6f-4b98-ba4c-46c3c064cbb3">
      <Text>The stream opens and the room DISAPPEARS in steam. Black water runs into the short hall as the fire drops and the attack crew backs to the doorway, charged line still trained inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="89d696f1-835a-4e11-a8ca-269d28484067">
      <Text>Outside the gate, Rucker’s Suburban skids onto the shoulder. He leaves the driver’s door open and runs across the gravel, stopping beside the engine as Mercer reaches the command post.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c1fcd280-89f1-462e-bd74-46964b8cbe84">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8b70a2d2-9e5a-4201-8629-f0da8d587387">
      <Text>Hold the overhaul. We need the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ee19c864-19c1-41df-af41-1a5a09932bdf">
      <Text>The captain keys his radio.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f2245365-ba51-46cb-8277-7bb430839efc">
      <Text>ENGINE CAPTAIN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2507ea82-99c6-4b99-8b03-4faaf463df47">
      <Text>Interior, hold at the doorway. No pike poles. Nothing moves unless it’s still burning.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="58d555b8-727d-4be5-93bc-24bc24f1c14c">
      <Text>A pocket of flame shows behind the shelving. The nozzle opens briefly and knocks it down. The crew holds at the threshold. Mercer watches them cool the room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5f82752c-64c5-43ce-92ec-0cee156bc96b">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="350d0cbd-43f7-4647-9025-c2c1315e02ff">
      <Text>(quiet, to nobody)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9417b849-139b-4427-a887-9a1ac0917848">
      <Text>Put it out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d9bd0ab4-cf95-4ce5-9d1f-f1c6db83e122">
      <Text>Inside the steam, the clean new window glass lets go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9816756c-72cd-4126-ba5d-f98aef5ba796">
      <Text>Rucker stands among the hose lines with his hands at his sides.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0488c654-530e-4b9e-8876-9cf22b37c8fd">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="97" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="009d9454-8988-4be7-8172-f1fef5561579"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PRUITT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2837aa87-8046-4701-93f4-fc2bb4c2a866"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ROOKIE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="acd90fa7-c4d1-423a-bb46-500ca8bf3f33"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="dc16ac4d-f51a-4ddc-8f8b-43714be725a1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="afb1fbd8-0429-459d-8ca3-7df9418c04e9"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. TEST STRUCTURE - THE ROOM - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2873a358-87fe-440e-8091-6d4c006c22cd">
      <Text>Out. Overhauled. Ruined.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eb32eaee-8a4e-4001-b20a-8684601d879a">
      <Text>Six inches of black water cover the floor. The foam is fused, shelving down, ceiling hanging in wet tongues. Outside the doorway, the taped photographs remain dry on the staging wall. Rucker and Mercer stand in the water with flashlights; Pruitt, soaked, holds the doorway, her clipboard gone somewhere.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="75bfa4c0-ac1d-4543-9c47-f95f16947660">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c83d0264-97bd-4ff9-a63f-db819a56274c">
      <Text>That foam was every yard of that run left in the state.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1d609105-23b6-4f2b-8b7f-88ba5af2ba8b">
      <Text>Rucker’s light crosses the ruined room. Everything they meant to test is gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="25ab9f63-756e-45d3-ab1d-b849503c59ff">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fdd82e84-c5b0-4772-a217-57748ed95a6e">
      <Text>Thursday’s gone. All of it’s gone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ca68a403-4f10-4db1-8f47-cce5c74116a0">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ca1c046a-96a6-4619-a7e4-4575831bf550">
      <Text>I know it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="07219ab6-cc99-4723-9f87-31fce226143f">
      <Text>Silence except for dripping. Then, from the doorway, small:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b43ea108-727d-48eb-a9a4-2fba40db72c7">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="046ad3e5-733b-4db1-8b75-977af5115be1">
      <Text>It’s all on the trailer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a1271a9a-3544-4ffe-bcf1-6925ec8210cf">
      <Text>Mercer turns.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="90f19945-146a-4397-a703-809e717a4297">
      <Text>PRUITT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8d781c9a-54da-47ce-a4b5-45e0d47dbf90">
      <Text>Every minute since we sealed. I just watched it go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="8cb17134-6e93-4536-83cb-ec51538530ae">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="98" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="324a84b9-282a-4a03-b2b5-d7dd157b065f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="c432f7f7-1278-411f-afac-80be357da905"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="caa931c5-cc28-41b7-ba3c-b84868b02892"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="abe55ad3-536e-4822-8e55-ce3e1efba581"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SITE TRAILER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="45f8bbf1-161a-4a67-9c85-cd4cb79ca816">
      <Text>One monitor lights the work trailer. Rucker, Mercer, Vance and Pruitt crowd behind a folding chair nobody sits in. By the door, the water-spotted countdown rescued from the staging wall: 17 DAYS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1a576b85-4ea4-4bae-9aec-f3703d11b4d0">
      <Text>ON SCREEN — THE ROOM, whole again: timestamped, silent, gray.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ed02ed26-7b65-4045-b573-758f844046d1">
      <Text>Pruitt scrubs through Saturday — gray glass, rain on the sill, nothing — then Sunday. Hours run by in seconds, the room unchanged, the timestamp spinning. Morning. Midday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8afcdf97-a902-4cb7-b9ac-f5892956ff88">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9af31b2b-d89f-48c1-8ceb-62effd16e05f">
      <Text>Slow it down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1285e5e6-79bd-4a40-b8fa-8a32c891f662">
      <Text>Real time: 14:31. The room, nothing. A patch of daylight crawls across the floor below the window.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1424bf14-cfa6-4267-94a7-e5003757d09f">
      <Text>14:44. The patch climbs the sill. At 14:52, it reaches the ordinary glass jug. Passing through curved glass and water, the light contracts to a hard white point on the rolled foam below.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b7963f38-a18b-4124-8e6c-a1b642f8f4ec">
      <Text>14:58. 15:03. The point holds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4e597ed2-b7c0-4b0f-b42c-b76fdced6e12">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="363b2a58-594e-4d27-b3ba-5ac9cce10afb">
      <Text>Let it run.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5bd09712-a7da-4393-8a72-505516360b15">
      <Text>15:07. The foam darkens at the point. One gray thread rises, then another. The room remains empty, the door shut. No one enters.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0c00cf3b-df8a-47b5-baa2-4cb8277b1081">
      <Text>The threads thicken into a rope of smoke, climbing the wall and pooling along the ceiling until the room disappears.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c959fbb0-69b1-4a41-ad3b-f772e1afad8f">
      <Text>Pruitt scrubs forward. 17:00. 19:00. Daylight fades as smoke fills the frame. Soon only the timestamp remains readable.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bd0b8e0e-8b04-4dcb-a125-b29d442640e8">
      <Text>Mercer raises a hand. Pruitt stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="927db50b-074b-4c82-af7d-b3981734650f">
      <Text>Real time: 19:26. Gray, edge to edge. 19:27. 19:28. Nobody reaches for the mouse. Mercer breathes through his mouth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f549589c-3b97-4f0b-ab3e-96af6576854b">
      <Text>He nods. Pruitt scrubs on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5b8e1b0a-7b24-4d70-9803-e1536d36ab12">
      <Text>23:54. Deep in the murk, the light CHANGES — a bloom swelling low against the west wall. The second camera shows it more clearly: a flame-colored glow rising through the smoke where the roll stands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="53c5dd95-4b90-4323-9f72-bb0af2e20117">
      <Text>23:58. The whole frame is lit from inside. The timestamp remains readable to the last.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="51a7393a-1d5f-486a-84ab-793f2bb043ad">
      <Text>Vance covers her mouth. Mercer sits in the folding chair without deciding to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e802d6d5-9d85-4903-bd5c-b3b0a2ebff4e">
      <Text>Beside the monitor lies the archive print of FRAME 61 — the same window, sill and slumped glass. Rucker holds it beside the screen, then sets it down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a634dd35-24db-4f13-8bca-de49602e8d8a">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="ccf081fe-8661-459f-923a-b852243503d0">
      <Text>(barely out loud)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4d06f66e-dfee-4229-9b43-32a361e3c488">
      <Text>What time does that make the Magnolia?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7934ab0e-0075-410c-bca2-09726e987d1f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="30d51745-4654-49a5-b0b2-f183708b12cd">
      <Text>(level)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5225db2d-d87d-4c22-9599-df79b630cc75">
      <Text>Middle of the afternoon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2c51f8ef-d3c4-4194-85ad-287bec7c8a73">
      <Text>Nobody answers. Rucker studies the white screen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fa42079b-27a7-41ff-89b0-aec83aa957ea">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fc517aed-0ad1-4acf-8313-49ee8dd4734e">
      <Text>Thursday we’d have put a match to it ourselves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="455557d0-c001-421f-8024-8d1b09f29183">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e66fce49-e58e-461a-9da0-40dde954ca37">
      <Text>I built it true. True is what lit it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="33052c0b-43be-4065-b6bb-8cd58f253438">
      <Text>Nobody moves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ffaa31f0-ad40-4f23-b921-78fe158e43cd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2bc176ee-9c58-46c7-abaf-5204a7ed13cf">
      <Text>Play it again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="c2eba90c-4d90-4d90-abd3-704d3c224f3f">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="100" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b667f071-9ec6-473f-a680-14c89b5f56f1"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="PRUITT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f6a5ca60-032f-465a-b42e-9d32bbdb1eab"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d0df7caa-9535-420d-92c5-bd09dbe4d2c8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. SITE TRAILER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="93b4f687-0ad7-4105-917f-e12c95f1a7e8">
      <Text>The monitor is dark. Pruitt seals the original drive in an evidence bag and logs it; copies go into numbered bags. Mercer signs the source line. Pruitt signs the copy line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aaa2bfc4-7cdd-4988-8daa-e795c227a699">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="52058304-f6a1-42ff-bc34-5be607836f7a">
      <Text>From here forward, every hand signs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9bba9a4e-4370-475b-ba33-6362d7a84ea2">
      <Text>Vance takes the pen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1371bed7-99d4-43b8-abdd-ca57911cec4f">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="41e9137b-5953-4c4a-9cfd-860bb8ef5569">
      <Text>Starting with mine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5c3b24bc-0f27-4544-86ca-64de87e6a674">
      <Text>She signs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="d08fd7b3-e538-44ce-8b29-246251a1a269">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="100" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5a7ff5e6-3f50-46ae-9b3a-a2c20055607b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="bcb1c974-31d8-4f48-87f7-73865e0d3c2f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HALE RIVER FIELD OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="389fb146-ef71-4cec-bddd-5d9a6bcf8b37">
      <Text>Rucker’s county key turns in the lock. The old field office. The State seal is gone from the door, leaving a clean outline on the glass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="79820fac-956c-4aac-a9bb-bc0cc2a8eddf">
      <Text>Rucker sits at the desk, glasses on, a legal pad in front of him. Vance reads the two handwritten pages. She reaches the end, returns to the first page and reads them again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d4f3ae2e-b0f6-4ae3-be24-e84aafaabffd">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="d4c2d5d6-5c52-43dc-a06b-493c45ac7d2c">
      <Text>(reading)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fc4a2db5-a101-46fa-a069-181dbb5976c9">
      <Text>In light of newly available evidence and advances in the science of fire investigation, the undersigned revises —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b6ab92e0-bfd6-4cc3-a0c2-018146f7754c">
      <Text>She sets the pages down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9f1932a8-e08a-4685-a52a-c47763cadbb7">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bf30ccb8-9e94-4f84-9857-bed73ac6182a">
      <Text>Newly available.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="197f5f00-52f0-4bc7-81ca-215ec66396c7">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9c6089c7-de55-41de-8a42-504c8c7c2510">
      <Text>The recording is new.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="52d1ede4-eb1f-4c5e-a5fb-40a5b887609b">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4aa1ecea-f8de-4232-901b-dcc2feeb5b6a">
      <Text>The recording is. The facts it confirmed aren’t. The gap page was in your file in 2014. The jug was in your photographs. The dog and the lab both came back negative.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e2534dc9-5771-4461-a013-18e4ae3a819a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="16ff3ee7-1f98-495c-8fbd-77f0e308b240">
      <Text>None of that told me what lit the foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="371d6c47-ccba-41f7-b7ce-ab3a51601103">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d5b9b06b-8213-4a00-bc3d-79b622bd3a4e">
      <Text>No. But it told you there were things your answer didn’t explain.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7bbd8ef1-15f1-40d0-98a7-8db24825302f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c3284874-6545-414d-b22c-c8ac611add7e">
      <Text>I didn’t hide any of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a53ed864-1384-45d9-be5c-16e352199481">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b8b52d34-7e01-4e72-8552-b2aeb5c9e30b">
      <Text>I’m not saying you did. You decided the fire was arson, and everything that didn’t fit became inconclusive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c9aaaa2a-b7f1-4d9c-bb0b-55ef3fe6c650">
      <Text>Rucker doesn’t answer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8cb304fd-0a0c-4b7f-92b8-670f59194624">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e3f053f4-21da-4e30-bddf-3c53337d0a8f">
      <Text>You can file this. It might even work. Every sentence is defensible. It’s the same kind of true your first report was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="035ee93c-e02a-47ad-9ca1-5a90f3825749">
      <Text>She slides the pages back across the desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="44c557fb-27c8-4131-87cc-0cbde83c724f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="40c5a7c6-46a2-4f19-8afa-e43c0a904c43">
      <Text>What do you want me to write?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7e082455-b9db-46d9-92f4-aaa2db16bf10">
      <Text>Vance stands and shoulders her bag.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c88f9caf-dd37-4487-a723-efe9ce3b4f7a">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2cb4e63e-6c76-4249-98ee-4236dac54a8e">
      <Text>Write the one with your name in it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="624780c2-dca3-4449-aff6-49d783e15922">
      <Text>She leaves. Rucker sits with the two pages in front of him. After a long moment, he turns the pad to a clean sheet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e0e80127-aa6c-4285-9797-4f4f05ab56b3">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="101" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="14c06e5c-16ee-40fc-beeb-ac6477a0b46a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="647c975f-0720-478d-b812-7c74bae98b46"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HALE COUNTY FIRE TRAINING SITE - STAGING WALL - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f36cdaab-70e9-4bd6-991e-b6762ff02f92">
      <Text>Rucker and Mercer take the photographs down off the staging wall one at a time, into a box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4929e29e-172c-4063-a64d-d034afb21385">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a762e5fa-4e49-43ff-9f3e-2a472a050a5c">
      <Text>Focused sunlight. It’s in the book.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ad7c8517-a45f-4f3d-b433-c2a04d3c054c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d4630198-dfae-41ce-9e40-d34a1a5d56d1">
      <Text>Been in there longer than I have.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2190a509-31a0-4c2b-9aaa-fc0a584a87b0">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="316cd4c1-d80f-49da-8b9f-13f04a98bfb0">
      <Text>I said we had him. In your doorway. On the phone to Montgomery.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7b6437c5-726d-4eaa-bdfc-d2d20423b6b3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5135a1a7-7e29-4310-a972-b73e5fe0dedc">
      <Text>I heard you both times.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="df558e07-a7c0-490c-9c4d-cb955ac0f02d">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cf331877-0423-438b-9751-21753dc17334">
      <Text>You didn’t say anything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5e4ac19d-8a3b-46da-8daa-b0cc67b6787d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="481e5bbe-427c-4d4b-a7e8-f63f4523b5cf">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1b34233e-9325-429c-8cd8-501ee3c4c6a4">
      <Text>They work.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c88d9052-c1b5-41e5-addc-9f8f4443b3e1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b41c89c8-5368-4357-b507-8cd4b50b2aac">
      <Text>Winter of nineteen I did a crib death in Perry County. Space heater in the nursery. The mother had pulled the batteries out of the smoke alarm the night before. It kept going off when she cooked.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d4f5278-df25-449c-93b4-0769ad6b8bef">
      <Text>A photograph comes off the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="31414e8f-b0ab-4dea-8bcc-20728ec43c06">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5199f1a3-df39-4370-b021-0d3bc9da3bba">
      <Text>She asked me if she killed her baby. I told her I could tell her what caused the fire. I couldn’t tell her what to call herself.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97cc7991-0454-4b05-91d0-b4b0ca1ca26a">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d0cf0b7a-14b4-4595-a863-6d672a6fcd38">
      <Text>You never lost a night over that one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4b3e5035-b7c4-44c2-9a38-10b1ab947191">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d1eccb4b-d0d7-4377-ba93-27c42e229088">
      <Text>No. I told a whole county what to call Amos Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c00354a2-6dc5-4a03-a276-e5288920138d">
      <Text>Rucker’s thumb can’t catch the next piece of tape. Mercer reaches past and peels it free. Rucker steps back, staring at hands that won’t hold still.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="430a611a-88fd-4827-b49b-3282458f5050">
      <Text>He turns toward the pines and presses both hands flat against his thighs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d3cb48b6-d068-46c5-b915-bc4530e89550">
      <Text>Mercer keeps taking down photographs without looking over.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f24a1f41-39ff-49d5-9bda-b8f0bece0642">
      <Text>After a while, Rucker returns to the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3de1c4b3-3a4e-427c-9a47-a013ddc93b6b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3687a9bc-1681-4441-8594-cc0add5f131c">
      <Text>You were twenty-five.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="42a22dc8-8f2d-40c8-b5ce-d0097d4520c0">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0bfc36d2-5984-4262-bd80-07821141726e">
      <Text>Six years with that seal on my door. I never once pulled the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="7be7eb77-d9da-4ca9-bba7-c3e92146361d">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="103" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="DONNA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="8fc6289a-fce7-4dbc-b1c8-cd1ec046f542"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="95640c63-95d3-400c-bf65-b0262c336fa3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. RUCKER HOUSE - KITCHEN - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3041f316-4561-4396-b785-d70f78e4ffed">
      <Text>Late. Donna in her robe at the table. He stands, holding a single handwritten page, and reads it to her out loud.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0cd4cfa1-7bf9-41e7-98a1-108838ba7a35">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f257296c-9b58-4ee5-8565-ba34fe1ccb01">
      <Text>‘In 2014 I classified the cause of the Magnolia fire as incendiary. The classification was wrong. The evidence available to me at the time did not support it. The cause should have been recorded as undetermined. The error was mine.’ Signed and dated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="872c7980-399d-4bb4-a1bb-e9415be0ffb7">
      <Text>The scanner on low. Donna looks at him a long moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e7e836e1-200b-46ff-b001-15cbb5b0cdd0">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8889388e-74f2-4fb7-b751-c73bab653772">
      <Text>That’s the whole thing?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="86e7fa74-1806-43c2-a6f6-1c64e697702e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="50ce3e58-43a6-45a2-99a8-21f895b98c2c">
      <Text>That’s the whole thing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bf270d4b-74b1-4397-b1e9-e87c98c4e789">
      <Text>DONNA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="afce0c91-f7a1-4069-ad05-27cf04c981c4">
      <Text>Send it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="53e8ad83-a1da-4afb-94ca-b33e9ae5d4dd">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 3/8" Page="103" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="3561814b-8dde-40ed-a0e3-01edf4195184"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUTH">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9df53e47-c56b-4bb7-a41d-d961a1ed7adf"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. MOUNT OLIVE BAPTIST CHURCH - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fd02d5cc-e84e-421e-875e-722cc91f836b">
      <Text>Weekday. Empty. Hand fans in the pew racks. RUTH TILLMAN, 60s, heavy through the shoulders, a rag in one hand and a bottle in the other, works down the pews. She is on the fourth row from the back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9fe40c36-cdba-452d-ae2b-5415df98de35">
      <Text>Rucker stands inside the doors with his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d204ad5b-8b5e-48b5-9d4c-577e737b0e7c">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c3477cfe-b443-4f1a-add8-d41aaa92f26c">
      <Text>Miss Ruth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bafc91b3-135c-4908-9c46-161045a5b716">
      <Text>She keeps working.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6bf29642-59a6-45a6-a831-91f3a3d5e2a1">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f5280ad0-fc5c-4ef3-a7f0-b27294ec6c54">
      <Text>I’d rather you heard it from me than the television.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="171c900e-2256-42eb-9242-2dda986b6a75">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de517b56-bd8a-4816-82af-1b973a27b1ab">
      <Text>Then say it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7a470a95-baf1-4a50-b711-6b6dee10292f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2133e857-b0dc-48a1-a7c8-1d6c9b46e068">
      <Text>Nobody set that fire. It started itself, middle of the afternoon, in a room nobody was in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fa97a2fe-c296-4f47-9b08-93dd2bd8133f">
      <Text>The rag stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f218db84-ad5b-4c6c-b6ee-55389bff5cd3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2a6b0cf7-43c9-4204-a5ec-73a6b6d5147c">
      <Text>Pete was at that door because Merle had it chained. I know that now. I should have known it then.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0a8def32-aeba-47e0-8bdf-693a83d5a87d">
      <Text>Ruth sets the bottle on the pew. Looks at the wood in front of her, not at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="db118ee9-1712-4a87-8fcc-298f270fb508">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="18f47d0a-2e40-4fe5-a675-4e41e5e24668">
      <Text>Twelve years I’ve had a name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="88a8ccb5-b7e3-41fc-9dcf-f6e45910bf1b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="150a72b1-93c4-4a7c-b62a-56051062f974">
      <Text>I gave it to you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4f4c8843-1aad-4cad-9a1e-cb2a1cd811a2">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0db0f8ab-1f9a-459f-aae9-bbfc72d787ae">
      <Text>You did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9e2bc8e6-09a8-4407-a403-2ccb938c7b8c">
      <Text>A moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="25c98139-da22-4d25-b4c2-597cf128cdc3">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4e3ffc02-2050-4423-a893-8b5cea6fded5">
      <Text>Merle chained it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ebd3c304-57e9-491e-9567-a205b27b7265">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="077b4a08-9dc9-4f69-b1c2-8da7b7ae94b1">
      <Text>Yes ma’am.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="56d4a855-fd32-4ede-953c-916e0d9a25a2">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af2dee34-dad8-41b2-9c8d-ea34a4c13b9d">
      <Text>And that man in Holman.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="896b650d-6a8e-4206-a8d4-02a4f392f7d5">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="de880a35-39dc-46b2-9ad9-960510ce5ad7">
      <Text>Tried to open it. Burned both his hands doing it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="86338361-1397-498f-9b08-ed10b02ed960">
      <Text>She picks the rag back up. Goes back to the pew.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2fdc9aff-d74c-4cd1-9259-f3afea8458d7">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d0e49773-342b-4073-975c-4f4059597b29">
      <Text>You can go now, Eldon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cbc18276-8d4b-4e3e-bfab-f0bf7a965a92">
      <Text>He puts on his hat. Turns to the doors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f3056528-e0e8-479a-8ff3-b361216a410d">
      <Text>RUTH</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="77db2383-59c3-4df6-b7e0-efcb535b1a03">
      <Text>Tell Donna she can have her pew back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c3c33730-9b5c-4493-a789-fbf02a4e8012">
      <Text>He goes out. The rag starts again behind him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="7d5acb31-6527-4f05-b4f8-7b8dd4291d5d">
      <SceneProperties Length="2" Page="105" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d8f9869b-f5cb-44a8-82b3-687347208d3f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="ODOM">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7fbb89f0-c4ca-4a4e-842e-a28be1324387"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="82700ca9-d16b-461a-9664-cb40bb067c2e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HALE RIVER FIELD OFFICE - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a5f58ea1-0da4-4593-908d-7ab55a5c795c">
      <Text>County file boxes fill both desks, twelve years of evidence tape on the lids. Odom sets the last box down and places a checkout sheet in front of Mercer. Mercer signs the custody line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e68c9c8f-f5ea-49c4-982c-71e8806d87e5">
      <Text>ODOM</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56402029-0100-4987-8e73-bd606b8aa9b3">
      <Text>They stay in this room. Anything turns into a lead, you call me before anybody moves on it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6a66742b-3bac-4b77-a4a3-b3408f2d07a1">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="20ab2382-94a3-4a03-afb9-6d6758d08bce">
      <Text>Understood.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="58617a0d-d028-52a2-a517-286c961214cc">
      <Text>Odom leaves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6e14b5a0-cfa3-5be2-b2aa-4e322d943bde">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7c007d0c-cb41-58f7-928a-813dfaa2904e">
      <Text>Hoyt said he turned three people away from that door. Find me one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9512161a-6ab8-479e-83a8-49544faf6d2a">
      <Text>Mercer works the intake cards one by one until three from the morning after the fire stop him — same date, same block letters. He squares them in a row on Rucker’s desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="b1ebb69f-bc81-4e43-abfd-3562c9d77897">
      <Text>INSERT — THE THREE CARDS:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b4d4452c-c9a2-4594-b9a4-b386ab202b80">
      <Text>EARLINE COX. SAYS A MAN INSIDE TURNED HER BACK FROM THE SERVICE DOOR. PUT HER OUT THE FRONT. NEVER ONCE USED HIS HANDS. DID NOT SEE HIS FACE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="964a9745-cbb7-496c-ba35-57649e4ee81f">
      <Text>T. WASHBURN. SOMEBODY HAD HIM BY THE COAT IN THE BLACK. A VOICE SAID FRONT. HE WENT FRONT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fa4cbdc0-bf71-4143-bb6b-77362bb02f7e">
      <Text>R. PENN. SAYS SOMEBODY TURNED THEM AROUND AT THE BACK HALL. NEVER KNEW WHO.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="bc6b1be8-08fb-4f86-8b35-82c7f3aac924">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c7d430e1-bf94-4d20-a480-c9464a13099e">
      <Text>There’s nothing behind them. No interview. No report. They went in the box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="381e238c-1190-4874-bb64-68b8acb51386">
      <Text>Rucker stops on NEVER ONCE USED HIS HANDS. He pulls the ER photograph of Hoyt’s burned palms and lays it beside the card. Nobody speaks.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fd0f69e6-ab48-42d0-b488-3d6474252447">
      <Text>Rucker turns the box tag where it hangs. The intake line, dated the morning after the fire. Received into the file. Initialed in a careful hand: E.R.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="85e57e97-7d30-462d-a091-6dfa44bf557d">
      <Text>Rucker doesn’t move.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="03bddb21-80e7-4834-afe1-3de480c1518e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="69ce5b71-7668-42c7-8beb-921639bc17eb">
      <Text>Log them tonight. All three.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="08e7c2e0-3b45-4ef7-aedf-d15edda74d52">
      <Text>He slides the cards back across the desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d10e26c0-ae07-4d3c-8f61-8fed6fe5dd58">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4cc2e9f2-e966-428e-b608-2f4f9629427e">
      <Text>My initials next to the old ones.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="19296b1b-e27e-4da6-82c5-a347bebe713e">
      <Text>Mercer logs the cards with Rucker’s initials beside the old ones, then opens the next box. Rucker starts again at page one.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0864e94c-5503-41f1-986d-c92994df5d26">
      <Text>The 2014 county map is back on the wall — four pins and the blank space where a fifth never went. Beside it, a torn legal-pad page reads: 13 DAYS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a9744b3d-f3ae-4645-b9a9-02b2053e482f">
      <Text>Mercer spreads crowd photographs across the desk: file sheets from Aldridge and the store, his own from the hall and the Magnolia tape line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="10c14dbb-8560-4183-aa8e-9ed3ba8f848b">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="2a50bed3-c138-47dc-bca4-aa644f141b64">
      <Text>You told me to shoot the crowd at every fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="42ea8d0d-e742-4330-9c8e-6680585b6f8c">
      <Text>With a loupe and grease pencil, they find the same figure at three fire crowds — back from the front, hands in his pockets, watching the water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b359cbfa-b753-4958-a58e-4f4966d22930">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="468ed8c5-83b3-4dbc-874e-0e2c6984d00a">
      <Text>He’s not in the Magnolia line. Four rolls and he isn’t in one frame.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c5736fe6-7cac-4b20-848d-6065d67cf8a9">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5e2b197d-2dbb-4d24-a247-d096483814cb">
      <Text>Because it wasn’t his.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0b2f0005-0000-4000-8000-000000000005">
      <Text>MERCER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0b2f0006-0000-4000-8000-000000000006">
      <Text>You know him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0b2f0007-0000-4000-8000-000000000007">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0b2f0008-0000-4000-8000-000000000008">
      <Text>I sat in his mother’s kitchen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="285104c7-c3bf-4e96-b824-a8a3227cea44">
      <Text>Rucker walks his fingers through a box of thin 2014 county files and pulls one: JUVENILE REFERRAL, the flap he closed twelve years ago never reopened.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d7fff1eb-3167-4225-b5ea-a1f0bf776adf">
      <Text>Inside: VERNON HATCH. An address off the county road. A grass fire behind a school. On the map, the address falls inside the four pins.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b47c1a02-0000-4a01-9a01-000000000003">
      <Text>Rucker sits with the one-page file, reads it through and starts again at the top. Mercer returns to the photographs, leaving him with it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e6526f95-4443-43ec-8705-48809250fbb3">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="107" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="63f5ead6-9d52-4c13-9775-838694c09153"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VERNON">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="f8ebdb4b-70e4-413a-afd5-83a6f97b631d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. VERNON HOUSE - EDGE OF COUNTY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6d71aa75-6282-4f1c-a62d-e3e0ff2372a0">
      <Text>A tidy double-wide, swing set and kid’s bike in the grass. Rucker parks roadside, makes one call and approaches alone. VERNON HATCH, 28, now thick through the shoulders, opens the door in work pants, socks and a work shirt with a heating-company patch. He recognizes Rucker and goes still.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="12993e97-b434-4f3f-b38c-359cfe3a287e">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6fb7d7fe-4f84-4e13-abdc-da043abb5d6b">
      <Text>You wrote your number on a card.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a1f337f2-5f15-4368-85c7-dce0e1a42be0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="61f42ec6-a637-4d9b-97dc-49d9b0caf0b8">
      <Text>I did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2c1c3629-a8fb-4136-81df-ab4c09da0048">
      <Text>Cartoons play inside. Vernon glances back, then lets Rucker in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="2ac281d3-f377-47b5-b79c-51a61784d129">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 2/8" Page="107" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="5ae194a7-fd8d-49af-9b86-4d0e81c0cc2a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VERNON">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4f22e806-91f7-4a46-9ef8-ab0054510a84"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. VERNON HOUSE - KITCHEN - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e1a3d793-5811-4f98-b8cc-b3cb84f30f36">
      <Text>Vernon makes coffee. Drawings on the refrigerator. T-ball on the calendar. On the oven door, a dish towel of old mill sheeting. Rucker looks at it. Then sets the open juvenile referral on the kitchen table. The broken flap lies beneath it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="65d08003-f5a9-48b4-9010-9883b09861a4">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cebb6ae3-5da6-4d57-92d1-43af50de10da">
      <Text>I seen the news. About the club. About the sun.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dcd09295-2663-4d4a-a070-d1ef9ecf2542">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b7e4ba37-eb3d-4a7b-b9fb-badef48fc8b5">
      <Text>The Magnolia was nobody’s. We can prove that now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="eb96cd12-63be-480a-a356-005dc17d8ea4">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="604e6cdd-16f1-4143-bc7a-4221755b3756">
      <Text>Yes sir.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="63c6e41a-c3dc-4f15-972f-6d0f12853f0d">
      <Text>Vernon turns his cup a quarter turn.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dfa8fafd-3f8a-4a22-a948-cf60fb7b100b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dad8ff3b-cae9-577c-998e-ae7d926a044c">
      <Text>I’m not here about the Magnolia. Aldridge. Cedar Street. The hall. The store.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1178d9fd-b0fb-578d-9f82-85f8a4a5326f">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="16cb6e33-9205-5b5e-83f3-b4cca933d76c">
      <Text>That club wasn’t me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="08afb334-4b53-5c1d-94d7-bb472473fb77">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0ad7cbcd-bd35-5d24-8d31-ca73cd49966f">
      <Text>I didn’t say it was.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7257d724-6381-5518-af9a-b0acc17f7f4b">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="64452810-ddff-580f-8f2a-f71b6a623402">
      <Text>The hall was after you sat in my mama’s kitchen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="408417ae-4a73-5e7c-8aa9-29bf7e74fb7b">
      <Text>Rucker says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c8ca49fb-5da6-4f4c-96a0-f755755c1c34">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0e34a37d-312d-415b-9c7d-e89e706c8a89">
      <Text>Simmons Heating took me on that summer. Apprentice wage.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="049d3ebc-4f16-456c-b650-90f15cd3f686">
      <Text>He turns the cup another quarter.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="62d6d946-84a1-4b71-a849-b4f47a26f3ed">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c3ce842b-ff1f-4f01-9a7b-5903d3fc83d3">
      <Text>It don’t come on when my hands is full.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b6c99091-6289-4622-bcce-39715388edb7">
      <Text>He looks at the folder. Doesn’t touch it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="018c4b09-89be-4065-b3ab-b691e6dc5021">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b8aa4993-4968-4ca2-a6d3-5184b2df3ccb">
      <Text>Them four was before Simmons.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b2a81edf-29b0-4687-aef5-eafe75a330f0">
      <Text>Vernon looks through the window at the bike in the grass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8e9eb5d2-4d99-46b8-bd60-c54999eb783e">
      <Text>VERNON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="45b2e049-f23b-45f9-9992-5b013799b3fd">
      <Text>My boy’s six. Whatever this is, it don’t come in the house. He’s got practice at five. After five.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e0bf5d94-1a22-47a2-af7d-c2b0a3d34e37">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="55d4a263-0000-445b-bdcd-b8cb43945890">
      <Text>After five.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="957802e3-a9a0-40ba-b8c9-73a38fbf71d7">
      <Text>Rucker looks at Vernon a moment. Then closes the folder, takes it and leaves.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="562b3c84-7e31-4c8a-8e9d-b21e977ed963">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="108" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4e36657b-e07f-4c24-a306-2e1a81a3796b"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="d86f9a39-8b5b-40c9-a86c-0821476c15a7"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. VERNON HOUSE - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5e80b357-b9a4-44a2-ac53-a53482f69613">
      <Text>Five-forty. The family truck is gone. Two sheriff’s cruisers turn in without lights.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="36df5cb8-7230-4aa7-9cfc-0394708ba1ad">
      <Text>Vernon waits on the front step in a plain clean shirt. There is no struggle when the cuffs go on.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b15bf5e4-43ef-4085-8fd6-65a19bff2e3a">
      <Text>Rucker watches from his truck up the road.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="2157ec13-3520-4bf7-8577-8cce4b786ebb">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 5/8" Page="108" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e172a4b1-3bc7-490e-9e73-b25f60953568"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="92b94a34-7200-4796-9edb-92e9f46e5856"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="aa645ca4-930b-42aa-8ffb-96a6bebf4812"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9eeae6aa-29bc-4686-aee2-99e83eb41335"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - VISITATION - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="15eb5bb4-2155-4203-9c6a-83030540255f">
      <Text>A legal visit arranged by Vance, who waits one booth back. Rucker holds five timestamped tape stills to the glass one at a time — light on the sill, the point on the foam, the first smoke. Hoyt studies each from his side, silent until the fifth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97df94c1-e04c-4b03-80e6-c424c0a5a850">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fe1bf671-a11e-4447-935a-d37d03bba6a0">
      <Text>Middle of the day.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97c76a32-2543-4d2a-a160-f5531c91bb87">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="12cbb50e-c980-40e4-81eb-81682019baca">
      <Text>Middle of the day.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fcec14ec-5f07-4936-b93e-4f959c6b192f">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="653c9508-2078-4571-9d01-825a36cbe5e6">
      <Text>I stood in that hall that night and listened to my cooler run. It was already going in there and I—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bef5c6e1-4562-47f1-9a3f-1dccb83fecf4">
      <Text>He stops, pressing the heel of his hand against the counter edge.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="361b9cbc-3514-45e5-bbb6-b2e1ba074f8f">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b17494ce-48e1-47f4-bc9d-1c2d54478fc8">
      <Text>Nobody could have seen it. Nobody. That’s what the tape is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="459ac1c1-fc50-4e84-ba5f-1667d31c839e">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f8797555-c16e-47a1-9e4e-7663a9e33b53">
      <Text>Pete chained that door after the fire had already started.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0a578014-366e-453e-aec7-70d8e6abfa54">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="caa4083a-a747-4f41-bdef-89fa9b6ab83b">
      <Text>Yes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6fdb5ab7-ce46-49d5-b295-ad34eddb05c2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="edf22615-533e-4e8e-bde3-57d1c95afe72">
      <Text>And the other ones. The four.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1e57c74a-9da3-487e-8dd3-36f5e9f0a116">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43e11400-4bd2-45c0-9d4e-49666817fe4a">
      <Text>A man’s in custody. He didn’t argue the four. Won’t say the Magnolia was his.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2651a3fa-95a6-484e-822e-b9b0b752547b">
      <Text>Hoyt takes that in, then gives one short laugh that dies immediately.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e70a8c8d-ed6a-410b-9f21-f13f63730867">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e6f31226-d4aa-485e-a49e-13de43d19495">
      <Text>Twelve years. And his took y’all an afternoon.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="be0f6d69-eae4-4718-a1f3-91cb5773ac2a">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="eca3e8f1-efb5-44ed-8d9d-17bd70dbe49b">
      <Text>It took the tape. I’d have gone to my grave—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d54f3ca-9434-499e-9ae9-355c82e6534b">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c516ee40-ad4c-42cd-bdee-7404621bc55f">
      <Text>I know what you’d have done.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13bf1d35-ef3f-479a-ba7f-e1eaee60f1cd">
      <Text>Rucker has no answer. He holds one more page to the glass. Handwritten. Signed and dated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="10259be3-c414-4334-9f73-8ac1991d8f25">
      <Text>Hoyt reads it through the glass. Reads it again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9dcc4e9d-560a-4965-9cc1-336a57afd058">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="af6b5cc2-106b-4a02-bfd3-06f482e2152c">
      <Text>That one’s yours. Ms. Vance will get it inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="6611f5d2-45d1-43bc-8149-5caeb7a6f9c3">
      <Text>Hoyt’s eyes stay on the page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c3b0a6af-50f3-4174-8349-91ef87f1893c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="35e94875-2938-4a07-8e6f-3cdc234357ad">
      <Text>So what happens now?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="894781ab-9cf4-47c8-89ed-7463955e6f87">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ce59c96f-90ac-48b0-a0ea-fab547df104f">
      <Text>It goes in front of a judge. All of it. Under my name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e5dc9570-9d58-46e0-a8a7-9f80f5836eb4">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="30909dd1-df89-45a2-9c5e-bbb9cde57982">
      <Text>And the execution date?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2a2669e4-01b3-4fea-8244-24784c475bc8">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0a6a0b14-3246-4fc4-a512-cf130faf067f">
      <Text>Still stands. Nothing changes until the judge moves it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="db94c417-1c9e-4a15-bc83-e66ecc2aef78">
      <Text>Hoyt looks at the five stills.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a99c6a56-12cf-4d59-a515-d0a9bc23a133">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="da8c92a7-4e08-43af-adb5-414357490a52">
      <Text>Even with this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9e08566e-f170-4da3-a883-6cd8195c1e42">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e70c7c65-ff5d-414e-8122-6bfa288df36a">
      <Text>Even with this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0d3513d6-0f84-4f8c-ace7-f7839f007a35">
      <SceneProperties Length="3 3/8" Page="110" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="1ef97abd-2b42-4b07-8661-f6873e7bdc8f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="OFFICER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="58879a63-2527-4a8c-82c7-4853ea8de946"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="0fd41c2f-ba9e-4040-8229-5f2b73dd146f"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - ATTORNEY ROOM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8fe77659-0af9-4fbf-bc12-db319be993f9">
      <Text>A contact room — table, no glass. HOYT waits while the OFFICER lets Vance in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="33d50e9e-bada-4bb2-b10e-d2a77e196846">
      <Text>She’s talking before the door closes, her bag coming off, a single sheet coming out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ab46efc7-57e6-4760-8320-5b948c49a676">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="31253cc0-376d-4271-8810-cfd08cb25c8f">
      <Text>The Governor is offering a conditional commutation to life without parole. The execution comes off. In exchange, you withdraw the petition with prejudice and waive every future claim based on the new fire evidence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="405bcb5a-9c04-461a-b0a2-de18b6a4795c">
      <Text>She lays the unsigned GOVERNOR’S OFFICE letter in front of him and sets her pen on it. She does not sit.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="72718f9a-1900-46e9-b78e-3a75730837b5">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a3cba040-4fe1-4b59-9e8d-3c7175f95039">
      <Text>If they doubt the conviction enough to stop the execution, why am I staying in prison?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e7b5bed9-73ac-4ee3-a0a2-12116a8f73c1">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e1093ae1-5132-48e0-a1f5-61bff3b9642b">
      <Text>Because the Governor can change the sentence, not the conviction. The Attorney General won’t ask a judge to vacate the verdict. This stops the execution without disturbing the judgment—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="baf32d20-60d8-40cd-be35-b51d3ef27284">
      <Text>Hoyt stands. The chair goes over.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="80435059-bead-445d-9d18-e9228f2f5e49">
      <Text>OFFICER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1da2ae9-dcc9-4785-8b94-08b2c86cf9e5">
      <Text>Hoyt. Sit down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="76fb32ec-3847-4966-9807-4e2af1215a3d">
      <Text>Vance stops. Hoyt rights the chair and sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ba9c9d33-ca55-44a8-ae10-9816ad22fcef">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f3634c0a-935d-4566-be15-0a05f65bf993">
      <Text>I heard the words. Say what they mean.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4bef9573-782c-4205-88be-a9ea258147d7">
      <Text>Vance sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="69a8bf88-661a-4b10-909a-30a7a0854e5f">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fba9eb91-8a57-45a5-8e41-e8ec9b8a0722">
      <Text>You sign, you live in here until you die and the record still says you burned them. You don’t sign, a judge hears Rucker’s paper, Cobb’s statement and the tape. If the judge says no, the execution proceeds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="833539e7-0ef3-4c37-a55f-3ddc2e4462da">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b2a9f725-6b31-423a-9e6b-e911a9761898">
      <Text>They ain’t offering me my life. They’re buying the tape. I sign, it goes in a drawer with Rucker’s name under mine, and nobody opens it again. Not Kendra. Not him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5674b187-e992-4e73-9c79-177193e66aa6">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6442abe4-bd6b-4fe0-bb12-87a653f75188">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4ce51cac-25d0-43c3-8af6-83710fc43f22">
      <Text>Amos, I have never had one of these on a table. You sign it, you see Kendra Sunday. And the Sunday after that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8b0490a1-5b01-4085-a27e-913b5db2e323">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="02547395-359b-4919-9e23-ef17a295b050">
      <Text>Every Sunday she drives here, everybody back home knows where she went. And that paper still says her daddy killed nineteen people.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="33f85436-309d-4101-8763-6f4cd26d8455">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a07830d5-dfc1-47b3-a090-a62b8de9b94d">
      <Text>It says you’re ALIVE—</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="31e74a53-f75c-44c8-b21d-cdc0bd5100b0">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a0d4c418-01f6-4004-bb29-9b0cae9817f4">
      <Text>Alive as who?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f1a20524-915e-451d-aaac-40523d4281b0">
      <Text>That stops her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="93f7ae38-fcad-40fb-bcba-254c406c3e57">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9d66cff3-ed10-4f2c-b87f-d7bf3d018cfe">
      <Text>They took my work. My house. Every year of my girl growing up. I couldn’t stop any of it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d91d9269-9f23-4c81-b39b-dfa269f61b91">
      <Text>He looks at the agreement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cd2ebc0a-bbe4-4eae-a854-d77b93055925">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="940a9de9-c018-4f59-854e-2f61aa91a4bb">
      <Text>The one thing they never got was me saying I did this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="91a036c1-7498-4915-9ed6-0ee572457ff3">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5aec67b2-24bb-491e-a711-0c048d01ad13">
      <Text>This is not a confession.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="76c39791-b22b-43f5-b179-6d95f7923bed">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0573b72a-e070-486d-bbf8-855646691299">
      <Text>Kendra has spent twelve years carrying my word against the State of Alabama. Every Sunday she comes through that door knowing her daddy told her the truth.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e5dda72a-b492-4890-9b09-a0bc45a3cd17">
      <Text>He puts one finger on the agreement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4dd2312f-8c42-4817-9906-1e3cf29bc2f6">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f391c264-fca9-4462-a1cd-9717fb3b0c46">
      <Text>I sign this, I tell her maybe. Maybe she was wrong to believe me. Maybe everybody who looked at her and saw a murderer’s daughter was right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b64f7b26-e2cc-4244-be28-c5fe54d7f57b">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d7f4bf3d-e2b3-4efb-bba4-a8de0a5d8cd3">
      <Text>That is not what the paper says.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="01c3c858-0760-41b7-a1e9-1f853dfd98ce">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="48cd0e8e-d7d3-497d-a698-b701ff6e8764">
      <Text>It’s my name under their lie. Ain’t nobody going to care what the fine print says after I’m dead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="46f079c6-6477-4f1b-a7b3-e669969c7d93">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c45dab9d-0a88-4bbd-89d0-5b923ada44d6">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="3ae0ec18-c416-47f3-b47c-6f5582985094">
      <Text>I can let them take my life. I cannot help them take my word.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8090cde1-f455-4baf-a283-7fa2e00bf9bb">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c45c5b27-c79f-4cf3-b98a-3c27ebd58996">
      <Text>I need you alive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9695d8f5-7e98-4b03-b3ad-55c01bf25041">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a449ceed-7f03-42b1-b114-8a12af828f80">
      <Text>And I need my name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="44a765f6-44e6-47b1-9a73-228ccf702ff5">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dba8b42e-05ab-4125-a256-34a9fd3c68cb">
      <Text>If the judge says no, they kill you.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d9452e09-0572-4687-b000-8c15be6a72c8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7968dfae-4b96-4aec-9176-ae5b02e518c9">
      <Text>Then he puts his name on that. I’m not putting mine on this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="28af3303-3bbc-4b93-bdc7-623503b9c485">
      <Text>Hoyt slides the pen back with one finger. He never touches the agreement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="67870514-b430-42d3-b9f4-88ae7f0e95e1">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="df3c3263-6702-467a-b819-fcd18f8ac2c2">
      <Text>File it. All of it. Under everybody’s name.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2fb55c32-2f54-42cf-9259-df74fed1dfad">
      <Text>Vance looks from Hoyt to the agreement.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d7a8492a-7213-4cc0-89a6-4ec7008ddb29">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e46c1be9-33b4-4a92-9a9c-9210141c6213">
      <Text>I don’t know if I can understand choosing this.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0df78f09-67be-40fb-a406-35ef2b49c2c9">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a40afa1e-81d7-4b29-8fe3-7ad6930c95a7">
      <Text>You don’t have to.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="94ab77f5-cdf3-441b-a177-49754d05e2d1">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="834c8895-8e56-4791-9450-a3df96ef5230">
      <Text>I have to know the choice is yours.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="53fb4f2c-e262-4b63-9c9b-ff934b3a13f4">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0a6605d7-6539-4686-b06a-66db29044b3b">
      <Text>It is.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6a62fefb-f66b-47ee-99c3-d96b60417019">
      <Text>Vance takes her pen off the agreement and turns the page face down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="1baac55d-0d08-4f2d-8dcc-694cd34f8a1a">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83d849d5-7ded-4a06-9990-d2e322b36eb5">
      <Text>All right.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="76d473b2-6999-4575-b88f-b5d920205890">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9b0b3ba8-27fa-4f90-8459-522794a64dec">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e4b7d4b5-948b-4676-830f-e2052bd08c8f">
      <Text>Then we go to court, Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fa85cafb-bdcc-4dee-8524-d919a78ee1cf">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9da23253-90a2-4b48-853e-55880a4695b2">
      <Text>First time anybody said that to me like it was good news.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="bc8179fd-5727-4d91-9a8c-37a56ed43fa2">
      <SceneProperties Length="6 1/8" Page="113" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COURTROOM DEPUTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="25b32bda-2df4-41d3-8d37-f8bccedfdb97"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUDGE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ebb01754-2f4b-4394-a513-f0b7e1086924"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="LAMBERT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6f9f03b6-ea69-4736-80c2-1513b795d775"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="ab3519b0-279e-4b6e-99c3-3328c1443b3e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9e00f390-bd8f-4bcb-a17e-5618e94870fd"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. U.S. DISTRICT COURT - MONTGOMERY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a8036b38-e356-47a2-a5a1-f416996a0e78">
      <Text>A federal courtroom under cold white light. Built for a jury, but the jury box is empty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7b4991dd-fbf7-4207-b893-d467e0100b5b">
      <Text>The JUDGE’S BENCH above everything. Beside it, the WITNESS STAND. Below: the COURTROOM DEPUTY and a COURT REPORTER at her machine.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="75908303-1abd-4955-96c9-255fa2e8ff93">
      <Text>Two counsel tables face the bench across a center lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="26362d24-35cd-4c43-8b8b-ecd516fdb7e3">
      <Text>Vance at the PETITIONER’S TABLE. Lambert at the STATE’S. On Vance’s legal pad, written at the top:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="559bca91-7329-42da-844b-f49adb2315a7">
      <Text>7 DAYS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6df0c24a-d375-4f49-847b-5bb1f3bbf65a">
      <Text>In the gallery, Rucker waits in his good suit, his hat beneath both hands. Mercer and Pruitt behind him. Reporters along the rear bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="25fc6b8e-8da9-47bd-9f85-10cf3e58275e">
      <Text>KENDRA sits alone in the second row, very straight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="12629662-4cda-4f1b-b3f8-175d517974c1">
      <Text>COURTROOM DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f47351f7-9a26-4637-87de-2f9047b167bf">
      <Text>All rise.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3840e817-c0e7-44ae-b168-2aa48184cda6">
      <Text>The room stands. The JUDGE, 50s, enters and takes the bench. Half-glasses. A closed folder and an untouched pen before him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3a30bd75-b579-4f13-a605-35dfc1272f02">
      <Text>COURTROOM DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="53085c6b-99a1-4e02-bf60-7a52a4c3efb4">
      <Text>Be seated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1078cada-e6c3-4161-9644-5ff37b0690bc">
      <Text>The room settles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f01248e7-0f18-4e79-a316-086d3efa9594">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="44454e90-0f40-48da-9c14-eb9800285430">
      <Text>Ms. Vance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="93519afe-c6f7-4e65-9a02-e45a0ccfe0e8">
      <Text>Vance pushes back from her table. Before she can reach the lectern, Lambert is on his feet.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="754f7e46-6228-457c-a033-2c74a7e54195">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e401295c-d155-4ff4-8b94-a95c8e5ee2f3">
      <Text>Before we retry a twelve-year-old case: this petition is successive. The evidence is late. The claim is time-barred.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d5a0203d-cc29-4e1c-ad0e-b2187a906589">
      <Text>Vance remains standing behind her table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2852a659-d4f8-4171-b223-e66a96112375">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a34af829-4637-41fe-b11e-494e64d43618">
      <Text>The State made this capital murder by proving arson. Its own marshal now says there was no arson.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ef489c96-2eb8-4255-b7d1-5cd98dece458">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8e46b881-278c-490f-be65-860701c69c29">
      <Text>A deadline doesn’t move because the man who missed it finally opened the file.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9ad490cb-3c74-4ca9-bbdd-f7f833a6b7bf">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="03296e85-e995-4b85-82f9-b7b96d3dffd3">
      <Text>Trial counsel received nine photographs of a hundred and forty-two, and never saw three witness cards taken the morning after the fire. That is suppression.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2ffe4c03-4c6f-48da-8004-7ca0c8bc9ecf">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7320514f-2ad3-4b0f-a3ca-a4ffd45b73c4">
      <Text>The index was disclosed. The cards sat in a county file trial counsel could have walked into any day of the week. He didn’t ask. That isn’t suppression, Your Honor. That’s the record.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="23b18527-16fb-4c36-bc58-145c6a473901">
      <Text>The Judge looks from Lambert to Vance.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6a92cbfc-cf29-4cd6-9ba0-e2de2c016749">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="739198cb-3bb6-4b7d-9ba4-0129f17f2be9">
      <Text>I’ll hear the witness on the petition and the motion to stay. I have not ruled that the petition came in time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8e592e0e-f8cc-4bfc-a94e-3c60bc8e3ae4">
      <Text>Lambert sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="774689c9-6ba6-425e-820d-ee4ed669d8e0">
      <Text>Vance steps to the lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="97f8a8e0-3d46-44fa-a69f-cc8e4192c075">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="39514e54-5cdc-4531-a357-07b0418dac12">
      <Text>Petitioner calls Eldon Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d4e23d9c-72cb-4195-8cd7-1cc712e9199c">
      <Text>Rucker leaves his hat on the bench and comes down the center aisle. He passes through the gate in the rail and stops beside the witness stand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="926f0bec-dc97-404f-bb7d-bc822cda103b">
      <Text>The courtroom deputy swears him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9cb5d38c-1146-40d9-87a3-32d29ca3e9d3">
      <Text>Rucker takes the witness chair. Vance waits until he is settled, then begins.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="746be55d-f72a-4f5d-a9b0-92d2778976f5">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1850a52-b599-403b-8ac2-53571ea25229">
      <Text>Marshal, whose classification was it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="802629cf-fd3f-46de-9699-1676ec5eb37b">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a70ac832-c9ea-4393-a21f-8f783d49afeb">
      <Text>Mine. Nobody wrote it but me and nobody signed the cause but me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b01b4158-7fff-40af-a5e0-9ad45abb3a4a">
      <Text>At a touch from the courtroom deputy, the courtroom monitors wake:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9c8980c8-62f2-45f0-936d-a6266e3f7d11">
      <Text>The State’s trial photograph of HOYT at the edge of the firelight, both hands held away from his body.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="17287dfd-8cff-4f0f-9728-ea5aefc6f5e5">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cf41de17-a2cd-4f88-b66f-764b72fe56b1">
      <Text>State’s Exhibit Fourteen. Who took this photograph?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="594777e0-e7fb-4ed5-9db6-daadaa22de20">
      <Text>Rucker looks at the monitor built into the witness stand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d8c36fd1-bc29-4cb4-8f21-c9456dc2e1ac">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b1a027ed-2e5e-48ab-9b1e-c4f7dad02e55">
      <Text>Investigator Mercer. The night of the fire. The State used it to put Amos Hoyt at the scene.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fa3c94fc-7229-4f7b-97fe-c329214da902">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="966af550-27d4-4ed8-aee1-6510a82fd854">
      <Text>Look at his hands, Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8141a644-1215-4103-b118-dff3daddbdf0">
      <Text>Rucker looks. The room looks with him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="5f68869c-4e23-4eb9-adf7-1296f9f6dedd">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="25d629da-d075-4832-a1bb-4aaca9f7210b">
      <Text>Held away from his body. Both palms open. That’s a burned man.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3f65932b-0e49-48a5-96b0-026960c85b84">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a849144d-a91d-4573-87e5-49913867f1d3">
      <Text>Whose exhibit is it?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4ae0473c-9fa6-4b2c-8b1f-18e9a34111bc">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="96895dda-e052-42b8-96c8-ee6d55163757">
      <Text>The State’s.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d9e25d7f-1852-42d2-9237-34c1fb5970f7">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a711cf3b-2ed3-4db1-b76d-8d1d59ec719c">
      <Text>What from the original night corroborates a hidden fire?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7ae42373-da64-4e6c-9a2e-c35e005fd2e3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d2614d86-5229-4445-b627-df3bb714c297">
      <Text>At ten-thirty, Lacey Stroud smelled heated plastic in the rear hall. No visible smoke. That is consistent with fire already inside the foam.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="87f7267f-0121-4292-9801-cf70659598cb">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="15456dba-ac4c-4440-8c6e-730e026893dd">
      <Text>And your correction?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="710c0634-2cc9-48d3-a7d8-03ca91db70b6">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="59b20040-32c1-4ef3-8b36-c242e7d54d87">
      <Text>The classification was wrong. The evidence didn’t support it in 2014 and I signed it anyway, because I believed I was right. The error is mine and it’s signed and dated.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a2446f31-df72-4803-a9c4-790e14320138">
      <Text>The Judge’s pen moves for the first time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="764de78e-c433-4455-92f4-f9faa106f971">
      <Text>He looks over his half-glasses at Rucker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ccfedd9a-e298-47cd-b37d-fbe817796ffd">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1dd07dd3-a2d3-4fa4-9f11-4d6fd11c7c2f">
      <Text>Marshal, to a reasonable degree of professional certainty, was the Magnolia fire intentionally set?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6b16bd6a-b270-4f65-ac2e-4b6f8221dced">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a7c3cd0d-2820-4473-8462-c7e1847512d0">
      <Text>No, Your Honor. I can’t tell this court what lit that room. I can tell it the fire was burning at ten-thirty, while Amos Hoyt sat at that bar in front of witnesses.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="83ad126a-8128-4164-a708-acc78e48f8a7">
      <Text>The court reporter’s keys are the only sound.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="daa1fa91-ccda-42ac-bcd4-3c9010881262">
      <Text>Vance returns to her table and sits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9d78c3bd-aa12-41e3-b241-65473d6ae050">
      <Text>Lambert buttons his jacket, rises and takes her place at the lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dcc476d6-c83f-4d44-9813-446af9d9f0cd">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="230616e1-d554-4e70-8f29-3b3733ef306a">
      <Text>This office did not authorize your reconstruction.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ff767d99-aa96-4396-bf9d-991c82eefc53">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="bb5b191d-d615-47ef-940b-51a525554dc4">
      <Text>No.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89bd3b5e-8c3b-47e9-a6a0-b3fe3a71994b">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b324e833-0a51-4619-80a5-dc4f84e21352">
      <Text>You chose the room, the materials and the arrangement. You paid for it yourself after the State ended your commission.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="520bbb27-8130-49e3-85b6-bfe266069044">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="966b8d1c-9dce-4709-b4eb-133a5ca654bf">
      <Text>I copied the State’s measurements, the county photographs and Cobb’s invoices. And yes, I paid for it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="336a0aa5-6c7f-48cc-b431-356aab8a8bf5">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ecd5a4f7-41a1-4174-95b8-29017c2e29fb">
      <Text>Who put the water jug on the sill?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="829855b2-91b8-4b76-9867-4b60c85a4efe">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4d80dcb2-4d7d-428a-b786-180d931241de">
      <Text>Amos Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d35c8ed-95e7-4822-9cde-2fbc26af15e9">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b8bf7672-84e4-4c1a-b999-c5fcc09bbc36">
      <Text>Then his hand created the condition you say started the fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4e2bbe51-de8a-4a90-8d6d-96ec049f8b7e">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="fa2d88d0-2513-44ca-ad43-2bc0e68a2db6">
      <Text>He moved it out of a work crew’s path in daylight. That made the geometry. It did not make arson.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d8d40edc-580e-4e54-93fb-d5d0da74c70f">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="681cc7df-8f0b-4c7e-bad8-573652eeb5b8">
      <Text>That jug sat on that sill all week, Marshal. Why Friday?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="57648125-eda2-4c57-bcbc-93e893f9ead0">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f1d92fc7-5ffb-4b6f-9b7a-ae78a73bf411">
      <Text>All week it sat over a partial stack. Friday morning the last rolls filled the space beneath it. The insurance photograph and the delivery count put them there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d7d030a-39ee-48e5-a9e7-330fd9ab6df1">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4eddb512-8186-4029-bb2b-696653e791a5">
      <Text>Your reconstruction burned on a Sunday afternoon in July. By accident.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="19e2029b-e711-4604-bd7e-a5c844c78cad">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4631c4b6-c1ed-4432-8d80-206b54b53922">
      <Text>That window faces where the Magnolia’s faced. Sill’s the same height. We built it in July because July is when they handed me the clock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d943e462-bf85-4079-b987-7cee9bb7241b">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c703dfde-916d-46d5-95a4-2519c1dc5fe4">
      <Text>You’re asking this court to accept a one-in-a-million event.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="cc88da92-d405-418c-9123-1fdfe6bc86d4">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="83fa67fd-1746-495e-b2f1-f594fb29173c">
      <Text>It happened twice in the same room, twelve years apart. First clear afternoon, both times. That’s not a million to one. That’s a window.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="524a95b5-71d8-4931-ada3-765b9e449992">
      <Text>Lambert leaves the lectern long enough to switch the image on his counsel-table screen.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e26437f5-98e3-47ee-9fef-d5697dea332e">
      <Text>A laboratory report fills the courtroom monitors.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4ad9669d-b865-4189-a948-01c41e1e1f03">
      <Text>He returns to the lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e09bc302-b8b7-48e6-aa85-4a646d4814d3">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="6e528bb8-42ad-4c10-b999-4c8f682620b8">
      <Text>Gasoline on his sleeves, Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6f426992-b40e-4476-9640-1b3dde7c34d3">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ef626589-6f4a-4416-a203-942cbe075f23">
      <Text>On his sleeves. Not in the room. Nine cans off that corner and the lab found none. I told a jury it could have burned away. It could have. There was never a reason to think it did.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9158faac-9b8d-4d76-a260-3e9b5abf3f68">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b823682f-b8d1-44a3-b137-c4e4bb6d42bd">
      <Text>Nineteen families were told this was over. The State’s interest is that over means over.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="211c1674-986e-4694-8f2e-c97bdb2b8ec1">
      <Text>He lets that stand. Then, almost gently:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="85573e67-b711-44dd-8d36-fee063bae0c5">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="0954c4e8-4bd5-4b8b-81bd-b8cdb4b90029">
      <Text>Marshal Rucker. Were you incompetent in 2014, or are you unreliable now?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dfe9b59b-d75c-4db8-b811-26890e06146a">
      <Text>The room waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b0a6b8ef-2bd5-481d-ab76-55a58a175136">
      <Text>Rucker looks at him without heat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6f127b6e-1bb8-402e-8909-e4f977817199">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="39e0daf5-65ef-4681-9830-bd76320eacf1">
      <Text>Yes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3bf03c00-c824-4e73-b43a-5ed65868e1c0">
      <Text>A stir moves through the gallery.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3298b256-9eb2-469d-88f3-7cf0ec7804ec">
      <Text>The Judge glances up. Lambert studies Rucker a moment, then closes his folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e76dac8d-1061-42dc-9bc5-8c89aab071cf">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e1eeb267-cb09-4890-839d-09dd7c2da43d">
      <Text>No further questions.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2c95bf57-cf0b-4e81-94ab-b13a7c2929ae">
      <Text>He turns toward the State’s table.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9d80e28b-f13a-48ed-9d77-dfcf024eb0b8">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ab5232de-fc3f-475b-906b-d4a2ac98e7a6">
      <Text>Mr. Lambert.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24c0712c-199f-4fcc-91c2-16320adc779d">
      <Text>Lambert stops and faces the bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fdbcd88d-45d3-4879-9d41-11d9127208ca">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91afc213-93e0-441b-b6d0-17d1801915b8">
      <Text>If I reach the merits, what evidence does the State have today that this fire was incendiary?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="d26051c5-194c-4d50-9a29-f1e550288855">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="56278037-3863-4a43-9340-3ea8d348cb13">
      <Text>The State’s position is that the Court cannot reach the merits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0c92749c-6b39-4679-9bbb-d9ec1a3e4595">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="66549ed4-bd18-43e7-b98a-92f8871b0041">
      <Text>I know the State’s position. That wasn’t my question.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="57a7bb71-2817-4f16-977c-581442ccdc3a">
      <Text>Lambert returns to the lectern.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="643c1817-a69d-402a-a358-9bf36a39238a">
      <Text>LAMBERT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c1b0f0fd-9a96-47c1-bb47-2af2d14d8c92">
      <Text>No new physical evidence, Your Honor. The State relies on the trial record.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="060d119c-6330-42a8-b538-c69976315a4c">
      <Text>The Judge makes another note.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="821b4244-a1be-4524-9c6c-532c456f4142">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43c37b14-1d63-4b9f-a0c2-7f27fd8d5683">
      <Text>You may step down, Marshal.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ef2e5151-88c6-428b-8aaf-fdc38c2ccfa3">
      <Text>Rucker leaves the witness stand, passes between the two counsel tables and returns through the rail. Mercer shifts to give him room on the bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="edf55cb4-143e-403f-8f60-1a05223e5f5c">
      <Text>Rucker sits. His hat stays beneath his hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="ab04a2b0-52e1-46c5-a2f1-da35931f827b">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="120" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="COURTROOM DEPUTY">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="7b793685-4864-47b6-96e9-6c93fce8a47e"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="JUDGE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b4b04208-4738-4704-85ce-cce1557a6375"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. U.S. DISTRICT COURT - MONTGOMERY - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a745839d-626f-4d20-a502-0d946d15c1e1">
      <Text>The Judge closes the folder.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="49a44ade-a41d-4f33-8b91-6e8bc12ac117">
      <Text>JUDGE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="abb53b3f-1681-49bd-8c97-4335ba4e1823">
      <Text>The Court will take the petition and the motion to stay under advisement. We’re adjourned.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="4c72bc20-529d-4123-8a72-c7d2eb733244">
      <Text>COURTROOM DEPUTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="1fe25e51-2f18-4c44-8011-39741d6827d7">
      <Text>All rise.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bf2b21c6-e568-48ca-8f0a-168548cb5996">
      <Text>The Judge leaves through the door behind the bench.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b4493a6f-e94d-429c-96a4-48d601581195">
      <Text>Counsel chairs scrape back. The gallery rises.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="561c0a95-a836-4e56-9597-f461c187a07a">
      <Text>Across the courtroom, Kendra finds Rucker’s eyes for one second.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3a989cd8-e4f9-4234-bc3c-f2d543cee1d0">
      <Text>She turns away first.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e3fe303a-a54c-4a7f-b707-4e074b5e5491">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="120" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VANCE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="e7f334ca-6b28-4ac5-9cfb-33834258f1c5"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. VANCE’S OFFICE - BIRMINGHAM - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6d17a5c9-25d2-4ba3-b2ed-361169552954">
      <Text>The window unit rattles. The whiteboard calendar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c2725a78-1ae6-4f1e-886b-4dc7941272b8">
      <Text>A CHIME from Vance’s computer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1ef1161b-6b00-4e4f-8355-b188c871ed26">
      <Text>ON SCREEN — NOTICE OF ELECTRONIC FILING. An order entered minutes ago.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f40e975b-155e-4eb6-ac39-fa707238d0b7">
      <Text>Vance opens the attachment standing behind her desk.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="6e57a3d1-6b8c-47bd-b086-22d3f12a1e34">
      <Text>INSERT — THE ORDER:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c26b34a8-7212-48e8-99e3-be1b19a394f6">
      <Text>“...the petition is DISMISSED as successive and time-barred. The motion to stay is DENIED. Discussion of the merits is pretermitted.”</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3eedaf2e-3721-4d1a-94af-01583c8c67dd">
      <Text>One signature.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9a5d753-6cb0-4eea-b1fe-c2a40d0c69f5">
      <Text>The printer wakes. Vance waits as the order feeds out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f2be55ed-95c0-4bea-bf28-c91d3ced2a2b">
      <Text>Behind her, the whiteboard calendar: day after day struck through in marker, down to a circled date.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d9509328-c5eb-49f1-98c0-33a947e191c2">
      <Text>Six clean squares left before it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ba65a5eb-84f9-4ff4-9c89-f23587be2a82">
      <Text>Vance picks up the phone. Dials without looking anything up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="89ac93c9-3cc8-4daf-b044-10d2ac418a63">
      <Text>VANCE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical" id="57b59176-6982-4b8a-a734-8663541ba4cd">
      <Text>(into phone)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="43a6301b-eed6-4b55-8734-834ba2d88c33">
      <Text>They’re not saying he’s wrong, Eldon. They’re saying he’s late.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e691be5b-49d5-4f3f-9473-74c8fc2d643a">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="121" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RECORDS CLERK">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="cd6d7951-9d8e-4e39-b7f7-29e7309be687"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4fde03dd-45d7-4f8d-b46c-fa81c9bc34fb"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. COUNTY RECORDS ANNEX - BASEMENT - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="36efddbd-6093-42ae-9fe5-9b55010b746f">
      <Text>The same counter. The same CLERK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e0ece6cd-2664-461d-a4db-dedf8b318f59">
      <Text>Rucker signs the log and slides her a slim folder: his SWORN CORRECTIVE DECLARATION and Cobb’s SIGNED STATEMENT.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c1bb84b2-c870-43da-8822-a17ae18f89d9">
      <Text>She stamps both, opens the MAGNOLIA box and files them over the 2014 report.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="58ead716-4891-479f-9203-69aa44e2e08b">
      <Text>Rucker’s signature on the old cause. His signature on the correction, twelve years later.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="427cff59-378d-491c-8f44-d4fc32ee024b">
      <Text>RECORDS CLERK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="32101eea-34f2-4af0-8421-762a59594769">
      <Text>Anything else?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7def2f66-d762-4ed0-9717-a579cb76fe85">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="70c94575-00bc-4ddc-b7b1-220188afb75c">
      <Text>No, ma’am. That’s everything.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f9df418b-ebc3-4fd7-a084-aedbc4e49e57">
      <Text>She closes the box.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a5dda424-371c-4c5f-8f5c-f0e6c0a2e44c">
      <Text>Rucker puts on his hat and climbs the stairs.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="24dd3117-bab5-4843-8254-036206bf68f5">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="121" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b1b1bfcc-a5d1-461c-b272-d3c52b369632"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MERCER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="10ed431e-9110-4772-9006-fba6a1278af8"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="RUCKER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a8a59f74-a995-4a33-9a18-b1cc22bd9972"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="SLOAN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="de4cd834-df0a-48ea-85f7-fd722c2738b0"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. HOYT HOUSE - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="d20e65f3-2515-4d6b-9038-5f0d78294e8b">
      <Text>The same yard. A small sedan in the driveway now, hood up, a droplight hung from a loop of baling wire. KENDRA in past her elbows, a socket set open on the fender.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="629edb35-43d4-4367-875d-51c0afb0873f">
      <Text>Rucker’s Suburban stops on the road. Not the drive.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4e51ae4d-0120-40c0-88f3-264e1fb94121">
      <Text>He gets out with a folded sheet and comes as far as the edge of the grass. Stops there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="576acebc-2976-4340-abbe-8cdfc1e4ae9a">
      <Text>Kendra looks up. Sees who it is. Goes back in.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="44718c71-f914-4a5a-897b-c5bf9952ab5d">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="76515759-de19-4ede-b489-cb0afb564bd2">
      <Text>Miss Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="4632c79d-9976-4acb-a20d-6dae20a39c37">
      <Text>She gives a bolt a half turn. Checks it with her fingers.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e75ca4c3-523f-4ce3-b66c-4ae9e9a45d93">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="19e8d501-645d-4067-97bf-a6fe34d825b8">
      <Text>Miss Ondine told me. Sunday, after church.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="1c1bf2a6-7741-454d-864b-ad1dc9c3980d">
      <Text>He holds up the folded page. The county stamp shows through the fold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6d67cb08-9a16-4e92-9d42-34a6ddd43cda">
      <Text>RUCKER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cacff8a6-9c5e-4740-9394-53cab85e74d8">
      <Text>I’d rather you had it from me.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2bd69044-2248-4eeb-9542-a37b130c6df8">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7517b871-180d-4b52-b07f-51ca18aac6ea">
      <Text>You can put it in the mailbox.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="aa82e7a6-838b-4c4a-9464-7d2ad9dec538">
      <Text>Rucker looks from the mailbox to the page in his hand.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2bfa942f-9d48-4f3a-b340-e3a036bd0bce">
      <Text>He does not move toward it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dd8269e1-3191-4909-91cc-85c6acc54d3f">
      <Text>Without looking, Kendra wipes her hand on her jeans, reaches back and shifts the droplight two inches. Then she leans into the engine again, past her elbows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1dae875b-409d-4455-a830-0b792a361848">
      <Text>Rucker waits at the edge of the grass. Finally, he puts on his hat and returns to the Suburban, leaving the page on the seat beside him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="82fd9ab1-af52-4fd5-9fe2-8dd592ef26ff">
      <Text>Through the windshield: the open hood, the droplight, Kendra’s arms deep inside.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="6a9cf2ed-16f1-4427-9a9c-c9ec45de3db6">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="122" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>EXT. MAGNOLIA MEMORIAL - DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4baa3db9-fbf1-4747-bd96-9c115715eb05">
      <Text>Gray first light across the granite. Nineteen names.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="af4fac53-a143-416d-b73f-4c62e6ce5357">
      <Text>MERLE COBB sits facing them in the folding chair, its split rubber foot wrapped in electrical tape. His hat rests in his lap.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fb16b3de-0265-46e7-925a-0a07fbddbff7">
      <Text>Rucker’s Suburban enters the drive and slows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="be7f69f1-f0be-432b-a497-7ccc2eefcc59">
      <Text>Cobb hears the engine but keeps his eyes on the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="da31b6c1-2b80-40e2-b673-6da3424c78b6">
      <Text>Rucker stops. Never gets out.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="abf78be3-208b-46fa-8eba-16784c7627e2">
      <Text>A long moment.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3d3cf967-725b-4e20-b658-d93cc470390f">
      <Text>He reverses out and leaves the wall to Cobb.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="6d12294f-8c1b-438f-b0f5-f70c15ec3bbe">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="122" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="GOVERNOR">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="37f04479-7d19-4bcd-9712-b36b904e500c"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. DOT’S DINER - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8abd651c-7af5-4a3f-be43-9e07be8ead12">
      <Text>The lunch rush, quieter than it should be. Rucker sits at the counter. His old booth is taken.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="89f439e2-19ea-4499-bfbb-8064abad8070">
      <Text>Dot pours his coffee without a word.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4df0870c-ee31-5965-900c-2232828a633b">
      <Text>On the television above them: the GOVERNOR, 50s -</Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft"> </Text>
      <Text>a different man from 2014, the same suit -</Text>
      <Text Font="Sans Devanagari Final Draft"> </Text>
      <Text>at a podium.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="57869235-1a11-4621-b070-24acfff1b9e9">
      <Text>GOVERNOR (ON TV)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="9d9482b8-c194-54cc-a6e2-f4a8faf7ab3e">
      <Text>Mr. Hoyt was offered a conditional commutation to life without parole. He declined it. The courts have declined to disturb his conviction or sentence. I will not intervene further.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2a37de8f-2d20-5f26-af88-74ef659eeb91">
      <Text>Nobody at the counter looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="51fdb11c-0837-40dd-85d4-dbc95b58bc98">
      <Text>Down the counter, MISS ADELE puts money beside a half-finished plate and goes. The bell over the door jingles.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f3c32286-44bb-43d3-a4e8-76b9fc4eada7">
      <Text>Rucker drinks his coffee. He doesn’t hurry it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a28e35ef-75ab-47a3-a967-209fecd7e99d">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 6/8" Page="123" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="77a2469b-7b6c-471f-91d6-db6e59891174"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="KENDRA">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a1d68d5d-0344-4981-9288-59afe79f584d"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="OFFICER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="abfc3ad0-1652-4b57-9edd-d69dbac6c36c"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - VISITATION - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3c1f005e-1794-4391-8f3c-2039db3b9696">
      <Text>Kendra and Hoyt. The cloudy glass. Both phones already up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ed87298c-079d-44d8-9256-58d8624c7bce">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5fcec5a7-212d-4541-a147-d7a9a398d7dd">
      <Text>They moved you. Lady at the desk made me do the whole form over, the whole thing, so I know I’m late. I’m not — I just mean I know I’m late.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="2d11656f-0e2e-4676-a888-b4c07ed8a9f2">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="53febe8c-d6f1-4b83-9808-d2ad0564b743">
      <Text>Different hall. Food’s the same.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0688cd3c-7f5c-4e3a-9087-717454e8507b">
      <Text>She tries to smile at that. It doesn’t hold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e5cea565-e437-47f7-b05f-a0e0754c1162">
      <Text>He watches it not hold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="9c8edb26-7074-4596-a550-43e53b0b0840">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="d9a5628b-7f7a-4d61-8be8-6aa624fed55b">
      <Text>I know why you didn’t sign.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="44dad77b-a12d-4585-9fc5-d77f05087afc">
      <Text>A beat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="e1469746-1cc1-444a-b893-a92f0205f277">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8c4ba3e9-4e7d-4710-8470-e2539678b58f">
      <Text>Then you know. We don’t spend this on that.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="07e627f8-ec52-4bac-9815-0320bf11ff76">
      <Text>He gives her somewhere else to go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="ce271c6b-0ad7-4059-83fe-9bcbe277a905">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="dfb07bc7-534b-4b9e-92f0-1c19429d545d">
      <Text>Car still clicking?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a5965fb0-73df-43c3-a7af-02925e696ecb">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="b9e5ccee-d12d-49a2-b115-5d7e06e231d2">
      <Text>Fixed. Hundred and thirty. Boot was torn too.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="7ab127dc-ecd0-4149-8be8-042ec9c6f02d">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="c1d5b171-8ff9-4b93-8648-07c9733b02f4">
      <Text>Told you hundred twenty.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fd1c58d9-aef4-4c9a-a60f-7b21853a222b">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5461a3f6-0973-4553-9b6c-505b79ca0a50">
      <Text>Boot was torn, Daddy.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="f716dde6-d014-4aa2-bb2d-e711be00a31b">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5b891ff9-568a-44f3-87dd-a3f0e9a0524e">
      <Text>Then that’s fair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6717a0b5-d329-4b3c-8955-a8d05857e1e9">
      <Text>Silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6eaff0d0-6cb5-497e-aa9b-1a9245d76405">
      <Text>Kendra starts to put her palm against her side of the glass. Stops halfway.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="53fce28f-2782-437f-8a2f-57ccdf7f34cc">
      <Text>Hoyt’s hand shifts on the counter but stays there.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b096e051-2757-4af1-8159-d49fc57a08cf">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f4d055cc-bf30-48ed-a9d7-3742ed40c3d6">
      <Text>Trish’s still doing dumplings on Sunday?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="dc4a163b-c495-44ab-8a91-dad04108e219">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="455d7ce3-5f7a-4ba8-b7d2-6ef7fd4b098b">
      <Text>Every Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8049ac42-116a-4448-bf27-d77908679559">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="ad52648c-26bd-480b-a571-f035d115b4ee">
      <Text>You go.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="a1439aeb-3804-4e1d-8785-db61ac23d3b3">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="5ab95f51-6d73-4274-9a72-f06b72d6113f">
      <Text>I come here Sundays.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="b9546591-3834-4ecf-87e2-77bf90260000">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a09cd617-9fac-40c4-b4e9-dce2b46c541f">
      <Text>I know.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="634c7eb7-87c7-42f3-a6e4-624060e711ee">
      <Text>KENDRA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="cf5e550c-2103-4867-b7f1-35603a3c1ecc">
      <Text>Daddy —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="93d76000-8596-4597-b0da-4f38c1bba020">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="e293d9ca-4d9a-4f98-a181-ec46e03edfd9">
      <Text>I need to know where you’ll be.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6715e298-2c75-48d6-acad-c91088461100">
      <Text>Her chin goes. She gets it back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e5889a14-f845-4a52-a017-01db35934602">
      <Text>The OFFICER at the wall checks the clock.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="63083f89-d1f9-4269-8b4f-7cf986be2dc8">
      <Text>OFFICER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="37d5ce80-d93b-4ac3-9084-6ab0cbae2e9e">
      <Text>Time.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="0e7a7b76-6ab9-43e8-8d55-630675cfb787">
      <Text>Hoyt stands. Looks at his daughter through the cloudy glass.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c20747a2-af30-4cb5-9bd6-299f82a6b7f8">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="8bdbf23f-991c-469d-bd0e-cd7f88f6c85e">
      <Text>Next Sunday.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9bb4882a-8441-4cb5-b141-67709a472c6b">
      <Text>He hangs the phone up gently and goes without looking back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="19b642be-57b9-47b8-93ff-4dd824bd86dd">
      <Text>Kendra remains there, holding her phone to her ear long after the line is dead.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="f7db1780-d7e1-4b91-9f9d-9c23b898a8c8">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="125" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="b252cf8c-370a-43a4-b870-7bee29a3415a"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - DEATH WATCH - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f7ca6c19-87bb-4200-9cff-234fd5b43251">
      <Text>A cell nearer the end of the world. Bright. Bare.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cccd6edb-2221-4282-a55c-3819bd8282d7">
      <Text>Hoyt’s few possessions fill an open paper bag: a paperback bound with a rubber band, letters, the chaplain’s folded burial list, a mechanic’s receipt in its envelope, and one handwritten page folded into quarters, its creases worn soft.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c4665250-6553-4a8e-a275-67a914933a33">
      <Text>On top, his METHOD OF EXECUTION form:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="236c130a-fe5d-4844-b2b2-52e28e36e921">
      <Text>NITROGEN HYPOXIA checked. Signed in block letters.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6d774823-0b38-4598-9191-9cc81d6be4f3">
      <Text>Beyond the bars, two OFFICERS work through a clipboard in rehearsed order.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e641d996-3a65-48f5-bd8a-9a2543dd7c3a">
      <Text>The younger one checks an item, then checks it again, never lifting his eyes from the page.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="34fb3d0e-bcb9-40f5-b4f8-28012af621ff">
      <Text>Hoyt watches him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="c2f5e0e5-09b7-4248-bf88-4aead1d48a74">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="62d7129d-11c9-4202-9f43-b1a9a0c19759">
      <Text>You’re doing it right. Don’t worry so much.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fb01af14-bcd3-4aca-b44a-3f025aaa75c8">
      <Text>The young officer finally looks at him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="49f61b63-f27f-4140-bd9f-c7475141e4b7">
      <Text>Hoyt gives him a small nod.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="7b96b96d-996f-40a8-a6ad-a58947703ac9">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="125" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - SECURITY DESK - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8a7d3326-4385-4f77-a9cb-638207194bd6">
      <Text>The same desk. The same SERGEANT who received Rucker before.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8ec448ef-501b-43c3-b80c-3d0c8c6985ec">
      <Text>The gray tray slides out. Rucker places his identification and keys inside, then removes his hat but keeps it in his hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="85e1ce38-59e8-4bde-ac4b-3601bd7023cb">
      <Text>Beyond the metal detector, a secured corridor leads to the witness room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="aa00bfea-8eae-49a7-a4af-77350f7459aa">
      <Text>Rucker looks down it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="b633bde0-72dc-48a5-bf02-9bca065f004f">
      <Text>He lays the hat in the tray and steps through. The detector remains silent.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c9cb769e-bebf-462c-b7f5-19ee49cd05cb">
      <Text>The sergeant collects the tray and presses the release. A steel door BUZZES open.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="61c5ca3f-bf41-4446-b67b-99f894746dab">
      <Text>Rucker walks through bareheaded.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action" id="69518512-1b87-41c6-813c-75887e5a8f25">
      <Text>The door locks behind him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="299a1649-a0df-46d0-8639-401764031bee">
      <SceneProperties Length="1" Page="126" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="786b4cbd-95df-4c32-a86c-e0fc1679a20c"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="WARDEN">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="9c6b5201-0fba-4986-b897-dbf3c219f3ac"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - EXECUTION CHAMBER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="01fb3a4e-0f11-42a4-8135-90295a946f94">
      <Text>Small. Clinical. A gurney beneath white light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3f18ad8b-65a3-4fc1-8944-1b1ed4a756cc">
      <Text>A clear hose runs from the wall to an industrial full-face respirator.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="637c3423-284d-4b6e-97b9-5e9dd09ce18a">
      <Text>Behind the glass, KENDRA stands in the front row, Vance beside her. At the rear, apart from them, Rucker stands bareheaded.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="576ec024-c085-42e0-97d6-15caef9e0a38">
      <Text>The EXECUTION TEAM brings Hoyt in and secures him to the gurney — ankles, wrists, a nylon harness across his chest and shoulders. A pulse oximeter clips to one finger.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a732669b-5f71-4651-9cb7-2147900ff0b7">
      <Text>The respirator comes down over his face. One strap catches. The seal sits wrong.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="24b146cd-45c6-4644-a0e8-29cd279dee2a">
      <Text>As an officer reseats it, Hoyt tilts his head half an inch into the man’s hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="59d730e0-e7ae-4420-8af7-31477490caff">
      <Text>The officer checks again. This time the seal holds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11aaec9c-ead1-41ff-a37e-b2d832736ed9">
      <Text>The WARDEN, 60s, gray and unhurried, unfolds the warrant and reads the authorization and Hoyt’s elected method: nitrogen hypoxia.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="209f24bb-b393-4dd2-97b2-aa1d13523bee">
      <Text>Then he looks down at Hoyt.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="6941f6c5-bbb2-406c-a862-2875a6cc1658">
      <Text>WARDEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="763619c1-b484-46a0-b951-1f7ad2da139f">
      <Text>Mr. Hoyt. Do you have a final statement?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c71df069-4921-44b2-a3ca-776dd2dfb449">
      <Text>Hoyt looks through the glass. His voice comes through the mask and the witness-room speaker.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="fe1557b4-e102-4afa-9137-f43b0c59ce7b">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="415913b0-abad-4ec1-b37e-fce1664d8f0b">
      <Text>I never set a fire in my life. Y’all have the man that lit the others, and a picture of what lit mine, and you’re here anyway. So —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7b85d1cc-710b-4d54-9593-b72eb946095c">
      <Text>Nothing comes after it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c5e0ea5c-3f29-4471-92cd-fdf691e6ff1e">
      <Text>His eyes pass Rucker at the back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="83def803-2830-428e-b7f6-64c9d0833142">
      <Text>Then find Kendra.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="aeacc64d-5699-4dbf-86f1-a2ad39b02093">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a51e8a52-da75-4449-a7ef-f76349e42ea9">
      <Text>Next Sunday, baby.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a654ddf2-4fa8-45da-bf8f-2e557234b722">
      <Text>Kendra holds his eyes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d2a40f40-29b2-4090-955b-eb1fc8b57ecd">
      <Text>The Warden activates the nitrogen system.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="957029f2-05b9-4b03-936b-6492a192156c">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="127" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - STOREROOM - THE TRUE DAY - AFTERNOON</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fade1bfb-d18e-4895-87be-6d64b62c84b9">
      <Text>And now — only now — the film goes back.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a5a9de0e-6420-4f5f-8d2a-ff425dcdebe7">
      <Text>The empty storeroom, striped with afternoon light through the high west window. Dust hangs. On the sill, the jug with two inches of water.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e0a42371-bf65-4466-a89e-cfd0d85057ef">
      <Text>A hard white point burns on the rolled foam below. The compressor cycles on, then off. In the empty room, a pencil-thin thread of gray rises and lays itself along the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ec85956d-bd56-48f3-a934-6e0bbbb86d85">
      <Text>Smoke crawls through the open louvered door into the rear hall, where the kitchen’s exhaust hood pulls the day’s air out through the roof. Nothing else in the building changes.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="a35d1c1b-e134-4a50-861c-2af2e4c61844">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="127" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - THE TRUE NIGHT - NINE O’CLOCK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="431e70a3-b9ed-483f-95aa-7e90cdc70c7d">
      <Text>ALIVE.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1e54b7c0-0c7c-4f3b-af4d-6cba733cbff2">
      <Text>Packed, loud and gold — Christmas lights, bandstand ready, bar three deep.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="cae8e168-a5d0-42ad-853a-5158b697f3f5">
      <Text>PETE works the front door: holds it for two old women, checks a young man’s ID, pushes back the folded twenty. DEENA crosses with three plates and a pitcher, the crowd parting for her.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="13d1f2d8-862f-46c5-bfc7-d573667cde76">
      <Text>At the bar, HOYT in a clean shirt nurses a beer. JUNE tunes on the bandstand in her good boots. LACEY, seventeen and grinning, slips past Pete.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="34ce9e79-0fc1-4f62-940b-46babcd1e762">
      <Text>RAY and ONDINE sit near the dance floor, thirty-one years married. Ray isn’t dancing. Ondine watches the floor and waits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="19aa2d67-d3ce-4d00-97e3-4f00be9f4274">
      <Text>In the kitchen, the last hand hangs up her apron and the hood fan winds down.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e1e64ee6-1d0e-42d7-bf02-d9173a163104">
      <Text>Behind the far wall, unseen, the thread of smoke has become a ribbon spreading across the empty storeroom ceiling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="1b6f2e00-1142-4dc0-b66c-776c777c886a">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="127" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - TEN O’CLOCK</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7ba4ebca-4abc-47ed-afdc-138d4f275d26">
      <Text>The first set ends. The jukebox takes over.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6f966cd6-461c-49b6-9103-b45a4b4d2edb">
      <Text>At the end of the bar, Deena rests with her feet halfway out of her shoes. June brings her water. Their words disappear beneath the music; both laugh.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="71cdd286-c613-490a-b6cd-dd294bd32f4a">
      <Text>On his hourly round, PETE reaches the service door, runs Cobb’s new CHAIN through the panic bar and snaps the padlock. One tug. Hall light off.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2cbad8ae-73ae-4870-bdfb-154b32db5706">
      <Text>He heads back toward the music as smoke begins slipping through the louvered door behind him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d379a6a2-cd0a-4405-b5ed-cd5926682b27">
      <Text>At the payphone, LACEY holds the receiver and a folded slip with a number on it. She catches the faint smell of overheated plastic and looks toward the dark storeroom.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="025808f0-3cba-4aa0-9df8-0b49cdc20e2f">
      <Text>A voice answers. Lacey turns back to the phone.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="7a146254-a7b2-409a-bf96-f536292ea8f6">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="128" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - QUARTER TO ELEVEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="34755dcb-f9e6-4b0d-b405-66611dc89782">
      <Text>JUNE takes the bandstand alone, humming the first bars of something slow. Her boot comes down — one, two — and the BAND HITS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1a41ba71-3d80-4b1d-8bed-fc7af65faf95">
      <Text>The floor fills. ONDINE takes Ray by the wrist and finally pulls him among the dancers. Hoyt smiles into his beer.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="84de7b0f-afe5-4812-bef6-ff7adbc3375b">
      <Text>Above them, the first smoke reaches the barroom — gray through the colored lights, thin enough to be cigarettes, thin enough to be nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c3674760-37b7-42ec-bb30-14f79e321f89">
      <Text>A woman waves it away and keeps dancing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="0e96de17-779c-4ec8-8c1f-e58ea753cc45">
      <SceneProperties Length="3/8" Page="128" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - STOREROOM - SAME TIME</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d18b2064-94cb-4d24-b7da-24825071e845">
      <Text>Smoke hangs to the sill in a room with no light in it. The foam roll is scorched at one point, no more. Deep inside, through a seam, an orange glow breathes, dims and breathes again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="6b48e9ac-7194-4f47-b668-c08eb2bacf47">
      <Text>Shelving, ceiling, louvered door and tie wire remain untouched. Nothing in the room is burning but the inside of the roll.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8a7d13a2-c160-4ca4-914e-fffca85e625c">
      <Text>On the sill above, the jug stands where Hoyt set it, its two inches of water undisturbed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="279d2874-c07b-4ace-8093-7e28a7c1006f">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="128" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BIG PETE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="2e318822-2c8f-49be-9f57-52381014bd56"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="293b485b-3ff8-4be1-9907-34674e9f7de4"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - ELEVEN-FORTY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="344298d5-423d-45fa-b85d-33413947032d">
      <Text>Hoyt sets down his beer and taps the bar twice. Across the room, Deena lifts two fingers from her tray.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="c79f58c6-3bf8-4c42-804d-a8e712c0a573">
      <Text>At the door, CARL VICKERS, 30s, in a feed cap, raises an empty red gas can. Hoyt shoulders through the crowd and takes it, then trades a grip with Pete.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="25f8731e-4cce-42cf-8a0c-c84a9363dc65">
      <Text>Pete’s big hand holds on an extra second.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0bf764cd-68f3-48f2-b4cd-3f915fb55b4d">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="7664235f-070c-4451-9219-4d6ae9330558">
      <Text>Amos.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="90d00786-30f7-4654-b7a8-9a08ab43e175">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="f3512cdb-b3da-43d6-8a2b-52b53db87e92">
      <Text>Pete.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7331f449-1f5b-4c20-b2e2-937defca415d">
      <Text>Hoyt follows Vickers into the night, the can swinging. The door closes behind them on the music.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dca2443a-235d-5043-988d-aa2d8abdc8c7">
      <Text>Down the mill road, beyond the lot, a pickup sits dark on the shoulder, run dry. They walk toward it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="63a00fd1-16cc-4fab-9404-a20efb42cad0">
      <SceneProperties Length="7/8" Page="129" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - STOREROOM - THE TRUE NIGHT - NEAR MIDNIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="62607ae4-51bf-42bc-8025-52a6f5682a69">
      <Text>Hours of smolder have hollowed the roll from within, leaving a shell of char holding its own shape.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5a786243-7df9-4826-ae94-03e99acb0a57">
      <Text>It collapses. A seam opens and draws air. The buried glow deepens, brightens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ad9b71ae-2b42-4241-a44c-2e260167aa7e">
      <Text>The first flame stands inside the split. Small. Then not small.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="011554fe-486f-48f7-b2b7-4f3818ac73db">
      <Text>It takes the exposed foam, the neighboring roll, the shelf stock — faster with everything it reaches. For the first time all night, the room fills with its own light.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bc3ae0e0-6d3b-4f2a-b24b-54ae30a86810">
      <Text>The hot upper layer brightens. Flame rolls through it, ceiling to wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d2cad965-ea75-4200-8d67-100ad914bdfe">
      <Text>TIME DILATES.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5048dba0-9978-498e-ab13-578faacfe2ba">
      <Text>In extreme slow motion, heat reaches across the room. Far from the flame, the wooden doorframe blisters. Shelf stock exhales thin gray threads. The face of a distant foam roll darkens.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ecd3b2e-1ae9-4c5c-a675-79fbff2b12b6">
      <Text>Separate surfaces approaching the same invisible threshold.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="39f6902c-8c46-439a-bae7-c428405ac35c">
      <Text>One suspended second. Then another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5d3f9be7-2797-4ef9-a5f6-d1849f26fc82">
      <Text>REAL TIME.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="593d2a75-aff5-4f21-a859-e82599422d52">
      <Text>Every exposed combustible ignites at once.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="129d5e37-cf9c-4369-94e7-3f03ba9b6874">
      <Text>The room is no longer holding a fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="20203549-ba2d-425e-be8b-2af80d67ceb2">
      <Text>The room is fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="419e7e50-d1b9-4aed-bfd5-25efcd439a95">
      <Text>Through the high west window, the first light the building has shown all night — visible from the road.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="dab4333f-e109-4e3c-aaab-997889304b65">
      <Text>Dense superheated smoke and gases roll through the open louvered doorway, hard down the rear hall and across the barroom ceiling.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="019ac090-9076-41f4-bb07-7ab7c755f5a7">
      <Text>The barroom never reaches flashover.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="1613411d-9030-4239-b3db-7b877ed2031d">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="130" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - MIDNIGHT-FIFTEEN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a0c14966-b844-4939-afca-d7d42c8f135e">
      <Text>The band plays to a packed dance floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ae4afe2b-bc98-4f08-a309-35b71fd9cb56">
      <Text>Smoke drives from the rear hall all at once — a dense gray layer, flat underneath. It spreads above the dancers, then begins to DESCEND.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="47a59fc4-755f-40e3-ba40-70f873cfb8e7">
      <Text>Hoyt comes back up the mill road at a run, both cuffs dark where gasoline splashed, smoke standing over the rear roofline. He reaches the front door as he and Pete look up together.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="533c16b3-26ca-4370-9476-69e5d4749528">
      <Text>On the bandstand, June watches the ceiling disappear. She stops singing mid-line.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="198562a3-db09-46cd-8db6-f38d214847fa">
      <Text>The band plays on without her for two bars, then quits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f4cbd479-8a44-4652-a3a6-983277299aa5">
      <Text>THE SILENCE IS THE ALARM.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="eed59bf3-5496-483e-b3c5-f6736157cd90">
      <Text>A hundred and forty people hear the music stop and look up as one room.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1a648d81-b6a0-4198-976c-070b4d6c60cd">
      <Text>Down the rear hall, the storeroom doorframe is EDGED IN ORANGE. Smoke pours along the ceiling toward them, fast now.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ddc449cb-e48f-4b88-89f7-4960f906ce45">
      <Text>Somebody says fire.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9bc3a852-0c1b-4e67-ae95-1adc2e696737">
      <Text>Somebody SCREAMS it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="36d34866-b224-4895-9a44-31f36490f55e">
      <Text>The lights die.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="784503df-b76f-4cc9-8f76-b7cb0653d2cb">
      <SceneProperties Length="4/8" Page="130" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="BIG PETE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="a2450952-06f9-46cd-bab7-aab5204aafe3"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - DARKNESS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9f3e705b-7f0e-4ce3-b3dd-8d156704e56a">
      <Text>BLACK except for the Christmas strands, the cigarette machine and a hairline of light around the front door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="685c9a47-cceb-4d92-a9d4-080fedf995f9">
      <Text>The entire crowd surges toward it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ac169ed9-781e-4a6a-b887-217b8089b6e8">
      <Text>Pete’s voice rises over everything:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="8f32e6e4-d61f-497e-8277-abe80c1f1159">
      <Text>BIG PETE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="91726aa1-e9da-40fc-8b74-512a727296a6">
      <Text>EASY — one at a time — I got the door! It’s OPEN! Keep coming to my voice —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="04606e19-42f9-4884-9cf3-366ab4c8c0ac">
      <Text>The crowd jams in the doorway. People force through by the dozens, reaching the lot coughing as the smoke descends behind them.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="11ebbd35-7f8c-4e81-bdbb-9d6badc7f9d7">
      <Text>Ondine keeps Ray by the wrist and pulls him through. He reaches the lot still clutching his hat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="66a766e6-afac-40e7-ac16-064f247182bb">
      <Text>Three people break from the clogged entrance and run toward the rear hall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="436eed9a-7ce0-488c-8596-9686113402ce">
      <Text>Hoyt sees them and follows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="c297469f-ab4a-4033-93b5-fa484c0d5c50">
      <SceneProperties Length="1 1/8" Page="131" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="HOYT">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="4ec49836-d0d4-4033-ae85-a79e36473485"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="MOMENTS LATER">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="6eb56332-5294-4195-abc2-d7c8f8defda0"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR HALL - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ba3df729-a49f-447a-9ed3-2011f1f1393f">
      <Text>Hoyt reaches the service door with three shapes crowded behind him. He hits the panic bar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2d722168-b7c2-49de-b4f9-cc8197c3b12f">
      <Text>The door gives an inch and STOPS. Cobb’s chain catches across the bar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="16d69b1a-5f64-41f4-9256-39c763682a1d">
      <Text>Hoyt feels through the black and finds the padlock. Clamps it between both bare hands.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5dc946a8-fdae-47a4-8d37-43df35b224f7">
      <Text>The metal sears him.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="37a60e8d-72d4-4b73-84f1-50e95b34f413">
      <Text>He holds on and wrenches once. Twice.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4f3f451b-9950-4832-991f-164ca8bf9c2f">
      <Text>It does not give.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a3cbfb07-fae0-4525-975f-e1d916a89548">
      <Text>Hoyt releases it, both palms already opening.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="3a69e79d-e698-402d-b7ac-555064b3220c">
      <Text>HOYT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="a1d1eb3f-6e67-4c4d-8fa9-6691cb5fe944">
      <Text>Front. Back the way you came. Hand on the wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7d55b24c-8036-4316-991b-a9aebd81f9a2">
      <Text>He turns the three with his forearms and drives them toward the barroom. At the front crush, he uses his shoulders and elbows to force all three through.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="1347b450-91c6-454a-8921-150b9e519258">
      <Text>Then follows.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4b960cc0-664b-49ba-83f1-d12d2d21101a">
      <Text>MOMENTS LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4b960cc0-664b-49ba-83f1-d12d2d21101a">
      <Text>Black smoke hangs just above the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="a1ececde-7caf-4032-bd55-9363d29a55e6">
      <Text>Pete feels his way toward the service door. Four people follow, each gripping the shoulders ahead. His building keys clench in one fist.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3a7bdd3f-9744-4590-8517-91cfdff5d299">
      <Text>He pushes the panic bar.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3aa4c203-ee21-4124-bda5-fc2790d5276b">
      <Text>The door opens an inch and STOPS.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="46350038-a902-421c-8357-2a0805959b49">
      <Text>Pete’s keys scrape across Cobb’s padlock — one after another. None fits.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="f43cbb7a-a57e-4876-b06b-4d3d4e28b206">
      <Text>They ram the door. It JUMPS in its frame, but the chain holds.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ba5a980-46ae-4d6c-a436-c48a1d12f0a4">
      <Text>Hands and shoulders hammer it. The panic bar rattles. Pete BELLOWS for help.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d083e62e-c35b-4cab-88f7-c6a7a4e02023">
      <Text>The smoke reaches the floor.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8028af71-cb82-4bb7-ab01-509d06a6ad67">
      <Text>One set of fists stops.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8ba41406-8113-420c-9bb9-47d2ef6fa587">
      <Text>Then another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="9e3e4e9c-0903-401b-95db-4c6b3f620642">
      <Text>The last blows weaken and stop.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="98882417-b783-4dd1-85e3-00898cf9dd1d">
      <SceneProperties Length="6/8" Page="132" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats>
          <CharacterArcBeat Name="VOICE">
            <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="0.00" OutlineLevel="0" RightIndent="1.39" SpaceBefore="0" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" id="23445e17-d5eb-46a4-a99e-ac7c414be573"/>
          </CharacterArcBeat>
        </SceneArcBeats>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - BARROOM - THE LAST MINUTES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="50b384c9-3b72-4520-8f68-d1f31ba3c5f4">
      <Text>No flame ever reaches the barroom. The smoke layer hangs at waist height, still descending.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="4d08357e-ee1c-4930-bc7a-36f5242251dc">
      <Text>In the darkness: COUGHING. A chair overturns. The front doorway jams, clears, jams again.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="323064aa-e47c-478b-b49a-9fa3efc86b77">
      <Text>A half-full longneck on the rail. A purse on the back of a chair.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="7b71abc9-964c-49e9-b937-d5419abea9a2">
      <Text>Deena reaches the doorway and draws one breath of night air.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character" id="0d6277a6-d999-47b2-be2b-c702eecec779">
      <Text>VOICE (O.S.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue" id="4e9a3b0e-5c1c-4420-a4d4-e23a21bc7035">
      <Text>Deena —</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="338f7d85-5bbf-46be-a71e-a7df0190ebbf">
      <Text>She turns back into the smoke.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="bf26b460-049b-4910-b9ec-243f175cfaf6">
      <Text>On hands and knees, Deena feels across the floor. Her hand finds a shoe. An ankle.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="8ff6d48a-fba6-4124-81b5-d57ff3ebd88e">
      <Text>She grips the trouser cuff and drags the person toward where the doorway should be.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="fa876132-9526-45ae-86db-0a5a3fbc77b1">
      <Text>Her free hand strikes a wall.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d7039ffb-efe8-41ef-9575-89efa2459f81">
      <Text>No door.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="d64d8a18-de03-419d-be27-ec42bf5611d7">
      <Text>Deena keeps her grip on the trouser cuff.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="85fb9259-6d02-4bb1-8338-d796e20cc57e">
      <Text>The Christmas lights disappear behind the descending smoke.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition" id="c8c13390-7a46-46f2-9d1d-2f74974fefd7">
      <Text>SMASH TO BLACK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2971b59f-8056-4bc0-8a6f-6eb0477c8249">
      <Text>Silence.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="dc96f998-5d45-4094-816a-66c3a978867c">
      <SceneProperties Length="2/8" Page="133" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. HOLMAN - EXECUTION CHAMBER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="2ea433c7-fefe-43bd-831d-a6c2ed7e932c">
      <Text>Out of the black: the ceiling lights of the chamber.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="29f24775-4e31-4593-a5a4-0bb63a16c8a2">
      <Text>It is over. A stethoscope, a time called out, a curtain drawn by hand along its rail.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="16c2fee3-f61f-406b-aa28-0eb10c937a1c">
      <Text>In the witness room, Kendra is still standing. She stays standing until the curtain is all the way closed. Vance’s hand is under her arm and Kendra has not noticed.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" id="e0e07294-99a7-4a2d-98ae-6b28b80de270">
      <SceneProperties Length="5/8" Page="133" Title="">
        <SceneArcBeats/>
      </SceneProperties>
      <Text>INT. TRISH’S DINER - SUNDAY - DAY</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="e030289e-4f96-4449-a1ff-a89a0aafd66e">
      <Text>After church. Full. Kendra alone in a booth with chicken and dumplings and sweet tea.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3308a647-8e77-4a16-a999-92cc8e510668">
      <Text>Above the register, among the church flyers and the local notices, a newspaper front page: Hoyt’s face, and a headline about a corrected record. Nobody in the room is looking at it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="17469435-f0dc-5d23-a486-9d58445d82b3">
      <Text>ONDINE BEASLEY, eighties now, in her church clothes, comes down the aisle with her plate. She stops at the booth. Kendra looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="5ae533c2-70a0-59ce-bab7-2ace67c2c19c">
      <Text>Ondine sits down across from her. Says nothing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ae9ed31b-2ff3-5748-8e45-c980b753baf2">
      <Text>Kendra looks at her a moment longer. Then goes back to her dinner. Ondine takes up her fork.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="224d7b8c-e48c-4b35-80b9-862154cb67a0">
      <Text>Kendra eats her Sunday dinner.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="3ff2f0ef-bcb0-44a6-9010-f4c98c2b7b7d">
      <Text>HOLD.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Alignment="Left" FirstIndent="0.00" Leading="Regular" LeftIndent="1.50" RightIndent="7.50" SpaceBefore="12" Spacing="1" StartsNewPage="No" Type="Action" id="ae5db1e7-894e-497e-88db-0abbb1691d3e">
      <Text>CUT TO BLACK.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
